WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.160
The first thing that tipped the Foundation
off to SCP-087’s presence were the reports

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.920
of numerous unexplained disappearances on
campus.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.240
There were plenty of rumors about what might
be behind them, but Field Agents suspected

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.680
that the true source of the vanishing would
be something beyond civilian imagination.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.140
All anyone knew for sure was that everyone
who had gone missing was last seen in a certain

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.760
administrative building on the university
grounds, and that the disappearances only

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.860
seemed to happen when the elevator was out.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.020
The campus was soon flooded with Foundation&nbsp;

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.600
agents, creating a barrier&nbsp;
around the administrative

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.860
building, and the presumed habitat of SCP
- 087.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.300
Nobody else could get in, and hopefully, whatever
was inside couldn’t get out.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.920
One of the Foundation’s lead scientists
was flown in to consult on the investigation.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.860
What could have been behind all those students
disappearing?

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.760
The doctor’s preliminary interviews with
university staff who worked in the building

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.460
yielded some interesting details: Strange
noises, like banging and even a faint, shrill

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.740
crying, would be heard from a door that lead
to a no longer used stairway in Hallway 3B.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.360
Staff in the building had no reason to ever
take these stairs, especially considering

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.800
how many of them reported a strange sense
of unease when just standing outside the door.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.200
The only reason someone might take those stairs
is due to…Elevator malfunctions.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.320
In that instant, the doctor had put it all
together.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.880
The staff they interviewed had their memory
wiped with Amnetics – special chemicals

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.000
used by the Foundation with the power to delete
human memories.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.680
The Foundation only used them for staff or
civilians who had confirmed contact with an

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.920
SCP, and the doctor knew that they had a live
one on their hands.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.420
The staircase.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.240
There was something terribly wrong with that
staircase, and it was the SCP Foundation’s

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.080
job to find out what – before it made anybody
else disappear.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:56.040
This is the story of SCP – 087, otherwise
known as The Endless Staircase, and the three

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.920
doomed journeys down into its murky depths.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.440
The doctor was more than eager to begin research
into the staircase, and its frightening, anomalous

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:04.920
properties.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.540
After all, you don’t claw your way up to
being one of the Foundation’s key researchers

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.560
without being brave, and perhaps just a little
bit deranged.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.720
As was standard, once a perimeter was secured
around the staircase, the good doctor requested

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.120
a selection of D-Class personnel for testing.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.860
For those not in the know, D-Class is the
Foundation’s polite way of saying “cannon

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.700
fodder.”

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.340
The doctor was sent three D-Class prisoners
for use in his investigation of SCP – 087.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:39.000
The first, D-8432, was – according to official
documentation on the incident – a “43-year

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.560
old male of average build and appearance and
unremarkable psychological background.”

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.480
This man once worked for the Foundation in
a more official capacity, but he was given

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.660
the often-deadly demotion to D-Class due to
a dangerous mistake handling SCP – 682 that

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.700
lead to the deaths of several other agents.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.340
Now, it looked like it would be his turn.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.560
The doctor explained his mission to him: Explore
the staircase, gather data, help us find out

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.240
exactly what we’re dealing with here.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.960
If you come back alive, there may even be
a promotion in it for you.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:15.780
And with that promise, D-8432 was given his
load-out: a 75-watt flood lamp with battery

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.000
power capable of lasting 24 hours, an audio
headset, and a handheld camcorder fitted with

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.080
a transmission stream.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.900
D-8432 was then pushed through the door in
Hallway 3B, and out onto the staircase.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.960
According to declassified Foundation files
describing the staircase, “SCP-087 is an

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.460
unlit platform staircase.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:41.280
Stairs descend on a 38-degree angle for 13
steps before reaching a semi-circular platform

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.620
of approximately 3 meters in diameter.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.700
Descent direction rotates 180 degrees at each
platform.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:54.420
The design of SCP-087 limits subjects to a
visual range of approximately 1.5 flights.”

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.920
But in D-8432’s mind, “unlit” really
didn’t seem like the right word.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.220
He would have chosen “all-consuming darkness.”

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:08.640
Despite carrying a powerful 75-watt lamp,
D-8432 was only capable of partially lighting

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.260
the platform he was standing on – and the
illumination only stretched down nine of the

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.060
thirteen steps to the next platform.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.820
When D-8432 observed how little help his lamp
was giving him, he was instructed to shine

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.100
it out of the doorway into Hallway 3B.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:29.280
When he did so, the light seemed to shine
far further than it ever could in SCP – 087.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:35.220
Already, the beginning of anomalous activity
was obvious: Everywhere else, darkness is

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.300
just the absence of light.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.020
In SCP – 087, darkness eats light.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.760
It was like a tangible, black mass that only
a certain amount of light could survive, while

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.200
the rest just wouldn’t show.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.620
D-8432 swallowed hard over a lump in his throat.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.880
The door to Hallway 3B was closed behind him,
and he was ordered to descend.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.500
Surviving to see that promotion was feeling
unlikely, but it’s not like he had a choice.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:04.860
If he tried to escape SCP – 087 before he
was permitted, he’d be shot by SCP Foundation

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.240
Field Agents on the spot.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.560
So he followed the high-ranking doctor’s
orders and began to descend the steps to the

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.160
next platform.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:16.800
Nothing about the physical makeup of the staircase
itself seemed abnormal – the base and walls

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.040
were a very plain, dull concrete, with a metal
handrail.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:25.080
The only thing that seemed unique about it
so far was the strange light-bending properties.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:31.740
That was, until he reached the second platform
down and he heard it, a soft, echoing cry.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.000
A child’s cry.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.620
It was shrieks of panic, or maybe even pain,
echoing up from below.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.700
He was asked why he had stopped, and he explained
the crying sound he’d been hearing.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.500
It sounded like it was coming from far down
the stairs, maybe 200 meters below him.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.360
He could just make out the words “please”,
help”, and “down here” coming from the

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:51.720
darkness.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:56.340
But the team outside the stairwell couldn’t
hear anything, so they asked him to descend

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:56.700
further.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:01.860
Another platform down, and they could hear
it too, the unmistakable cries of a terrified

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:02.580
child.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.340
“Please”, “help”, and “down here.”

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.640
D-8432 was ordered to keep going and only&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.160
stop if he noticed changes&nbsp;
to the visual environment

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.020
or in the sounds he was hearing.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:18.660
D-8432, knowing his life was on the line,
had to keep going, and descended another twenty

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.680
flights of stairs before stopping to remark
that the sounds of the child hadn’t gotten

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:23.280
any closer.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.820
They still sounded just as far away as when
he’d first heard them.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.120
He was told his observations were noted, and
pressured to continue.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:37.020
Within half an hour, D-8432 had descended
a full fifty floors, with no sign of a bottom

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:37.380
in sight.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:42.360
Somehow the volume of the child’s crying
had remained consistent throughout, as if

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.380
it was moving away from D-8432 at the same
rate he was descending.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.400
At this point, D-8432 reported that he was
feeling uneasy.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.820
The doctor said that this was understandable,
given the circumstances.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:58.440
He’d been watching what little there was
to see over a live video feed the entire time,

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:03.720
and something about the truly bottomless nature
of the staircase, and the ever-elusive crying,

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.340
was undeniably eerie.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.880
But things were about to really take a turn
for the worst.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.560
As D-8432 stepped forward towards the next
set of stairs, he froze.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:17.820
There was something on the platform below
him, barely illuminated by the light of his

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.840
75-watt bulb.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:19.800
It was a face.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:25.800
Vaguely human in size and shape, but with
a few terrifying differences: it had greyish

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.100
skin, and no mouth, nostrils, or pupils.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:34.800
And yet, D-8432 could feel that this thing
was making eye contact with him.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.220
He couldn’t move, trapped in this thing’s
piercing gaze.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:43.620
In an instant, the face jerked forwards, suddenly
only about a foot away from D-8432’s face

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.480
– eyes staring into his own.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:51.240
D-8432 screamed and ran, scaling all fifty
flights in an astonishing eighteen minutes,

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.820
before charging out into Hallway 3B.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:58.320
There, he collapsed from the exhaustion and
the fear of what he’d just seen.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:03.780
Upon reviewing the footage, the strange face
was designated “SCP-087-1.”

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.280
Fascinating.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.620
It was time for a second experiment.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.080
The doctor just had to know more.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:16.680
The second test subject was D-9035, a 28-year-old
male with a history of aggravated assaults

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.160
against women.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:22.440
He was given the same loadout as his predecessor,
except this time with an even more powerful

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.820
100-watt bulb.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:26.880
He was also given 100 small LED lights that&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.700
had adhesive backs and a&nbsp;
battery life of approximately

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.920
3 weeks, with which they intended to permanently
illuminate SCP – 087.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.480
However, despite the extra wattage of his
bulb, he still couldn’t illuminate beyond

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.140
the ninth step.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.320
SCP – 087 wouldn’t allow it.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:47.460
Having no idea of the horrors that lurked
below him, he descended on the doctor’s

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.720
orders, and began fixing the LEDs to walls
of each platform he passed.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:56.520
The LED always illuminated the landing, but
the light couldn’t pass the first step on

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.060
either side.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.380
The flights of stairs themselves would remain
in perpetual darkness.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:08.940
After the second flight, D-9035 noticed the
same crying D-8432 had heard and became uneasy.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:14.700
Just like before, as D-9035 descended, the
volume of the crying didn’t seem to increase,

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:20.400
as if for every step he descended, the source
of the crying descended one, too, keeping

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.800
them at a constant 200 metres apart.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:28.920
Still, he was ordered to continue his descent
and the placing of LED’s even as his paranoia

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.340
grew.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:34.740
When he reached the 51s floor, he observed
damage to the wall and steps – sections

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.920
appeared to have been smashed to rubble by
an extreme force.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:44.040
As he descended past the broken step, he only
felt his fear, anxiety, and paranoia grow.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:49.500
The doctor made a note of the fact that SCP
– 087 seemed to cause instances of anxiety

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:54.540
and terror in its occupants, even before they
encountered SCP – 087 – 1.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:10:02.760
As D-9035 reached platform 89 – a full 350
meters under the initial platform – he stopped

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:07.500
dead in his tracks, and saw something staring
up at him from the platform below.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:12.600
That same terrible, grey face, with those
dead, white eyes.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:17.880
He was encouraged to stay calm and try to
get better footage of the face, but it charged

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.880
for him and D-9035 ran for his life.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.380
He ascended the staircase at a staggering
pace, even passing out from exhaustion and

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.960
remaining motionless for 14 minutes half way.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:34.140
When D-9035 finally gathered the strength
to get up, he scrambled back to Hallway 3B

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.420
and fell into a state of catatonia.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:42.060
He remains unresponsive to all external stimuli
to this day, just staring off into the distance

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.620
with a haunted expression.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.320
Almost like he’s still there in the hallway.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.840
The doctor wanted to conduct one more test
before he ordered SCP – 087 shut off from

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.260
the world forever, and it was the most terrifying
of all.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:01.140
The final subject was D-9884, a 23-year-old
woman with a history of depression and the

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.520
use of excessive force.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.460
The doctor had hoped that D-9884 would travel&nbsp;

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.520
the deepest yet, and so,&nbsp;
he gave her the additional

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:14.940
supplies of a backpack containing 3.75 litres
of water, 15 nutrient bars, and 1 thermal

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:15.300
blanket.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:19.440
As far as the Foundation was concerned, she
was in this for the long haul.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.860
But none of them had any idea quite how right
they were.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:30.240
When D-9884 entered SCP – 087, all the lights
from the previous expedition had disappeared.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:33.060
Still, she was ordered to go deeper.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:37.860
She heard the crying of the mysterious child
– if it was even a child at all – and

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.540
again she was ordered to go deeper.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:46.560
At the 496th landing, even as D-9884 seemed
to slip into a state of mortal terror, once

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.960
again she was ordered to go even deeper.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:54.300
Every moment, he was hoping to get a better
look at the face of SCP – 087 – 1.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:12:00.240
And when D-9884 finally broke, and fled back
upstairs, he did.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:06.420
The face appeared but this time it was mere
inches behind her, staring directly into the

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.740
camera with its blank eyes – startling even
this veteran of the supernatural.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:15.720
The face appearing caused D-9884 to panic
and flee, but instead of going back up the

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:20.100
stairs to safety, she went deeper down the
staircase in an attempt to escape it.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:24.840
Deeper, and deeper, and deeper, until her
video feed cut out.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:28.200
D-9884 was never seen again.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:33.120
In the aftermath of the tests, the SCP was
classified as Euclid – it may have been

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.180
dangerous, but at least it was easy to contain.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.640
The door to Hallway 3B was replaced with one&nbsp;

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.100
made out of reinforced steel,&nbsp;
with an electro-release

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.000
lock mechanism.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.320
It has been disguised to resemble a janitorial
closet consistent with the rest of the building.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.700
The lock won’t release unless a classified
number of electrical volts are applied, while

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.260
the key is turned counter clockwise.

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:56.220
And after a few inches of foam insulation
were applied to the inner side of the door,

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:59.640
staff at the building never again reported
hearing strange noises.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:04.350
As for the fates of those lost within the
endless turning flights and platforms of SCP

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.080
– 087, we may never know.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.740
But one can only assume it isn’t pleasant.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:20.580
Here we go again. It’s time to return to the&nbsp;
acid-filled containment chamber of SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:27.120
more commonly known as the Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile. We’ve spoken about him and the ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:33.720
The SCP Foundation has attempted to destroy him&nbsp;
in a previous video. But as we said back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:38.580
we really only scratched the surface&nbsp;
of the huge number of insane ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.620
the Foundation has tried to wipe this&nbsp;
ornery lizard off the face of the earth.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:48.840
Today, we’re filling in some of the cracks.&nbsp;
Let’s take a look at the secret test logs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:58.380
detailing the Foundation’s unsuccessful&nbsp;
quest to finally destroy SCP-682. If you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:04.860
a real SCP Expert, you’re likely to recognize&nbsp;
some familiar faces we meet along the way...

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:10.620
Esteemed Foundation Researcher Dr. Alto&nbsp;
Clef - famed for his somewhat unconventional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:16.440
personality - entered the test chamber to see&nbsp;
if he could intimidate the beast to death. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:22.740
resulted in a long staring contest between&nbsp;
Dr. Clef and 682, towards the end of which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:28.200
Dr. Clef began to lose his nerve. He&nbsp;
tried to leave the room, only to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:34.020
that the door was locked, causing him to swear&nbsp;
loudly. Dr. Clef, who always tries to find the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:40.020
most direct solution to his problems, blew up&nbsp;
the door with plastic explosives and ran off.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:46.200
Test failed.
Next came SCP-662, a silver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:52.620
hand bell that summons the supernaturally helpful&nbsp;
butler, Mr. Deeds. When Mr. Deeds was summoned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:59.280
Foundation researchers asked him if he could kill&nbsp;
SCP-682. Deeds politely explained that he wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:06.840
be capable of killing 682, it’s just too strong.&nbsp;
When asked if he could at least incapacitate 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:12.120
he replied that the best way to do this&nbsp;
would be to poison himself and allow 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:18.300
to eat his body. But this, he reminded, would&nbsp;
only be a temporary problem for the lizard.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:23.220
Test failed.
The Foundation brought in SCP-689,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:28.980
a terrifying soapstone statue of a sitting&nbsp;
skeleton that can kill you if you see it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:34.860
then stop paying attention to it. 682 first&nbsp;
observed the statue, and then the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:41.040
turned off the lights. When they turned them&nbsp;
back on, SCP-682 appeared to be dead in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:47.040
puddle of gray and black liquid. D-Classes were&nbsp;
sent in to confirm that 682 was actually dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:53.580
but it instead got up and killed them. Researchers&nbsp;
theorized that 682’s definition of “life” is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:59.280
not quite the same as ours, rendering&nbsp;
689’s death-related powers ineffective.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:00.540
Test failed.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:07.620
SCP-807 was next up to bat. This is&nbsp;
an anomalous salmon-colored ceramic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:12.660
dinner plate with the words "Last Chance&nbsp;
Diner" printed on the edges in white. Any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.820
food placed on it becomes irresistible by any&nbsp;
definition, but when the food is consumed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.560
causes immediate cardiac arrest due to the&nbsp;
sudden clogging of the arteries with fat.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:28.620
Researchers made a meal known as the&nbsp;
“682 Special” - 10 kg of rotten meat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:34.680
and sharpened bone splinters, 10 L of&nbsp;
rancid mayonnaise, 1 L potassium cyanide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:39.780
and 1 kg morphine hydrochloride,&nbsp;
combined into a solid mass and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:46.740
transmuted by 807. When 682 first consumed&nbsp;
this disgusting meal, it seemed to collapse.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:52.560
However, when D-Classes were sent in to see&nbsp;
whether 682 was truly out for the count,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:58.020
multiple holes opened in its body. These&nbsp;
holes fired out high-pressure jets of blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:04.860
killing the nearby D-Classes and destroying&nbsp;
the containment cell. 682 was fine afterwards.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:08.220
Test failed.
To kill 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:13.200
it seemed that the Foundation really needed&nbsp;
to have God on their side. So they tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:20.520
recruit SCP-343, also known as “God”, to&nbsp;
help them destroy the beast. However, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:25.440
he entered the containment chamber, he somehow&nbsp;
couldn’t even see the beast. When researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:31.200
asked him whether he could kill 682, God replied,&nbsp;
“He's not one of mine. Deal with him yourself."

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.580
Test failed.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:41.460
Next, the Foundation recruited SCP-524: A small&nbsp;
white rabbit that can eat literally anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:47.880
including itself, without being harmed. The&nbsp;
rabbit was released into SCP-682’s chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:54.240
at which point it approached 682 and began to&nbsp;
eat one of its legs. 682 roared in pain and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.240 --> 00:18:00.360
scuttled up the wall, out of 524’s reach, where&nbsp;
it remained for a number of hours. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:06.120
SCP-524 seemed to become bored, and began eating&nbsp;
its way out of containment through a nearby wall.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.560
Test failed.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.580
Maybe the luck of the Irish was what&nbsp;
the Foundation needed to finally put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:18.600
this monster to rest. They recruited SCP-1933,&nbsp;
a fat man dressed as Santa Claus whose bodily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:24.960
fluids are entirely the alcoholic beverage known&nbsp;
as Irish Cream. However, if enough of this Irish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:31.080
cream is fed to something, all of their bodily&nbsp;
fluids will become Irish cream, killing them.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:39.480
The Foundation fed large quantities of this&nbsp;
Irish cream to SCP-682. At first, it appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:47.760
intoxicated, a promising sign. However, it vomited&nbsp;
out a massive quantity of SCP-1933 bodily fluids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:52.860
turning the walls of its cell into Irish cream&nbsp;
and allowing it to escape and wreak havoc.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.360
Test failed.&nbsp;

00:18:55.320 --> 00:19:02.400
The Foundation recruited the help of SCP-2337,&nbsp;
an intelligent corn crake known as Dr. Spanko,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:07.380
with a voice so loud it can quite literally&nbsp;
talk its victims to death if it speaks to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:14.040
for an extended period of time. It was sent&nbsp;
into SCP-682’s chamber to destroy the beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:19.500
but 682 just told it to leave, and the&nbsp;
talkative bird obliged - by blowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:25.800
away one of the chamber walls with a yell,&nbsp;
allowing SCP-682 to breach containment again.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.533
Test failed.

00:19:29.533 --> 00:19:32.040
As you can probably sympathize with right now,&nbsp;
the Foundation researchers were starting to get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:38.760
little frustrated with their lack of progress.&nbsp;
They even pitched the possibility of sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:45.780
SCP-682 into an alternate dimension, perhaps&nbsp;
into a stalemate against its alternate self.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:52.620
But this pitch was shot down by the O5 Council on&nbsp;
the grounds that it was way, way, way too risky.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:58.020
Back to the drawing board. By which we&nbsp;
mean, they literally transformed SCP-682’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:04.080
skin into a kind of drawing board.
SCP-2521 is an anomaly that manifests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:09.120
any time information about it is recorded, and&nbsp;
immediately grabs the source of the information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:14.040
wrapping it in its tendrils and taking&nbsp;
it away with it. The Foundation sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:21.060
to take advantage of this by using a laser to&nbsp;
cut this anomalous information into SCP-682’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:24.840
side. However, this didn’t have the&nbsp;
results that they were hoping for.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:30.240
SCP-2521 did turn up to take the&nbsp;
information, but it only took the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:36.540
skin on which the information was carved.&nbsp;
682 survived and quickly grew back its skin.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:42.420
Test failed.
Researchers suggested tracking down SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:49.200
an obscenely massive underwater creature known&nbsp;
as The Leviathan, and feeding 682 to the beast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:55.920
However, this idea was immediately shot down&nbsp;
by the O5 Council. If 682 did what it did best:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.700 --> 00:21:03.540
Surviving the attack and acting accordingly,&nbsp;
perhaps by growing to the size of SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:10.200
it would likely trigger an XK-Class End of the&nbsp;
World Scenario. It simply was not worth the risk.&nbsp;

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:19.800
The Foundation released two specimens of SCP-939&nbsp;
into 682’s test chamber. These voice-imitating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:24.060
amnesia-inducing monsters have&nbsp;
caused huge damage to human targets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:30.360
so maybe they had some hope against 682.&nbsp;
This hope turned out to be misplaced:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:38.280
Both specimens seemed extremely distressed by&nbsp;
682’s presence and refused to engage. 682 did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:44.580
have that same refusal. It charged in and brutally&nbsp;
killed both, before devouring their corpses.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:49.320
Test failed.
In a very well-documented case, the adorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:56.340
SCP-999 was introduced into 682’s test chamber.&nbsp;
The unassailable good vibes provided by 999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:56.340 --> 00:22:03.480
as well as an intense tickle fight, did actually&nbsp;
lead to the temporary incapacitation of SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:10.320
However, the otherwise wholesome incident ended in&nbsp;
tragedy when 682 adapted to the good vibes and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:15.420
able to release a kind of violent laughter&nbsp;
wave. This incapacitated much of the staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:21.900
and allowed 682 to breach containment and go on&nbsp;
another killing spree, before being recontained.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.473
Test, once again, failed.

00:22:24.473 --> 00:22:27.420
One of the closest attempts the&nbsp;
Foundation ever had involved SCP-294,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:32.040
an anomalous coffee machine that can&nbsp;
produce any liquid typed into its keypad.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:39.060
Foundation researchers requested “SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer” from the machine, and were astounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:48.720
at the results. During tests on SCP-682 tissue&nbsp;
samples, the liquid was capable of causing 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:54.660
tissue to decay and crumble. Tests on the living&nbsp;
creature were similarly promising. The acid in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.660 --> 00:23:03.000
682’s tank was receded, and one liter of SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer was poured onto it, causing that portion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:10.740
of its flesh to immediately decay. When the acid&nbsp;
was returned, this portion dissolved instantly.

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:22.080
Scientists believe that if they could one day&nbsp;
get a large enough quantity of this liquid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:27.600
they might have a viable option.&nbsp;
But until then, the tests march on.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:33.180
They introduced SCP-055, the self-keeping&nbsp;
secret, into the containment chamber of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:42.228
SCP-682. We don’t really know what happened,&nbsp;
but seeing as 682 isn’t dead, we now know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:42.228 --> 00:23:52.980
055 can’t kill it. That and the fact it isn’t&nbsp;
round is pretty much all we know about SCP-055.

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:57.660
Test failed.

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:09.060
Next came SCP-082, also known as Fernand the&nbsp;
Cannibal. Fernand was first presented a piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:13.920
of flesh from 682, but rather than eating&nbsp;
it, he inspected it and began to express&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:18.960
joy that his “friend” still lived. When&nbsp;
introduced into 682’s testing chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:24.600
Fernand attempted to subdue the lizard&nbsp;
and use it as his steed. 682 expressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:29.820
an intense hatred of both Fernand and the&nbsp;
idea of being Fernand’s steed, so the two of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:29.820 --> 00:24:35.640
them engaged in combat. Mobile Task Forces were&nbsp;
eventually brought in to subdue both subjects.

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:38.820
In the debrief interview, both hinted&nbsp;
that the two of them shared history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:38.820 --> 00:24:43.440
prior to containment. 682 was&nbsp;
reluctant to talk about it.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:46.680
Test failed.

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:53.160
Researchers were becoming extremely frustrated&nbsp;
with SCP-682’s unwillingness to die, so they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:53.160 --> 00:24:58.800
called in an SCP who responded&nbsp;
to reason much better: SCP-049,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:04.560
the Plague Doctor. This sinister surgeon can&nbsp;
kill with a touch, and the Foundation hoped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:04.560 --> 00:25:11.880
that would extend to 682. However, the result&nbsp;
was a dud. The Plague Doctor did touch 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:17.340
but it experienced no adverse effects, and&nbsp;
even swiped at the doctor. Upon leaving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.340 --> 00:25:24.420
049 reported feeling “emotionally&nbsp;
disturbed” by his encounter with SCP-682.

00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:27.900
Yep, you guessed it: Test failed.

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:32.220
If it gives you any indication of just how&nbsp;
desperate the researchers were at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:37.800
Dr. Richard Graham pondered whether introducing&nbsp;
SCP-682 to a human with just as pessimistic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:43.500
misanthropic feelings as itself would somehow&nbsp;
pacify it. They sent in a particularly nasty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:48.900
D-Class, and the two spoke. Fascinatingly,&nbsp;
682 didn’t attempt to harm this D-Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:48.900 --> 00:25:52.860
they just shared their profane and bleak&nbsp;
sentiments about the human race with one another.

00:25:52.860 --> 00:25:58.920
However, some of 682’s opinions were a&nbsp;
little too spicy for this D-Class. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:58.920 --> 00:26:03.600
listening to the reptile speak for twenty&nbsp;
minutes, the D-Class fell into a catatonic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:07.380
state from the sheer depression&nbsp;
of it all. He died not long after.

00:26:07.380 --> 00:26:11.280
One anonymous researcher suggested&nbsp;
perhaps the worst idea of all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:18.240
Letting SCP-682 out into the wild. Not even to&nbsp;
really terminate it, just to see what it does.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:22.620
The anonymous scientist figured there would be&nbsp;
some merit in analyzing the creature’s behavior.

00:26:31.980 --> 00:26:36.660
As you can probably guess, this&nbsp;
request was shot down by the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:40.740
Council. The note attached to the request&nbsp;
by one of its members summed it up best:

00:26:40.740 --> 00:26:45.360
“I'll tell you what it'll do. It'll go out for&nbsp;
a nice stroll, murder a few innocent people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:50.880
go fishing, slaughter a few more innocent people,&nbsp;
start up a tech-company, eat a few more innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:56.520
people, go on a vacation to Florida, dismember a&nbsp;
few more innocent people! I swear, when I find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:56.520 --> 00:27:01.680
who wrote this, you can personally enter 682's&nbsp;
containment chamber to analyze him yourself!”

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:08.040
Over fifty men and women, clad in red robes,
kneel before an unholy altar.

00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:14.640
They chant and mutter indecipherable words
- words of cruelty and madness… of obsession

00:27:14.640 --> 00:27:16.080
and sacrilege.

00:27:16.080 --> 00:27:18.660
Not long ago, these were regular people.

00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:25.260
Computer technicians, teachers, plumbers,
construction workers, accountants.

00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:30.060
This was before they fell under the ungodly
influence of a new ruler.

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:35.520
The center of this makeshift place of worship
was once a normal school gymnasium, but it’s

00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:37.800
now the home of a huge statue.

00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:41.160
A humanoid being, wreathed in tentacles.

00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:47.580
Its head is more like a squid or cuttlefish
than anything resembling an actual human face.

00:27:48.120 --> 00:27:52.560
While he’s known to the cultists as the
Tentacled God, the beast they worship is known

00:27:52.560 --> 00:27:59.220
to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 2662, and he
sits in the belly of one of their expansive

00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:02.220
containment facilities, locked away from the
world.

00:28:02.220 --> 00:28:07.440
But not for long, if his devoted followers
have anything to say about it.

00:28:07.440 --> 00:28:11.460
This is their god, all-powerful and unchanging,&nbsp;

00:28:11.460 --> 00:28:14.100
and when it comes to springing&nbsp;
him from containment,

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:18.780
no tactic is too vile or underhanded to get
the job done.

00:28:18.780 --> 00:28:23.880
Their mortal leader and high-priest, a man
in a purple robe calling himself Brother Marsh,

00:28:23.880 --> 00:28:26.580
walks among their crouched forms.

00:28:26.580 --> 00:28:32.340
He whispers instructions for the great day
of liberation that’s soon to come, providing

00:28:32.340 --> 00:28:34.080
everyone plays their part.

00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:39.540
It’s a plan months in the making - and one
that, if it goes off without a hitch, could

00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:41.940
free their monstrous god into the world.

00:28:41.940 --> 00:28:48.300
They would strike at the very heart of their
enemy, The SCP Foundation, when they least

00:28:48.300 --> 00:28:51.960
expect it, and nothing shall stand in their
way.

00:28:51.960 --> 00:28:54.960
How could they lose when they have a god on
their side?

00:28:54.960 --> 00:29:00.000
But why did all these normal people become
violent zealots for squid-faced deity?

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.040
It all began with a dream.

00:29:02.040 --> 00:29:07.920
To those who experienced these dreams, they
felt more like prophecies, premonitions of

00:29:07.920 --> 00:29:09.540
the glorious horrors to come.

00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:14.340
A red sky, billions dead and billions more
enslaved.

00:29:14.340 --> 00:29:20.700
A dark silhouette on the horizon - Their Tentacled
God, holding dominion over all.

00:29:20.700 --> 00:29:23.640
At first, it just seemed like a strange nightmare.

00:29:23.640 --> 00:29:29.220
The ones who experienced it woke up shaken
and afraid, hoping to shake the images from

00:29:29.220 --> 00:29:29.640
their mind.

00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:30.840
But they couldn’t.

00:29:30.840 --> 00:29:33.420
Every night, the nightmare would return.

00:29:33.420 --> 00:29:39.660
They’d see the images - the red sky, the
dead and enslaved, the Tentacled God.

00:29:39.660 --> 00:29:45.240
And after a while it would come to them even
when they weren’t asleep, eventually happening

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:46.920
whenever they closed their eyes.

00:29:46.920 --> 00:29:53.580
Little by little, this scene stopped looking
so hideous… and started to look glorious.

00:29:53.580 --> 00:29:59.220
They felt his presence in their minds, slowly
pushing them towards their inevitable future.

00:29:59.220 --> 00:30:04.740
They started to realize that they wanted him
to rule over the universe, and to experience

00:30:04.740 --> 00:30:06.180
the honor of serving him.

00:30:06.180 --> 00:30:11.820
Many of them abandoned their homes and families
- leaving their friends and loved ones left

00:30:11.820 --> 00:30:14.520
to worry that they’d gone insane.

00:30:14.520 --> 00:30:17.460
In their eyes, they were safer than they’d
ever been.

00:30:17.460 --> 00:30:20.100
They finally had purpose.

00:30:20.100 --> 00:30:24.360
They were working in service of something
far greater than themselves.

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:28.140
The influence of the tentacled god drew them
closer to one another.

00:30:28.800 --> 00:30:34.020
They would meet in secret, exchanging information
from the prophecies their ruler sent them

00:30:34.020 --> 00:30:34.920
in their dreams.

00:30:34.920 --> 00:30:39.000
They worshipped together, building altars
and idols to congregate around.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:43.920
They performed dark blood rituals, involving
human and animal sacrifice.

00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:49.260
It was when Brother Marsh, The Anointed One,
arrived to guide them towards their true mission

00:30:49.260 --> 00:30:51.900
that things kicked into high gear.

00:30:51.900 --> 00:30:57.300
Just three months prior, Brother Marsh had
been an office drone working in data entry

00:30:57.300 --> 00:31:02.520
for a large insurance company, before the
Tentacled God invaded his thoughts with a

00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:09.240
simple message: “FREE ME, AND THE NEW WORLD
I CREATE SHALL BE YOUR PLAYGROUND.”

00:31:09.240 --> 00:31:15.480
Since then, he’d devoted himself completely
to the cause, quitting his job and maxing

00:31:15.480 --> 00:31:21.240
out his credit cards to help fund his new
life’s purpose - infiltrating the SCP Foundation,

00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:24.960
and releasing his inhuman&nbsp;
ruler from its imprisonment.

00:31:24.960 --> 00:31:30.780
That was the single goal he united the cultists
under: Freedom for the Tentacled God.

00:31:30.780 --> 00:31:35.040
And at long last, they had all the pieces
in place to strike.

00:31:35.040 --> 00:31:40.020
They’d finally gathered the necessary intel
to subvert the will of the most powerful secret

00:31:40.020 --> 00:31:41.340
organization on earth.

00:31:41.340 --> 00:31:47.100
Even the strongest institution is made of
people, and people are weak.

00:31:47.100 --> 00:31:51.180
Unlike the almighty Tentacled God, people
could be broken.

00:31:51.180 --> 00:31:57.780
The people in question were Kelly Thompson,
Sidney Levitt, Jordan Brosh, Dr. Juan Gutierrez,

00:31:57.780 --> 00:31:59.160
and Gillian Larson.

00:31:59.160 --> 00:32:04.200
Dr. Juan Gutierrez was a researcher with Level
3 clearance on the site where the Tentacled

00:32:04.200 --> 00:32:05.580
God was being contained.

00:32:05.580 --> 00:32:10.680
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both Security
Officers charged with verifying personnel

00:32:10.680 --> 00:32:11.760
clearance on site.

00:32:11.760 --> 00:32:17.640
Kelly Thompson was a member of Site Administration
with research authorization powers, and Gillian

00:32:17.640 --> 00:32:21.900
Larson was a research assistant who often
collaborated with Dr. Gutierrez.

00:32:21.900 --> 00:32:29.940
These five were the key to getting access
to SCP-2662 and bringing their plan to fruition.

00:32:29.940 --> 00:32:35.040
Normally, personnel dossiers on people working
for the Foundation were highly confidential,

00:32:35.040 --> 00:32:38.820
but the Devotees of the Tentacled God had
their ways.

00:32:38.820 --> 00:32:43.380
They had a number of computer experts in their
ranks more than capable of hacking in and

00:32:43.380 --> 00:32:47.700
pulling some basic information off of Foundation
servers without being detected.

00:32:47.700 --> 00:32:52.560
For the other information they needed they
turned to some good, old-fashioned torture,

00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:56.640
which is often the most effective method when
you need some quick results.

00:32:56.640 --> 00:33:02.820
Of course, while the cult’s grip on sanity
may have been a little tenuous, they weren’t

00:33:02.820 --> 00:33:03.240
stupid.

00:33:03.240 --> 00:33:07.920
While gathering their intel, they also made
sure to find out what exactly they were up

00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:08.100
against.

00:33:08.100 --> 00:33:16.560
SCP-2662 was being held in a humanoid containment
cell, and guarded by on-site Task Force TAU-9,

00:33:16.560 --> 00:33:19.320
better known as the “Belligerent Bodyguards.”

00:33:19.320 --> 00:33:25.140
These aren’t lazy, donut-chomping mall cops
- these are a heavily trained, heavily armed

00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:25.980
fighting force.

00:33:25.980 --> 00:33:31.500
Though the cultists had one thing that these
Foundation soldiers didn’t: The element

00:33:31.500 --> 00:33:32.880
of surprise.

00:33:32.880 --> 00:33:37.800
For everything to go off perfectly, Brother
Marsh’s plans would have to be executed

00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:41.160
within a single day, and they were already
on the clock.

00:33:41.160 --> 00:33:47.940
TAU-9 had been charged with tracking down
any new SCP - 2662 cults and dismantling them,

00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:52.500
and Brother Marsh knew that it was only a
matter of time before the Foundation tracked

00:33:52.500 --> 00:33:54.600
them down and did the same to them.

00:33:54.600 --> 00:34:00.360
If they wanted any chance of freeing the Tentacled
God, then they needed to strike quickly and

00:34:00.360 --> 00:34:02.040
with overwhelming force.

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:05.880
The SCP-2662 worshippers were able to secure&nbsp;

00:34:05.880 --> 00:34:08.820
the addresses of the five&nbsp;
key Foundation personnel,

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:12.360
and station members outside&nbsp;
each of them - including&nbsp;

00:34:12.360 --> 00:34:14.880
one who could realistically imitate each.

00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:19.860
They waited for night to fall, and broke into
each of their homes as they slept.

00:34:19.860 --> 00:34:25.440
What followed was a sequence of ruthless and
efficient murders done in the cause of freeing

00:34:25.440 --> 00:34:25.980
their god.

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:29.280
Dr. Gutierrez was shot in the head while he
slept.

00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:34.080
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both stabbed
to death before either even realized what

00:34:34.080 --> 00:34:34.560
was happening.

00:34:34.560 --> 00:34:39.660
Thompson, who’d gotten up to use the bathroom,
went down in a hail of machine gun fire.

00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:44.280
Gillian Larson had seen that masked figures
were breaking into her home and attempted

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:47.820
to flee, but was caught and beaten to death
by cultists in her hallway.

00:34:47.820 --> 00:34:52.980
It was a strange irony that people whose day
jobs entailed working with some of the most

00:34:52.980 --> 00:34:58.440
dangerous and nightmarish anomalies imaginable
were murdered in their homes by nothing more

00:34:58.440 --> 00:34:59.880
than regular humans.

00:35:00.780 --> 00:35:07.020
So far, Brother Marsh’s plan had gone perfectly,
with all five key personnel murdered within

00:35:07.020 --> 00:35:08.100
a two minute period.

00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:13.140
Next, the selected doppelgängers stole clothes
from their victims’ closets and were handed

00:35:13.140 --> 00:35:14.640
the correct forged documentation.

00:35:14.640 --> 00:35:19.920
The next morning, each replacement began their
journeys to the site where the Tentacled God

00:35:19.920 --> 00:35:24.780
was being contained, while the rest of the
cult armed themselves in preparation for their

00:35:24.780 --> 00:35:26.100
own part in the plan.

00:35:26.820 --> 00:35:31.560
Nobody at the Foundation seemed to notice
anything amiss when the five arrived on site.

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:36.360
When you work for the SCP Foundation, more
mental energy is devoted to following the

00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:41.640
rules that keep you alive than to memorizing
the faces of all your co-workers and each

00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:46.800
one slipped neatly into position, disappearing
into the familiarity of office life.

00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:52.860
But, infiltrating the site was one thing,
getting past the Belligerent Bodyguards and

00:35:52.860 --> 00:35:57.240
into the cell of the Tentacled God would be
another thing entirely.

00:35:57.240 --> 00:36:00.240
That’s where the rest of the cult would
come into play.

00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:04.740
Heavily armed with whatever firearms they
could get their hands on, the rest of the

00:36:04.740 --> 00:36:09.840
Devotees of the Tentacled God - Brother Marsh
included - would attack the containment site

00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:10.980
head-on.

00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:15.780
In the ensuing chaos, the five cultists who
had already infiltrated the site could take

00:36:15.780 --> 00:36:19.200
advantage of the distraction, and break into
the containment chamber.

00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:20.820
It was perfect.

00:36:20.820 --> 00:36:25.140
They’d launch their attack from the outside…
and from within.

00:36:25.140 --> 00:36:29.280
When Brother Marsh declared that the time
was right, the assault began.

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:33.780
A legion of gun-wielding cultists seemed to
spring out of nowhere and started shooting

00:36:33.780 --> 00:36:36.660
up the warehouse that was a front for the
containment site.

00:36:36.660 --> 00:36:41.580
The site quickly mobilized guards and task
force members to take on the sudden threat,

00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:46.560
and just as Brother Marsh had anticipated,
the Site Director called on the majority of

00:36:46.560 --> 00:36:50.040
TAU-9 to help repel the violent cultists from
their perimeter.

00:36:50.040 --> 00:36:57.000
TAU-9 obeyed, leaving three task force members
behind to guard SCP - 2662’s containment

00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:57.480
chamber.

00:36:57.480 --> 00:37:02.400
They expected to be guarding the cell from
rampaging religious zealots seeking an audience

00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:03.180
with their god.

00:37:03.180 --> 00:37:08.520
What they didn’t expect was a group of five
Foundation employees walking right up to them

00:37:08.520 --> 00:37:14.100
and opening fire, killing two TAU-9 members
and taking the third as a hostage.

00:37:14.100 --> 00:37:19.260
While the war was being waged outside, the
infiltrators had found the Tentacled God’s

00:37:19.260 --> 00:37:21.900
containment cell in the low-risk humanoid
ward.

00:37:21.900 --> 00:37:27.300
Their hostage insisted that using him wouldn’t
give them any leverage - the rest of his team

00:37:27.300 --> 00:37:31.860
would neutralize the whole group, him included,
if that’s what it took to stop them.

00:37:31.860 --> 00:37:36.840
The infiltrators explained that using him
as leverage was never their intention - he

00:37:36.840 --> 00:37:38.100
wasn’t a hostage at all.

00:37:38.100 --> 00:37:40.680
He was a sacrifice.

00:37:41.400 --> 00:37:46.680
The cultists of the Tentacled God detonated
explosives, creating a hole in the wall and

00:37:46.680 --> 00:37:48.720
finally giving them access to their deity.

00:37:48.720 --> 00:37:51.900
They climbed through and gazed upon him in
awe.

00:37:51.900 --> 00:38:00.300
There stood SCP-2662, twice as tall as a regular
man, with ten huge tentacles emerging from

00:38:00.300 --> 00:38:00.780
its back.

00:38:00.780 --> 00:38:05.400
In their months of envisioning this creature,
they’d pictured it sitting on a throne made

00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:10.500
of thousands of human bones, ready to dictate
its commands to the obedient liberators.

00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:16.500
What they certainly didn’t expect was to
see the Tentacled God hunched over a computer

00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:16.980
screen.

00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:23.040
Still, gods work in mysterious ways, so they
stuck to the plan and began chanting.

00:38:23.040 --> 00:38:28.080
They pulled out a sacrificial dagger, and
began sacrificing their captured TAU-9 member.

00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:34.020
It was at this point that SCP - 2662 turned
and saw what they were doing with a look of

00:38:34.020 --> 00:38:35.040
pure horror.

00:38:35.040 --> 00:38:38.880
He rose up from his computer, his headphones
getting caught as he did so.

00:38:38.880 --> 00:38:43.740
He told them to go away, that he didn’t
want them here, and that them murdering people

00:38:43.740 --> 00:38:46.980
in his bedroom like this was inconsiderate
and disgusting.

00:38:46.980 --> 00:38:52.140
The cultists became even more confused - why
wasn’t their god accepting their offerings?

00:38:52.140 --> 00:38:53.760
What were they doing wrong?

00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:59.340
They tried more chanting, and painting arcane
symbols on the floor in blood, but this just

00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:00.900
seemed to make the creature angrier.

00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:06.660
He told them, in a tone more fitting for a
teenage boy than a Lovecraftian God, to just

00:39:06.660 --> 00:39:09.420
leave him alone so he could play his video
games.

00:39:09.420 --> 00:39:12.780
This was seriously not cool!

00:39:12.780 --> 00:39:15.060
The cultists were baffled.

00:39:15.060 --> 00:39:17.880
They told the Tentacled God they were there
to free him.

00:39:17.880 --> 00:39:20.160
He replied that he didn’t need saving.

00:39:20.700 --> 00:39:25.440
That crazy stalkers like them were why he
turned himself in to the Foundation in the

00:39:25.440 --> 00:39:25.920
first place!

00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:30.540
Before the cultist infiltrators could get
another word in, the remaining members of

00:39:30.540 --> 00:39:34.980
TAU-9 stormed into the containment cell and
gunned them down with surgical precision.

00:39:34.980 --> 00:39:40.320
The war outside was already over - Brother
Marsh and the rest of the cultists were all

00:39:40.320 --> 00:39:41.640
killed in the firefight.

00:39:41.640 --> 00:39:48.000
TAU-9 didn’t look the least bit surprised
upon entering 2662’s cell, this was a common

00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:49.200
occurrence unfortunately.

00:39:49.200 --> 00:39:56.640
They had to deal with an attempted cult invasion
every few months, because SCP-2662’s main

00:39:56.640 --> 00:40:01.560
anomalous ability is inspiring violent cults
who relentlessly track down and worship it

00:40:01.560 --> 00:40:03.960
with arcane and bloodthirsty rituals.

00:40:03.960 --> 00:40:10.680
The problem is, 2662 doesn’t do this consciously,
and definitely doesn’t like the results.

00:40:10.680 --> 00:40:16.080
That’s why he’s under the voluntary care
of the SCP Foundation who keeps him amused

00:40:16.080 --> 00:40:20.640
with video games and reading material while
fending off the deranged cults who try to

00:40:20.640 --> 00:40:22.200
invade and abduct him.

00:40:22.200 --> 00:40:27.480
Following the termination of The Devotees
of the Tentacled God, just one of many cults

00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:32.700
who’d broken into 2662’s containment cell,
the remaining TAU-9 members apologized to

00:40:32.700 --> 00:40:37.020
the tentacled creature for the disturbance,
allowing him to return to his gaming.

00:40:37.020 --> 00:40:41.340
They assured him that it’d probably be at
least a few more months before something like

00:40:41.340 --> 00:40:42.240
this happened again.

00:40:42.240 --> 00:40:49.380
SCP-2662’s cell was repaired, and the Foundation
returned to its task of seeking out would-be

00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:55.020
cultist emancipators, because for the SCP
Foundation, it’s not always about the anomaly

00:40:55.020 --> 00:40:58.560
that’s being kept in containment, but what’s
being kept out.

00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:04.140
It goes without saying that the SCP Foundation
archives are filled with some terrifying monsters.

00:41:04.140 --> 00:41:09.300
Even the deadliest creatures can, in theory,
be defeated, or at least soundly avoided.

00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:14.880
After all, they’re just flesh and blood
- or in some cases, metal or concrete.

00:41:14.880 --> 00:41:18.600
But what if reality as you know it one day
just…broke.

00:41:18.600 --> 00:41:23.880
Or worse, you were transported to a reality
so frightening and alien to our own that death

00:41:23.880 --> 00:41:27.840
seemed like the only escape – but you couldn’t
even give yourself that.

00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:34.560
This brings us to today’s topic – the
terrifying alternate reality of SCP – 3001.

00:41:34.560 --> 00:41:40.320
The Foundation is no stranger to freaky alternate
dimensions, but what was experienced by joint-lead

00:41:40.320 --> 00:41:45.240
researcher Dr. Robert Scranton at Site 120
is a truly unique nightmare.

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:51.780
Co-managed by his wife, Dr. Anna Lang, Site
120 is a facility largely designed for research

00:41:51.780 --> 00:41:55.140
into SCPs with dangerous&nbsp;
reality-warping capabilities&nbsp;

00:41:55.140 --> 00:41:57.960
in order to mitigate future containment breaches.

00:41:57.960 --> 00:42:03.300
Reality warpers are among some of the more
perplexing and dangerous SCPs, from the pocket

00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:09.540
dimension-creating SCP – 106 to the SCP-creating
Doctor Wondertainment, and everything in between.

00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:14.640
Scranton and Lang’s goal to further study
such entities was an admirable one, if a little

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:20.280
over-ambitious, and on January 2nd, 2000,
during the testing of a new technology created

00:42:20.280 --> 00:42:24.240
by the Foundation’s leading power couple,
disaster finally struck.

00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:29.340
Scranton and Lang had already been the brains
behind one of the Foundation’s most valuable

00:42:29.340 --> 00:42:34.560
tools in the fight against reality-bending
SCPs: The Scranton Reality Anchors.

00:42:34.560 --> 00:42:39.780
Their follow up, the Lang-Scranton Stabilizer
– or LSS – likely would have been an even

00:42:39.780 --> 00:42:44.340
more advanced variant of their earlier invention
and should have been a huge success for the

00:42:44.340 --> 00:42:44.580
team.

00:42:44.580 --> 00:42:46.860
But things didn’t turn out that way…

00:42:46.860 --> 00:42:51.780
Dr. Scranton and several other researchers
were gathered in Reality Lab A performing

00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:54.060
routine tests on the LSS prototypes.

00:42:54.060 --> 00:42:59.520
While other technicians ran diagnostics tests,
Scranton stood at the control panel, the blinking

00:42:59.520 --> 00:43:03.120
red light above the console confirming that
everything was going according to plan.

00:43:03.120 --> 00:43:07.320
But as anyone who’s fallen victim to one
of the Foundation’s many anomalies will

00:43:07.320 --> 00:43:11.280
tell you, just because you’ve done everything
correctly doesn’t mean you’re safe.

00:43:11.280 --> 00:43:15.840
Scranton began operating the machine, not
knowing that something was rumbling up towards

00:43:15.840 --> 00:43:16.560
him from below.

00:43:16.560 --> 00:43:22.020
Without warning, a sudden, unexpected burst
of seismic activity rocked the entire base.

00:43:22.020 --> 00:43:27.060
Researchers grabbed onto whatever was closest
as the world shook around them.

00:43:27.060 --> 00:43:32.160
In his panic, Dr. Scranton clung to the LSS
control panel as the seismic blast fried the

00:43:32.160 --> 00:43:34.260
circuits and kicked it into overdrive.

00:43:35.160 --> 00:43:39.660
There was a blast of magnificent, blinding
light, and when the rumbling stopped not only

00:43:39.660 --> 00:43:43.500
was the doctor gone, he had been erased from
reality as we know it.

00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:47.940
The earthquake had caused a deadly malfunction
in the machine meant to stabilize reality,

00:43:47.940 --> 00:43:53.400
and instead tore a rift in it, dragging the
unfortunate doctor and the control panel into

00:43:53.400 --> 00:43:54.120
oblivion.

00:43:54.720 --> 00:44:00.540
His wife, Dr. Lang, and the many researchers
who idolized him were devastated by his unexpected

00:44:00.540 --> 00:44:03.480
demise at the hand of what should have been
his crowning achievement.

00:44:03.480 --> 00:44:06.300
The one silver lining was&nbsp;
that this reality-ripping&nbsp;

00:44:06.300 --> 00:44:08.520
event had almost definitely eliminated the

00:44:08.520 --> 00:44:10.200
doctor quickly and painlessly.

00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:14.460
As far as The Foundation and his loved ones
were concerned, Scranton’s death had been

00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:19.560
immediate and complete – a luxury afforded
to few Foundation employees who die anomalous

00:44:19.560 --> 00:44:20.100
deaths.

00:44:20.100 --> 00:44:27.180
But sadly that isn’t how Dr. Scranton’s
story – or the story of SCP – 3001 – ends.

00:44:27.180 --> 00:44:29.820
No, this is where it all begins.

00:44:29.820 --> 00:44:31.440
How do we know all this?

00:44:31.440 --> 00:44:36.060
In the hellish new place where Scranton had
been transported, the control panel from the

00:44:36.060 --> 00:44:40.920
LSS that he’d been clinging to for dear
life had been transported with him, and continued

00:44:40.920 --> 00:44:43.500
to record audio data from this anomalous location.

00:44:43.500 --> 00:44:47.280
Not that Dr. Scranton realized it, not at
first, anyway.

00:44:47.280 --> 00:44:51.660
As far as he knew, he’d suddenly been transported
into a pitch-black location.

00:44:51.660 --> 00:44:54.720
No sights, no sounds, no scents.

00:44:54.720 --> 00:44:57.120
True nothingness.

00:44:57.120 --> 00:44:59.340
At first, the doctor was confused.

00:44:59.340 --> 00:45:04.620
One second, he was testing out his new technology,
and the next he was quite literally nowhere.

00:45:04.620 --> 00:45:09.060
In spite of his current situation, the doctor
was still an intelligent and rational man.

00:45:09.060 --> 00:45:13.620
He took a moment to compose himself, hoping
that in time his eyes would adjust to the

00:45:13.620 --> 00:45:14.700
new darkness around him.

00:45:14.700 --> 00:45:19.800
But that moment never came: The darkness remained
perfectly absolute.

00:45:19.800 --> 00:45:25.200
Much like the darkness in another reality-defying
SCP, the deadly endless staircase known as

00:45:25.200 --> 00:45:29.880
SCP – 087, the dark seemed thick, almost
like you could touch it.

00:45:29.880 --> 00:45:34.260
The doctor, not wanting to give himself to
despair and die in this impossible place,

00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:37.860
and with no other options seemingly available,
began walking.

00:45:37.860 --> 00:45:40.980
Either he’d find his way out, or the Foundation
would find him.

00:45:40.980 --> 00:45:42.120
No need to panic.

00:45:42.120 --> 00:45:47.040
It may have altered the doctor’s temperament
if he knew that the Foundation already assumed

00:45:47.040 --> 00:45:50.220
he was dead, and that no search party was
going to come looking for him.

00:45:50.820 --> 00:45:55.140
Still, logic dictates that if a person walks
for long enough, they’re bound to find something.

00:45:55.140 --> 00:46:00.900
The problem Scranton was about to face was
that SCP – 3001 doesn’t run by any kind

00:46:00.900 --> 00:46:02.160
of conventional logic.

00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:08.220
He walked and walked and walked, but he didn’t
seem to get any nearer to or farther from

00:46:08.220 --> 00:46:10.260
anything but how could even know?

00:46:10.260 --> 00:46:15.240
After all, in total darkness, there aren’t
any landmarks to assist in navigation.

00:46:15.240 --> 00:46:20.700
The doctor walked and paced and screamed for
days on end, but he made no progress.

00:46:20.700 --> 00:46:23.220
He was alone in an empty world.

00:46:23.220 --> 00:46:28.680
He had no choice though, so he kept walking,
and walking, and walking.

00:46:28.680 --> 00:46:30.780
For eleven days.

00:46:30.780 --> 00:46:34.260
During that time, he felt his hunger and thirst
grow.

00:46:34.260 --> 00:46:39.900
He was in terrible pain from a mix of starvation
and dehydration, but the release of death

00:46:39.900 --> 00:46:41.520
didn’t seem to come for him.

00:46:41.520 --> 00:46:45.960
He was going to have to learn the rules of
this new place the hard way, and it grimly

00:46:45.960 --> 00:46:50.700
dawned on Dr. Scranton that dying in this
place might not even be the worst possible

00:46:50.700 --> 00:46:51.300
outcome.

00:46:51.300 --> 00:46:56.100
He paced and repeated facts to himself, hoping
to ground himself in the moment and avoid

00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:58.080
the panic that could so easily set in.

00:46:58.080 --> 00:46:59.940
“Name, Robert Scranton.

00:46:59.940 --> 00:47:01.260
Age, 39.

00:47:01.260 --> 00:47:04.080
Birthday, September 19, 1961.

00:47:04.080 --> 00:47:05.640
Favorite color, blue.

00:47:05.640 --> 00:47:07.740
Favorite song, "Living on a Prayer."

00:47:07.740 --> 00:47:08.520
Wife…

00:47:09.420 --> 00:47:10.200
Anna…”

00:47:10.200 --> 00:47:14.940
Little by little, the words seemed to turn
to nonsense in his mouth as the terror grew.

00:47:14.940 --> 00:47:20.400
Just as he felt like he was about to lose
his mind, he noticed something - a small oasis

00:47:20.400 --> 00:47:26.940
in the endless darkness of SCP – 3001: The
glowing red light of the LSS control panel.

00:47:26.940 --> 00:47:28.440
Where had it come from?

00:47:28.440 --> 00:47:30.300
And how was it still recording?

00:47:30.300 --> 00:47:35.460
The doctor had no idea, but he was grateful
for any kind of familiarity in the strange

00:47:35.460 --> 00:47:36.480
darkness around him.

00:47:36.480 --> 00:47:40.860
Perhaps the LSS could be the key to saving
him, or at least figuring out what on earth

00:47:40.860 --> 00:47:41.760
was going on here?

00:47:41.760 --> 00:47:46.740
Whatever the case, there was no denying that
having the panel here was better than nothing.

00:47:46.740 --> 00:47:52.440
At least, when it was found… if it was ever
found, then people would know what had happened

00:47:52.440 --> 00:47:52.860
to him.

00:47:52.860 --> 00:47:55.860
As the days passed and he&nbsp;
continued to mysteriously&nbsp;

00:47:55.860 --> 00:47:58.620
survive, Dr Scranton deduced that one didn’t

00:47:58.620 --> 00:48:02.700
need food or water to survive continually
in SCP – 3001.

00:48:02.700 --> 00:48:06.120
The location had an anomalous effect on its
inhabitants.

00:48:06.900 --> 00:48:11.700
As the days passed and turned to weeks of
wandering in the darkness, Dr. Scranton further

00:48:11.700 --> 00:48:16.140
deduced that he was no longer in his home
dimension – this was an entirely separate

00:48:16.140 --> 00:48:21.360
pocket dimension, much like the one possessed
by SCP – 106, but featureless.

00:48:21.360 --> 00:48:24.240
A perfect, self-contained void.

00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:29.760
Now dimly illuminated by the red light of
the panel, Dr. Scranton explored further into

00:48:29.760 --> 00:48:30.780
the void around him.

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:36.120
He travelled for months on end, the pain of
his deficiencies growing by the day, but found

00:48:36.120 --> 00:48:37.260
he was getting nowhere.

00:48:38.040 --> 00:48:42.540
All things considered, he wasn’t even sure
he was moving, or whether reality and the

00:48:42.540 --> 00:48:45.060
darkness was swirling around him like a thick
liquid.

00:48:45.060 --> 00:48:47.760
Rather than walking on a single flat surface,&nbsp;

00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:50.880
he was moving in all directions&nbsp;
across a three-dimensional

00:48:50.880 --> 00:48:51.360
plane.

00:48:51.360 --> 00:48:55.980
The space-time continuum appeared to be entirely
broken here, where movement is more defined

00:48:55.980 --> 00:49:00.180
by the conscious intention to move than any
real geographical repositioning.

00:49:00.180 --> 00:49:05.220
Dr. Scranton knew that this place broke every
single one of Kejel's Laws of Reality Parameters,

00:49:05.220 --> 00:49:10.740
and from his years working with a plethora
of reality warpers in Site 120, he had a theory

00:49:10.740 --> 00:49:16.140
for why this pocket dimension was so strange:
It had an extraordinarily weak Hume field.

00:49:16.140 --> 00:49:20.820
Before we get back to Dr. Scranton’s semi-living
nightmare, we need a quick primer on Hume

00:49:20.820 --> 00:49:23.400
theory, and why having a weak Hume field is
such a problem.

00:49:23.400 --> 00:49:27.660
A Hume is a unit of measurement for the strength
and amount of reality in a given location

00:49:27.660 --> 00:49:28.320
or being.

00:49:28.320 --> 00:49:33.780
In an area with an incredibly low Hume field
relative to our world, such as SCP – 3001,

00:49:33.780 --> 00:49:37.380
universe breaches and anomalous incidences
rise significantly.

00:49:37.380 --> 00:49:42.540
At the time of his being trapped there, SCP
– 3001 had the lowest number of Humes in

00:49:42.540 --> 00:49:46.320
any recorded environment, making it a phenomenally
anomalous zone.

00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:51.000
It was for this reason that starvation and
dehydration never took hold of him despite

00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:54.900
causing him great pain, and the worst by far
was yet to come.

00:49:54.900 --> 00:49:58.620
Dr. Scranton wasn’t trapped in this dimension
for weeks or even months.

00:49:58.620 --> 00:50:00.960
He was trapped in the darkness for years.

00:50:00.960 --> 00:50:04.020
And it took a nightmarish toll on his body
and mind.

00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:09.600
The small flashing red light on his LSS control
panel became his only friend and as the years

00:50:09.600 --> 00:50:13.800
drew on, he would hold entire conversations
with his only source of illumination.

00:50:13.800 --> 00:50:18.300
He knew that his days were numbered – if
he didn’t escape dimension within around

00:50:18.300 --> 00:50:23.220
three years, the Hume field would diffuse
further, and he would be left in a truly horrific

00:50:23.220 --> 00:50:23.580
state.

00:50:23.580 --> 00:50:28.020
But based on how little headway he’d made
in the time he’d been there, he didn’t

00:50:28.020 --> 00:50:28.860
feel optimistic.

00:50:28.860 --> 00:50:33.180
He kept speaking into the recorder, if only
to break the silence and prevent him from

00:50:33.180 --> 00:50:34.620
going completely insane.

00:50:34.620 --> 00:50:37.920
But even that would only hold it off for so
long.

00:50:37.920 --> 00:50:42.720
Alone and talking to himself endlessly in
the darkness, Dr. Scranton could feel his

00:50:42.720 --> 00:50:47.760
mind slipping as the confines of the pocket
dimension constricted and his body began to

00:50:47.760 --> 00:50:48.060
change.

00:50:48.060 --> 00:50:53.280
The low Hume field slowly diffused his physical
matter, destroying the physical integrity

00:50:53.280 --> 00:50:57.120
of his body but never being merciful enough
to actually let him die.

00:50:57.120 --> 00:51:01.980
In his haunting audio logs, the doctor described
his hands as diffusing and thinning out like

00:51:01.980 --> 00:51:02.760
spider webs.

00:51:02.760 --> 00:51:08.340
Over time, there was less and less of him,
and what was left wasn’t entirely human.

00:51:08.340 --> 00:51:14.220
As Scranton’s Hume level lowered to equalize
with that of SCP – 3001, the lines between

00:51:14.220 --> 00:51:19.620
his body and the LSS control console began
to blur in a twisted marriage of warped flesh

00:51:19.620 --> 00:51:20.040
and machine.

00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:23.520
The Lang-Scranton Stabilizer was anything
but stable.

00:51:23.520 --> 00:51:28.440
Before his mind and body became something
else entirely, the doctor still had the presence

00:51:28.440 --> 00:51:32.100
of mind to finally realize how he’d come
to be in this terrible place.

00:51:32.940 --> 00:51:38.760
The LSS had opened a wormhole known as a Class-C
“Broken Entry” into a paradoxical pocket

00:51:38.760 --> 00:51:42.000
dimension between layers of reality, and taken
him through it.

00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:46.920
He’d slipped through a crack in reality
into absolute darkness, and now he was stuck

00:51:46.920 --> 00:51:48.900
with a fate far worse than death.

00:51:48.900 --> 00:51:50.460
How do we know any of this?

00:51:50.460 --> 00:51:53.700
Much like the event in the first place, it’s
a total accident.

00:51:54.420 --> 00:51:59.400
Testing superior reality-bending technology
almost six years after the disappearance caused

00:51:59.400 --> 00:52:03.360
the sudden return of the missing LSS to Site
120’s Reality Labs.

00:52:04.140 --> 00:52:08.040
The only trace of Dr. Scranton that it brought
back with it was the blood and viscera that

00:52:08.040 --> 00:52:12.420
coated the console, much to the abject horror
of his still grieving wife, Dr. Anna Lang.

00:52:12.420 --> 00:52:17.400
To this day, Dr. Scranton, formerly one of
the Foundation’s brightest minds, remains

00:52:17.400 --> 00:52:20.280
trapped in the nightmare of SCP – 3001.

00:52:20.280 --> 00:52:25.020
His current condition whether the doctor is
still alive after twenty years of being warped

00:52:25.020 --> 00:52:29.580
by the low Hume field of 3001’s darkened
confines is still unknown.

00:52:29.580 --> 00:52:34.440
But, for the doctor’s own sake, we hope
he’s been dead for quite some time, because

00:52:34.440 --> 00:52:38.100
few things on earth are as horrifying as the
alternative…

00:52:38.100 --> 00:52:44.580
On an ordinary day in 1991, a young man known
by the initials J.S. went on a hike with four

00:52:44.580 --> 00:52:47.340
of his friends on the wooded outskirts of
their small town.

00:52:47.340 --> 00:52:53.040
Everything seemed perfectly normal until J.S.
began to feel a strange sense of familiarity,

00:52:53.040 --> 00:52:55.260
like he had been in this spot before.

00:52:55.260 --> 00:52:58.680
He couldn’t shake this weird feeling, but
thought nothing more of it.

00:52:58.680 --> 00:53:02.400
Little did he know that this was a sign of
deadly things to come.

00:53:02.400 --> 00:53:07.800
Several hours after first experiencing that
sense of deja vu, J.S. was found by the side

00:53:07.800 --> 00:53:12.240
of the road, covered in cuts and scratches,
with his friends nowhere to be found.

00:53:12.240 --> 00:53:18.660
This is the story of SCP - 939, an unforgettable
monster that you’ll never remember.

00:53:19.620 --> 00:53:24.000
There was no way for J.S. to know that the
unsettling feeling he felt and the horrors

00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:29.580
that followed it were the result of an experiment
conducted by the SCP Foundation, an experiment

00:53:29.580 --> 00:53:31.620
with deadly unforeseen consequences.

00:53:32.460 --> 00:53:38.520
J.S. and his friends were exposed to a substance
known only as AMN-C227 as part of a series

00:53:38.520 --> 00:53:43.980
of tests performed by the SCP Foundation intended
to determine the effectiveness of this substance

00:53:43.980 --> 00:53:45.780
as a deliberate amnestic.

00:53:46.740 --> 00:53:52.800
Dealing with as many mysterious, secret creatures
and objects as they do, the SCP Foundation

00:53:52.800 --> 00:53:57.660
has long needed a way to tamper with the memories
of those exposed to the foundation’s various

00:53:57.660 --> 00:54:03.300
prisoners and test subjects, and, when the
foundation discovered AMN-C227, it seemed

00:54:03.300 --> 00:54:05.280
like it might be perfect for this purpose.

00:54:05.280 --> 00:54:08.700
So where did AMN-C227 come from?

00:54:08.700 --> 00:54:13.980
Over a year before the incident with J.S.
and his friends, the SCP Foundation captured

00:54:13.980 --> 00:54:15.540
SCP-939.

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:21.780
SCP-939 is a species of endothermic predators
that live and hunt in packs.

00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:26.700
They are designated Keter class, and regarded
as highly dangerous and hostile to human life.

00:54:26.700 --> 00:54:33.540
Native to caves, they have no eyes, translucent
red skin, and stand at an average of 2.2 meters

00:54:33.540 --> 00:54:36.480
tall, with an average weight of 250 kg.

00:54:37.140 --> 00:54:40.380
They have four limbs, each&nbsp;
ending in three-fingered&nbsp;

00:54:40.380 --> 00:54:42.840
claws and a fourth opposable digit resembling

00:54:42.840 --> 00:54:43.260
a thumb.

00:54:43.800 --> 00:54:48.360
In addition to their sharp claws, their mouths
are filled with red, fang-like teeth that

00:54:48.360 --> 00:54:50.340
reach up to 6 cm in length.

00:54:50.880 --> 00:54:53.520
In place of their absent eyes,&nbsp;
they have light-sensitive&nbsp;

00:54:53.520 --> 00:54:56.400
spots running along their backs, which are

00:54:56.400 --> 00:55:00.540
covered in spines believed to detect changes
in air pressure and flow.

00:55:00.540 --> 00:55:06.060
In addition to their many other terrifying
attributes, the internal anatomy of SCP-939

00:55:06.060 --> 00:55:08.100
poses a biological mystery.

00:55:08.100 --> 00:55:11.880
These creatures have no circulatory system
and no digestive tract.

00:55:11.880 --> 00:55:17.220
That’s right, in spite of being predators
seemingly acting on a need to feed, they have

00:55:17.220 --> 00:55:17.880
no stomach.

00:55:17.880 --> 00:55:22.620
Instead, when they eat their food builds up
in their respiratory system until its presence

00:55:22.620 --> 00:55:25.740
inhibits function, and then it is regurgitated.

00:55:25.740 --> 00:55:30.720
In spite of being a creature that should not,
under any logical conditions, be able to live,

00:55:30.720 --> 00:55:37.200
SCP-939 continues to persist, and is even
capable of giving birth to live young after

00:55:37.200 --> 00:55:39.360
a gestation period of 12 months.

00:55:40.020 --> 00:55:44.340
The SCP Foundation was able to study a litter
of these young that were born in captivity

00:55:44.340 --> 00:55:49.500
in September of 1992, though the creatures
remain just as much of a scientific mystery

00:55:49.500 --> 00:55:51.360
as they were upon first discovery.

00:55:52.020 --> 00:55:57.060
Everything about them seems to defy the logic
of the natural world - which, to be fair,

00:55:57.060 --> 00:55:59.040
is really nothing new for the Foundation.

00:55:59.040 --> 00:56:05.700
The respiratory system of SCP-939 was found
to exhale small traces of an airborne amnestic

00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:09.060
substance, given the name AMN-C227.

00:56:09.060 --> 00:56:13.980
This compound blocks the formation of memories
for the duration of exposure to it, plus a

00:56:13.980 --> 00:56:17.160
thirty minute period following the exposure,
give or take a few minutes.

00:56:17.160 --> 00:56:22.680
It is colorless, odorless, tasteless, and
completely undetectable in the bloodstream

00:56:22.680 --> 00:56:24.420
after only 60 minutes.

00:56:24.420 --> 00:56:31.080
AMN-C227 was approved for use as a Class C
Amnestic by the SCP Foundation in 1990 following

00:56:31.080 --> 00:56:32.160
some initial tests.

00:56:32.160 --> 00:56:37.320
However, after one particular incident involving
a young man and his friends, the official

00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:39.840
use of AMN-C227 was suspended.

00:56:39.840 --> 00:56:46.020
J.S. and three of his four friends were previously
given a dose of AMN-C227, though the details

00:56:46.020 --> 00:56:49.080
of why they were given the amnestic have since
been stricken from the record.

00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:55.620
Several months after being exposed to AMN-C227,
J.S. and friends went out on their ill-fated

00:56:55.620 --> 00:56:56.340
hiking trip.

00:56:56.340 --> 00:57:00.180
While hiking, J.S. was suddenly overcome with
a sense of deja vu.

00:57:00.180 --> 00:57:03.600
When he mentioned it to his friends, three
of them agreed that they felt it too.

00:57:03.600 --> 00:57:05.820
One of the group, another young man - who&nbsp;

00:57:05.820 --> 00:57:09.000
had not been exposed to&nbsp;
AMN-C227 - was uncomfortable

00:57:09.000 --> 00:57:10.260
and decided to go home.

00:57:11.040 --> 00:57:15.060
J.S. and the remaining three members of the
group made the choice to stay in the woods

00:57:15.060 --> 00:57:19.020
and try to determine what was triggering the
unusual feeling of familiarity.

00:57:19.020 --> 00:57:24.120
As they got closer and closer to a large cave
near the hiking trail, the sense of having

00:57:24.120 --> 00:57:26.820
been there before grew stronger and stronger.

00:57:27.420 --> 00:57:32.700
Armed with only one flashlight and a foolish
curiosity, the four went inside the cave.

00:57:33.240 --> 00:57:39.240
They made their way deeper and deeper into
the darkness, not knowing why they felt this

00:57:39.240 --> 00:57:40.920
way or what they might find inside.

00:57:40.920 --> 00:57:45.960
None of the group could explain just what
felt so familiar, only that the further they

00:57:45.960 --> 00:57:49.620
made their way into the cave, the more pronounced
the feeling became.

00:57:49.620 --> 00:57:53.760
It was getting late, and they knew they should
have been afraid to venture so deep into a

00:57:53.760 --> 00:57:59.280
cave with only one light source and no knowledge
of what lay inside, but still they pressed

00:57:59.280 --> 00:57:59.460
on.

00:57:59.460 --> 00:58:03.360
One of the group remarked that they should
turn back, but the others refused to listen.

00:58:03.360 --> 00:58:07.380
They wanted to know what they were getting
close to, what was drawing them deeper and

00:58:07.380 --> 00:58:08.400
deeper into the cave.

00:58:08.400 --> 00:58:11.640
Unfortunately for them, they would get their
answer.

00:58:11.640 --> 00:58:17.640
In the heart of the cave was a pack of SCP-939,
waiting patiently for their prey to wander

00:58:17.640 --> 00:58:18.480
into their domain.

00:58:18.480 --> 00:58:22.440
There are no witnesses to account for what
exactly happened to J.S. and his companions,

00:58:22.440 --> 00:58:26.100
but we can reasonably piece the events together
from what happened after.

00:58:26.100 --> 00:58:30.300
Once the friends reached the heart of the
cave, the creatures were on them in seconds,

00:58:30.300 --> 00:58:33.600
raking them with their sharp claws and biting
with their fangs.

00:58:33.600 --> 00:58:38.880
SCP-939 are larger and stronger than most
people, so it was probably not much of a fight.

00:58:38.880 --> 00:58:43.740
However, while his friends were being devoured,
J.S. was somehow able to scramble out of the

00:58:43.740 --> 00:58:46.320
cave and make his way into the woods in search
of help.

00:58:46.320 --> 00:58:51.060
Under the influence of the AMN-C227 that had
built up in the cave from the presence of

00:58:51.060 --> 00:58:56.100
the pack of SCP-939, J.S. lost a large portion
of his memory of the event.

00:58:56.100 --> 00:59:00.960
He found himself on the side of the highway
late at night, seriously injured and his clothes

00:59:00.960 --> 00:59:01.560
ripped.

00:59:01.560 --> 00:59:06.060
An officer found him there, and asked him
to stay still and remain calm until an ambulance

00:59:06.060 --> 00:59:06.600
could arrive.

00:59:06.600 --> 00:59:11.640
J.S. was still in a panic and attempted to
run away from the officer, begging to be released

00:59:11.640 --> 00:59:12.540
so that he could get away.

00:59:12.540 --> 00:59:17.640
He babbled incoherently about the color red,
screaming over and over again about the “red,”

00:59:17.640 --> 00:59:21.660
though when prompted he could not explain
what the “red” he was screaming about

00:59:21.660 --> 00:59:22.560
referred to.

00:59:22.560 --> 00:59:24.120
His friends were not with him.

00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:28.200
Just as the officer managed to calm J.S.,
the ambulance arrived.

00:59:28.200 --> 00:59:33.060
Its flashing red lights sent him into another
frenzy, and he attempted to escape custody,

00:59:33.060 --> 00:59:35.520
claiming that the red lights were “going
to get” him.

00:59:35.520 --> 00:59:39.900
The official police report described J.S.
as perhaps being under the influence of a

00:59:39.900 --> 00:59:40.920
powerful hallucinogen.

00:59:40.920 --> 00:59:45.240
That he was just having a “bad trip,”
but the SCP foundation knew better.

00:59:45.900 --> 00:59:50.460
The foundation conducted an interview with
J.S. about his experience, and determined

00:59:50.460 --> 00:59:53.520
that SCP-939 was certainly involved.

00:59:53.520 --> 00:59:58.140
As part of their cover-up effort, they strongly
implicated J.S. in the disappearance and death

00:59:58.140 --> 00:59:58.740
of his friends.

00:59:58.740 --> 01:00:02.760
He was convicted of manslaughter, though the
bodies of his friends were never found.

01:00:02.760 --> 01:00:08.100
It is rumored that the SCP Foundation hired
him on a prison work release program, and

01:00:08.100 --> 01:00:12.360
that he now works as a member of the janitorial
staff at one of the Foundation’s facilities.

01:00:13.140 --> 01:00:18.780
This incident led to the suspension of the
use of AMN-C227, as it revealed some vital

01:00:18.780 --> 01:00:21.600
and disturbing information about the compound’s
side effects.

01:00:21.600 --> 01:00:27.420
After exposure to AMN-C227, a person who found
themselves exposed to it again would experience

01:00:27.420 --> 01:00:31.740
a sense of familiarity, and feel compelled
to investigate the source of this feeling.

01:00:31.740 --> 01:00:37.920
Essentially, anyone treated with AMN-C227
and not made aware of the existence - and

01:00:37.920 --> 01:00:43.680
danger - of SCP-939 would become a perfect
victim, primed to be attracted to dens of

01:00:43.680 --> 01:00:45.180
SCP-939.

01:00:45.180 --> 01:00:50.040
It is likely that this side effect is not
a coincidence, but rather a deliberate hunting

01:00:50.040 --> 01:00:53.640
tactic designed to attract prey that had somehow
managed to escape.

01:00:53.640 --> 01:00:59.580
With no memory of their attack at the hands
of SCP-939, this previous intended prey would

01:00:59.580 --> 01:01:04.260
find themselves drawn to the same den or even
a new one, not knowing that they were walking

01:01:04.260 --> 01:01:06.120
back into near certain death.

01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:12.120
While the SCP foundation suspended the use
of AMN-C227 as a Class C amnestic, they did

01:01:12.120 --> 01:01:16.200
recruit a team of SCP field operatives to
take advantage of this side effect.

01:01:16.200 --> 01:01:18.960
This team of operatives was&nbsp;
deliberately administered&nbsp;

01:01:18.960 --> 01:01:22.320
a dose of AMN-C227 and briefed on its effects,

01:01:22.320 --> 01:01:26.640
as well as the dangers of following the feeling
of deja vu should it surface in the field.

01:01:26.640 --> 01:01:32.220
These infected officers were essentially used
as bloodhounds, relying on any sense of unusual

01:01:32.220 --> 01:01:38.160
familiarity to sniff out new dens of SCP-939
so that they could be captured and contained

01:01:38.160 --> 01:01:39.000
by the foundation.

01:01:39.660 --> 01:01:43.260
As far as we know, this operation is still
ongoing today.

01:01:43.260 --> 01:01:48.780
However, now that the foundation has a sufficient
number of specimens to study, additional dens

01:01:48.780 --> 01:01:52.920
of SCP-939 that are discovered are ordered
to be immediately destroyed.

01:01:52.920 --> 01:01:55.620
As for the SCP-939 still in captivity?

01:01:55.620 --> 01:02:00.360
They are contained in environmentally regulated
and negatively pressurized cells with walls

01:02:00.360 --> 01:02:01.560
of reinforced concrete.

01:02:01.560 --> 01:02:07.740
The doors to the cells are air-tight to prevent
the leakage of any AMN-C227, and any personnel

01:02:07.740 --> 01:02:12.060
that interact with one of the creatures is
required to wear Level C Hazmat gear to avoid

01:02:12.060 --> 01:02:16.260
exposure, and follow decontamination procedures
upon exiting the cell.

01:02:16.260 --> 01:02:22.200
All SCP-939 have subdermal tracking devices
implanted to find them in the event of escape.

01:02:22.920 --> 01:02:27.984
Only one SCP-939 has given birth in the time
that the creatures have been in captivity,

01:02:27.984 --> 01:02:28.020
and only one of the litter survived.

01:02:28.020 --> 01:02:34.440
Strangely, SCP-939 young look indistinguishable
from human infants, and change their physical

01:02:34.440 --> 01:02:37.140
appearance at some yet unknown point as they
age.

01:02:37.140 --> 01:02:42.060
If any more offspring are produced, they will
immediately be separated from the parent and

01:02:42.060 --> 01:02:42.480
studied.

01:02:42.480 --> 01:02:42.712
The SCP foundation has redacted all information
about the location of these creatures or the

01:02:42.711 --> 01:02:42.899
incident involving J.S., refusing to reveal
where their natural habitat is.

01:02:42.900 --> 01:02:47.400
All that we know is that they are found in
caves in the woods outside of a small town.

01:02:47.400 --> 01:02:50.580
It could be any town, even yours.

01:02:50.580 --> 01:02:55.560
Sp if you’re ever out hiking, and are struck
with a sudden feeling of deja vu?

01:02:56.100 --> 01:03:00.480
Don’t investigate, don’t get curious,
just go home.

01:03:01.140 --> 01:03:02.880
It might just save your life.

01:03:02.880 --> 01:03:04.260
What’s in a name?

01:03:04.260 --> 01:03:08.640
Ancient folklore and fairy tales sometimes
tell of the importance of names, that they

01:03:08.640 --> 01:03:10.740
can hold the power to summon or banish.

01:03:10.740 --> 01:03:15.840
Whether you buy into the superstition or not,
you’d be unwise to ignore the power a name

01:03:15.840 --> 01:03:20.220
can have, especially if you ever dare to venture
into SCP-4000.

01:03:20.220 --> 01:03:20.940
Why?

01:03:20.940 --> 01:03:24.180
Use your own name too many&nbsp;
times in this extradimensional&nbsp;

01:03:24.180 --> 01:03:26.574
forest, and you may find that what walks out

01:03:26.574 --> 01:03:28.140
of it isn’t you at all.

01:03:28.140 --> 01:03:33.300
At least once a year, the Foundation leads
an expedition into SCP-4000, to explore this

01:03:33.300 --> 01:03:34.500
Keter-class dimension.

01:03:34.500 --> 01:03:38.400
But if you go down to those woods today, then
you’d better follow the rules.

01:03:38.400 --> 01:03:42.960
Remember, the Foundation has implemented these
strict guidelines for your own safety, and

01:03:42.960 --> 01:03:44.880
it’s in your best interest to follow them.

01:03:44.880 --> 01:03:50.280
First and foremost, when referencing anything
inside SCP-4000, be it a person, place or

01:03:50.280 --> 01:03:54.180
thing, you cannot under any circumstances
use names or titles.

01:03:54.180 --> 01:03:59.760
Communication is key when exploring SCP-4000,
and making use of specific descriptors will

01:03:59.760 --> 01:04:02.040
deter any adverse effects on your journey.

01:04:02.040 --> 01:04:06.720
For example, you may want to refer to the
location of SCP-4000 as “the woods where

01:04:06.720 --> 01:04:09.900
you need to speak carefully”, an apt description
for such a place.

01:04:09.900 --> 01:04:14.520
Of course, there’s a reason the Foundation
doesn’t provide a handy flashcard of alternative

01:04:14.520 --> 01:04:18.840
descriptors for any personnel taking part
in the annual mission into SCP-4000.

01:04:18.840 --> 01:04:24.060
Nothing found there can be referred to with
any consistent name, so it is perhaps advisable

01:04:24.060 --> 01:04:26.580
to look over a thesaurus&nbsp;
and expand your vocabulary&nbsp;

01:04:26.580 --> 01:04:29.460
before visiting SCP-4000, as you’ll need

01:04:29.460 --> 01:04:33.240
to come up with a lot of different ways to
refer to the people and creatures around you.

01:04:33.240 --> 01:04:37.020
But don’t worry, the Foundation will be
able to train you how to properly refer to

01:04:37.020 --> 01:04:39.960
SCP-4000 in both written and verbal communication.

01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:44.160
In a similar vein, the second rule states
that no personnel member should respond to

01:04:44.160 --> 01:04:46.620
their own name while in SCP-4000.

01:04:46.620 --> 01:04:51.000
Naturally, you and your fellow expedition
team will not be alone in the forest you find

01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:51.540
yourselves in.

01:04:51.540 --> 01:04:56.880
The denizens of SCP-4000 are perpetually-mutating
creatures, some appearing to be trustworthy

01:04:56.880 --> 01:04:57.960
while others are hostile.

01:04:57.960 --> 01:05:02.880
It is for personnel members’ own safety
that no consistent names or titles are used

01:05:02.880 --> 01:05:04.560
to refer to each other in conversation.

01:05:04.560 --> 01:05:10.260
This has been known to cause personnel returning
from SCP-4000 to experience vivid hallucinations,

01:05:10.260 --> 01:05:15.540
and in some instances has led to appearances
of creatures found in SCP-4000 in our world.

01:05:15.540 --> 01:05:20.940
Thirdly, when interacting with the lifeforms
residing in SCP-4000, personnel are advised

01:05:20.940 --> 01:05:25.080
to accept any gifts that they are offered,
but are warned to, under no circumstances,

01:05:25.080 --> 01:05:28.680
consume anything that is given to them while
inside the forest.

01:05:28.680 --> 01:05:33.660
Finally, and above all, do not divulge any
name, nickname, codename, alias, or any other

01:05:33.660 --> 01:05:38.880
personal designation when interacting with
any native entities, and disregard any designator

01:05:38.880 --> 01:05:42.300
that an inhabitant of SCP-4000 attempts to
assign to you.

01:05:42.300 --> 01:05:46.800
Personnel must, however, remain courteous
in the presence of any native creature of

01:05:46.800 --> 01:05:50.820
SCP-4000, and treat these entities with respect
and formality.

01:05:50.820 --> 01:05:57.180
Access to SCP-4000 can only be achieved by
performing Procedure 4000-Halloway, a ritual

01:05:57.180 --> 01:06:02.040
requiring a steady flame in an indoor fireplace,
fuelled by only organic kindling.

01:06:02.040 --> 01:06:07.260
Personnel are required to combine the powdered
bones of one male lion, one male red fox and

01:06:07.260 --> 01:06:11.880
a baleen whale, and cast these into the fire
with a personal possession holding strong

01:06:11.880 --> 01:06:14.940
sentimental value to the staff member performing
4000-Halloway.

01:06:14.940 --> 01:06:19.800
Next, personnel are to add three feathers
of a bird such as a raven, or crow, and must

01:06:19.800 --> 01:06:23.520
respond with the correct counter phrases once
the fire begins to emit a voice.

01:06:23.520 --> 01:06:27.900
If these conditions are met, and the correct
responses given, Foundation personnel will

01:06:27.900 --> 01:06:30.660
gain access to the entry point of SCP-4000.

01:06:30.660 --> 01:06:35.700
If any error is made during the course of
performing Procedure 4000-Halloway, then under

01:06:35.700 --> 01:06:37.980
no circumstances should this ritual be repeated.

01:06:37.980 --> 01:06:42.360
Staff are urged to apologise for any incorrect
actions, then refrain from engaging in this

01:06:42.360 --> 01:06:43.200
procedure in the future.

01:06:43.200 --> 01:06:48.000
Should Procedure 4000-Halloway be completed
successfully, Foundation personnel will find

01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:52.800
themselves arriving in the access point to
SCP-4000, emerging from the mouth of an old

01:06:52.800 --> 01:06:54.360
well in the center of the forest.

01:06:54.360 --> 01:06:59.700
Exploration teams sent into SCP-4000 are advised
that this dimension does not adhere to the

01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:02.340
laws of physical space that personnel will
be accustomed to.

01:07:02.340 --> 01:07:07.560
There is a single, confirmed-safe route that
must be used when traversing the forest of

01:07:07.560 --> 01:07:12.780
SCP-4000, a dirt path leading in a circuit
both beginning and terminating at the entry

01:07:12.780 --> 01:07:12.960
point.

01:07:12.960 --> 01:07:17.580
Previous attempts to map the landscape of
SCP-4000 all confirm that the only way to

01:07:17.580 --> 01:07:21.660
safely exit this dimension is to follow the
entire length of this path in one direction,

01:07:21.660 --> 01:07:23.880
until eventually returning to the well.

01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:28.740
You have been warned, any attempt to travel
back the direction you came will result in

01:07:28.740 --> 01:07:31.080
a loss of contact with the rest of the expedition
team.

01:07:31.080 --> 01:07:36.240
As mentioned, SCP-4000 is home to a number
of entities, often noted to be undergoing

01:07:36.240 --> 01:07:38.220
continuous and dramatic changes in form.

01:07:38.220 --> 01:07:43.020
These physiological mutations appear to occur
whenever these creatures are unobserved, making

01:07:43.020 --> 01:07:44.760
distinguishing between them difficult.

01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:49.200
When questioned about the exact nature of
these changes, the inhabitants of SCP-4000

01:07:49.200 --> 01:07:54.180
claim to have no control over them, and express
distress and dissatisfaction when said changes

01:07:54.180 --> 01:07:54.480
occur.

01:07:54.480 --> 01:07:56.760
Guidelines have been put&nbsp;
in place by the Foundation&nbsp;

01:07:56.760 --> 01:07:58.860
regarding the interactions between personnel

01:07:58.860 --> 01:08:03.240
and creatures found in the forest, and adhering
to the rules regarding the use of consistent

01:08:03.240 --> 01:08:05.400
names and titles remains vitally important.

01:08:05.400 --> 01:08:09.900
The native creatures appear semi-humanoid,
and are reported to be highly temperamental.

01:08:09.900 --> 01:08:14.580
Should any staff member happen to offend one
of these natives, they may be subjected to

01:08:14.580 --> 01:08:19.920
anything from verbal assault, to acts of extreme
physical violence from the SCP-4000 resident.

01:08:19.920 --> 01:08:24.660
If any Foundation personnel further question
why there are so many rules when visiting

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:30.180
SCP-4000, then they need look no further than
the discoveries and fate of Dr Eugene Japers,

01:08:30.180 --> 01:08:36.120
who during his initial expedition to SCP-4000
in 2005, encountered a humanoid native entity

01:08:36.120 --> 01:08:37.680
whose head resembled a rabbit’s.

01:08:37.680 --> 01:08:42.120
As the pair shared a polite conversation,
the rabbit-like creature made an enquiry regarding

01:08:42.120 --> 01:08:44.580
Dr Japers’ name, asking:
“How is your name?”

01:08:44.580 --> 01:08:49.740
Keeping to the rules, Dr Japers did not divulge
any name or other form of title to the creature,

01:08:49.740 --> 01:08:50.460
at this time.

01:08:50.460 --> 01:08:53.880
However, Japers remained courteous and polite
during this interaction.

01:08:53.880 --> 01:08:56.880
The rabbit responded with the following:
“Are you simple?

01:08:56.880 --> 01:08:58.620
I'm merely asking how your name is.

01:08:58.620 --> 01:09:03.240
My name has smelt of raspberries lately, I
think - or snapdragons, perhaps.

01:09:03.240 --> 01:09:05.640
It's so hard to tell these days, but one makes
an effort.”

01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:10.320
In his reply, Dr Japers made reference to
his own name as having ‘tasted rather tart

01:09:10.320 --> 01:09:13.680
as of late’, before concluding the conversation
with the rabbit entity.

01:09:13.680 --> 01:09:18.720
Upon returning to the SCP-4000 forest three
years later, Dr Japers was met with the same

01:09:18.720 --> 01:09:21.480
creature, and once again engaged in conversation
with it.

01:09:21.480 --> 01:09:25.860
After briefly discussing their previous encounter,
Dr Japers was able to turn their exchange

01:09:25.860 --> 01:09:29.700
towards something the rabbit had mentioned
before, about finding it difficult to describe

01:09:29.700 --> 01:09:30.240
its own name.

01:09:30.240 --> 01:09:32.880
When asked to clarify this point, the rabbit
replied:

01:09:32.880 --> 01:09:37.440
“I can only assume it's because of how long
we've been apart - my name and I, that is.

01:09:37.440 --> 01:09:40.020
It was a good name, a proud name, I'm fairly
sure.

01:09:40.020 --> 01:09:44.580
By this point, though, it's probably decayed
from its former grandeur, if it even still

01:09:44.580 --> 01:09:45.180
exists.”

01:09:45.180 --> 01:09:49.500
After this mention of its relationship with
its own name, it should be noted that the

01:09:49.500 --> 01:09:52.560
rabbit referred to Dr Japers by the title
‘fellow scholar’.

01:09:52.560 --> 01:09:57.960
The third and final encounter between Dr Japers
and this entity came in 2013, after the doctor

01:09:57.960 --> 01:10:02.280
was sent into SCP-4000 with instructions to
conduct a more thorough interview with the

01:10:02.280 --> 01:10:02.580
subject.

01:10:02.580 --> 01:10:05.100
It was during their third conversation that&nbsp;

01:10:05.100 --> 01:10:07.920
the rabbit-man revealed&nbsp;
details of a long-forgotten

01:10:07.920 --> 01:10:10.920
war between human beings and the residents
of SCP-4000.

01:10:10.920 --> 01:10:15.120
Apparently these creatures, the ‘Fae’,
do not originate from the forest in which

01:10:15.120 --> 01:10:18.660
they now reside, and – according to the
rabbit-man’s claims – were born in our

01:10:18.660 --> 01:10:18.900
world.

01:10:18.900 --> 01:10:22.560
“Much as it grieves me to say it, we were
betrayed,” the rabbit explained.

01:10:22.560 --> 01:10:25.800
“We had fought side-by-side, you know, in
the war against that factory.

01:10:25.800 --> 01:10:28.740
We had done nothing but help them, and what
did they do?

01:10:28.740 --> 01:10:29.820
They destroyed us.

01:10:29.820 --> 01:10:32.580
They took so many of our lives, and all of
our names.

01:10:32.580 --> 01:10:35.700
Some of us fled here when the war was just
beginning, but not many.

01:10:35.700 --> 01:10:36.420
Not many.

01:10:36.420 --> 01:10:38.100
Still, though, I don't hate them.”

01:10:38.100 --> 01:10:42.540
It has been assumed by some that the Foundation
was directly involved in whatever may have

01:10:42.540 --> 01:10:47.580
wiped out the Fae, causing them to either
retreat or be banished to the forest of SCP-4000.

01:10:47.580 --> 01:10:51.480
An additional assumption has been made that
whatever weapons were used on these creatures

01:10:51.480 --> 01:10:54.000
is directly responsible for&nbsp;
their constantly-shifting&nbsp;

01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:55.920
state, rendering them without their own names

01:10:55.920 --> 01:10:56.760
or identities.

01:10:56.760 --> 01:11:00.720
Whatever the case may be, it was during their
conversation that Dr Japers, in reference

01:11:00.720 --> 01:11:05.220
to their second encounter, referred to himself
as a ‘fellow scholar’ to the rabbit, in

01:11:05.220 --> 01:11:06.600
order to coax information from him.

01:11:06.600 --> 01:11:10.620
However, in doing so, the doctor had unwittingly
accepted the title that the native entity

01:11:10.620 --> 01:11:11.220
had given him.

01:11:11.220 --> 01:11:15.480
By mistakenly responding to the name ‘fellow
scholar’, the doctor had broken the rules

01:11:15.480 --> 01:11:20.100
of interacting with the creatures of SCP-4000;
an easy mistake, but a costly one.

01:11:20.100 --> 01:11:25.260
The doctor would later leave SCP-4000, traversing
the safe path back to the well.

01:11:25.260 --> 01:11:30.120
Dr Japers vanished shortly after his exit
from SCP-4000, and his whereabouts are currently

01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:30.540
unknown.

01:11:30.540 --> 01:11:34.800
The Foundation has made several attempts to
investigate his untimely disappearance, but

01:11:34.800 --> 01:11:39.420
to this day he remains missing and the fur
left on the inside of his expedition gear

01:11:39.420 --> 01:11:40.860
displayed no strange properties.

01:11:40.860 --> 01:11:46.140
The single goal, it would seem, of the creatures
residing in SCP-4000, is the theft of names.

01:11:46.140 --> 01:11:50.220
However, this naturally extends far beyond
this dimension’s definition of identity

01:11:50.220 --> 01:11:50.640
theft.

01:11:50.640 --> 01:11:54.600
Through an unfortunate blunder, Dr Japers
allowed the friendly nature and demeanour

01:11:54.600 --> 01:11:57.780
of the rabbit-entity to trick him into accepting
the name ‘fellow scholar’.

01:11:57.780 --> 01:12:02.400
By giving Dr Japers a name, the rabbit was
free to steal, not only his name, but his

01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:03.060
very identity.

01:12:03.060 --> 01:12:07.260
While it is unclear how this transference
is achieved by the creatures, it is due to

01:12:07.260 --> 01:12:11.820
the risk of this that the Foundation employs
such strict rules for any research team tasked

01:12:11.820 --> 01:12:14.220
with travelling to the forest of SCP-4000.

01:12:14.220 --> 01:12:19.320
Make no mistake, names have more power than
we realize, and this is evident in few places

01:12:19.320 --> 01:12:25.020
more so than SCP-4000, a pocket dimension
where ever-changing survivors of a forgotten

01:12:25.020 --> 01:12:27.060
massacre exist as identities alone.

01:12:27.060 --> 01:12:31.380
Remember, a name is a powerful thing whichever
side of the well you find yourself on.

01:12:31.380 --> 01:12:36.000
Your name binds you to who you are, but if
your name becomes someone else’s, then what

01:12:36.000 --> 01:12:37.560
else of yours becomes theirs too?

01:12:37.560 --> 01:12:39.240
It was just a job.

01:12:39.240 --> 01:12:44.460
You were meant to be mopping floors and cleaning
toilets at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals

01:12:44.460 --> 01:12:46.380
Research Center for minimum wage.

01:12:46.380 --> 01:12:51.780
And you were happy about it, grateful for
any kind of employment - you didn’t even

01:12:51.780 --> 01:12:57.420
know that the company signing your checks
was the SCP Foundation, an organization dedicated

01:12:57.420 --> 01:13:00.480
to securing and containing&nbsp;
anomalies and protecting&nbsp;

01:13:00.480 --> 01:13:03.300
humanity from their negative effects at any

01:13:03.300 --> 01:13:03.720
cost.

01:13:03.720 --> 01:13:08.760
And today, you’re going to find out exactly
how steep that cost can be.

01:13:08.760 --> 01:13:13.380
The Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research
Center isn’t actually a research center

01:13:13.380 --> 01:13:15.780
at all: It’s a Foundation front business,&nbsp;

01:13:15.780 --> 01:13:18.900
with a building solely&nbsp;
dedicated to the containment

01:13:18.900 --> 01:13:22.980
of a single anomaly: SCP-3280.

01:13:22.980 --> 01:13:28.320
But again, you’re just the janitor, it’s
not like they would bother telling you what’s

01:13:28.320 --> 01:13:29.460
being contained here.

01:13:29.460 --> 01:13:34.140
If it breaks out, you won’t even know what’s
killing you until it’s too late.

01:13:34.140 --> 01:13:39.060
It begins, like most classic horror stories,
on a dark and stormy night.

01:13:39.060 --> 01:13:44.700
You’re mopping up a silent hallway, whistling
a little tune to yourself, when rain starts

01:13:44.700 --> 01:13:46.860
hammering down on the window next to you.

01:13:46.860 --> 01:13:52.560
Not long after, you see a bolt of lightning
split the distant sky followed by an immense

01:13:52.560 --> 01:13:53.400
thunder crack.

01:13:53.400 --> 01:13:56.760
Soon after you hear screaming and panicking
from below.

01:13:56.760 --> 01:13:58.200
Frantic footsteps.

01:13:58.200 --> 01:14:00.720
Then, the flashing lights and sirens.

01:14:00.720 --> 01:14:03.360
You think back to your employee orientation.

01:14:03.360 --> 01:14:09.600
These flashing lights and wailing sirens can
only mean one thing: Containment breach.

01:14:09.600 --> 01:14:13.200
You run for it, not even knowing what you’re
running from.

01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:16.980
You bring your mop and bucket with you, perhaps
just out of habit.

01:14:16.980 --> 01:14:22.680
You seek refuge in the only place in the facility
that truly seems to belong to you: The broom

01:14:22.680 --> 01:14:23.280
closet.

01:14:23.280 --> 01:14:26.040
The alarm blares as you lock yourself in the
closet.

01:14:26.040 --> 01:14:29.940
You’re shaking with terror and can hear
the screaming of your colleagues.

01:14:29.940 --> 01:14:37.320
You hear more noises - running, scrambling,
a wet dripping sound, gunshots, and then…

01:14:37.320 --> 01:14:38.400
silence.

01:14:38.400 --> 01:14:44.220
All this time, you can’t help but wonder,
“Why isn’t anybody coming to help us?”

01:14:44.220 --> 01:14:49.380
After a while, the only thing you can hear
is the rain and the distant thunder.

01:14:49.380 --> 01:14:50.640
It’s been hours.

01:14:50.640 --> 01:14:55.500
You’ve only managed to stave off dehydration
by drinking the filthy water from the mop

01:14:55.500 --> 01:14:55.800
sink.

01:14:55.800 --> 01:15:00.300
But at least it seems like the chaos outside
has died down.

01:15:00.300 --> 01:15:03.540
Carefully, you open the door and peek out
of the closet.

01:15:03.540 --> 01:15:06.840
Darkness, but no detectable movement.

01:15:06.840 --> 01:15:10.620
Now’s your chance and you make a break for
it, creeping down the hall.

01:15:10.620 --> 01:15:15.900
The dark hallway is suddenly lit up by lightning
and you can see that there are bodies everywhere.

01:15:15.900 --> 01:15:21.240
You step over the corpse of Dr. Cawthrone,
one of the few scientists working here who

01:15:21.240 --> 01:15:22.620
actually knew your name.

01:15:22.620 --> 01:15:27.600
If you can make it to the security office,
you might be able to radio for help, or maybe

01:15:27.600 --> 01:15:29.340
access a computer terminal.

01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:33.960
On the way to the office you hear another
horrific scream start to echo through the

01:15:33.960 --> 01:15:36.660
complex before it’s cut off by a thunderclap.

01:15:36.660 --> 01:15:39.120
You have to ignore it though and push on.

01:15:39.120 --> 01:15:44.580
When you enter the security room, you see
that the head security officer, Nichols, is

01:15:44.580 --> 01:15:45.300
already dead.

01:15:45.300 --> 01:15:49.800
His body has been cut open from neck to groin;
gutted.

01:15:49.800 --> 01:15:53.760
The anomaly, whatever it is, has already been
here.

01:15:53.760 --> 01:15:58.440
You access the computer terminal and open
the file for SCP-3280.

01:15:58.440 --> 01:16:03.840
You’re warned that, as Janitorial Staff,
you have Level 0 Clearance, and as a result,

01:16:03.840 --> 01:16:06.780
information will be omitted from the files
you access.

01:16:06.780 --> 01:16:08.160
It doesn’t matter.

01:16:08.160 --> 01:16:10.680
You press on and open up the file.

01:16:10.680 --> 01:16:13.920
Both the object class and the description
have been redacted.

01:16:13.920 --> 01:16:16.860
You can only see the Special&nbsp;
Containment Procedures.

01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:22.800
They dictate that 3280 is to remain contained
at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research

01:16:22.800 --> 01:16:26.160
Center until long term Containment Procedures
can be drawn up.

01:16:26.160 --> 01:16:32.040
If the entity ever reaches beyond Sub-Level
2, the facility enters full lockdown mode.

01:16:32.040 --> 01:16:37.620
Not even information is allowed in or out
of the facility, as this could result in an

01:16:37.620 --> 01:16:39.960
XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

01:16:39.960 --> 01:16:44.100
In other words, nobody is coming to save you.

01:16:44.100 --> 01:16:49.320
The only other information on the page is
a picture of a lightning storm, much like

01:16:49.320 --> 01:16:51.660
the one you find yourself in right now.

01:16:51.660 --> 01:16:53.580
Lightning flashes in the hall.

01:16:53.580 --> 01:16:57.420
You dart around, paranoid, knowing the anomaly
could be anywhere.

01:16:57.420 --> 01:17:03.480
All you can hear now is a quiet drip, drip,
drip of blood coming from the body of Security

01:17:03.480 --> 01:17:04.680
Officer Nichols.

01:17:04.680 --> 01:17:07.440
Whatever this thing had done to him looked
painful.

01:17:07.440 --> 01:17:12.240
You try to remember him as he was in life,
and then, a revelation hits you.

01:17:12.240 --> 01:17:16.320
A security officer probably has a lot better
clearance than a janitor.

01:17:16.320 --> 01:17:20.580
You feel around Nichols’ mutilated torso
until you find his key card.

01:17:20.580 --> 01:17:25.320
Thankfully, Nichols was the kind of guy who’d
write his password on the underside of the

01:17:25.320 --> 01:17:26.820
card so he wouldn’t forget it.

01:17:26.820 --> 01:17:31.500
You easily gain access to the Foundation servers
with his login credentials.

01:17:31.500 --> 01:17:34.260
You now have Level 2 Security Clearance.

01:17:34.260 --> 01:17:38.640
The terminal gives you the option to view
security footage taken throughout the site.

01:17:38.640 --> 01:17:43.500
You’re given access to every camera still
working after the containment breach and the

01:17:43.500 --> 01:17:44.580
subsequent carnage.

01:17:44.580 --> 01:17:47.640
You select the camera feed for the Second
Floor Barracks.

01:17:47.640 --> 01:17:52.920
There, you see Researcher Jenson hanging from
a makeshift noose attached to his bunk.

01:17:52.920 --> 01:17:55.140
There’s a puddle underneath his corpse.

01:17:55.140 --> 01:17:58.140
You access the feed from the Second Floor
East Wing.

01:17:58.140 --> 01:18:01.980
There, you see Doctor Emmanuel stumbling down
a dark corridor.

01:18:01.980 --> 01:18:05.940
His movements are oddly listless, like he’s
in a trance.

01:18:05.940 --> 01:18:09.480
Suddenly, there’s another flash of lightning
and a crack of thunder.

01:18:09.480 --> 01:18:13.560
Doctor Emmanuel clutches his gut in pain and
crumples to the floor.

01:18:13.560 --> 01:18:16.620
You access the camera feed from the First
Floor Entrance.

01:18:16.620 --> 01:18:21.240
It seems that the whole area is flooded, is
this because of the storm?

01:18:21.240 --> 01:18:26.820
In a panic, many lower-tier staff members
had tried to escape, defying the lockdown

01:18:26.820 --> 01:18:29.520
protocols in the special containment procedures.

01:18:29.520 --> 01:18:33.540
Now, they’re floating face down in the water,
all dead.

01:18:33.540 --> 01:18:39.300
You access the camera feed from Sub Level
2, and see another corpse lying in the corner.

01:18:39.300 --> 01:18:44.820
He’s wearing an orange jumpsuit - D-Class,
no idea why he was down there.

01:18:44.820 --> 01:18:49.920
The only other notable thing in the basement
was a burst pipe, leaking and spraying more

01:18:49.920 --> 01:18:51.000
water everywhere.

01:18:51.000 --> 01:18:55.980
With trembling fingers, you select the camera
feed for the First Floor Cafeteria.

01:18:55.980 --> 01:19:01.380
The whole room is practically underwater - the
only evidence of the massacre that must have

01:19:01.380 --> 01:19:05.220
taken place are the fragments of clothing
floating on the surface of the water.

01:19:05.220 --> 01:19:10.140
That, and the fleshy, pink slurry forming
at the bottom of the windows.

01:19:10.140 --> 01:19:14.340
It reminds you of the gooey meat runoff in
chicken nugget factories.

01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:17.040
You close your eyes and try to center yourself.

01:19:17.040 --> 01:19:18.840
It’s violent chaos.

01:19:18.840 --> 01:19:21.720
Looking at more of it isn’t getting you
anywhere.

01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:26.580
Instead, you decide to put those new Level
2 Security Access credentials to good use,

01:19:26.580 --> 01:19:30.360
and hop back onto the file for SCP-3280.

01:19:30.360 --> 01:19:34.020
You think to yourself, “There has to be
something I can use on here...”

01:19:34.020 --> 01:19:38.820
But even as you wait for the file to load,
some part of you knows that time is running

01:19:38.820 --> 01:19:39.480
out for you.

01:19:39.480 --> 01:19:45.600
Perhaps it’s the stress, or the fear, or
the filthy mop water you drank, but you’re

01:19:45.600 --> 01:19:48.360
feeling the pressure start to mount, physically.

01:19:48.360 --> 01:19:50.400
Your stomach is beginning to ache.

01:19:50.400 --> 01:19:53.760
You can see blurry shapes moving in the corners
of your eyes.

01:19:53.760 --> 01:19:59.040
It’s getting harder to focus your vision,
and harder still to quiet the terrified voices

01:19:59.040 --> 01:19:59.880
in your mind.

01:19:59.880 --> 01:20:04.320
But you can’t get up - not without knowing
what is doing this to you.

01:20:04.320 --> 01:20:08.400
The containment class for SCP-3280 is now
declassified.

01:20:08.400 --> 01:20:09.480
“Euclid.”

01:20:09.480 --> 01:20:13.620
And what’s more, the Special Containment
Procedures have altered, too.

01:20:13.620 --> 01:20:18.960
They now explain that every week, a new member
of D-Class personnel is to be deposited into

01:20:18.960 --> 01:20:23.760
the entity’s lair in Sub Level 2 through
Subterranean Access Point Gamma.

01:20:23.760 --> 01:20:30.180
The D-Class- or more accurately, the sacrifices
- are to be told lies about why exactly they

01:20:30.180 --> 01:20:33.120
need to descend to the lowest point in the
facility.

01:20:33.120 --> 01:20:38.280
They’re even given a working flashlight
and a defensive nightstick to create the illusion

01:20:38.280 --> 01:20:41.940
that the Foundation expects them to ever return
from the depths.

01:20:41.940 --> 01:20:46.500
Little do they know, they also have a tiny
transmitter sewn into their jumpsuit.

01:20:46.500 --> 01:20:53.040
This broadcasts a frequency that will attract
an eager SCP-3280 to the D-Class’ location,

01:20:53.040 --> 01:20:55.740
like a dinner bell only it can hear.

01:20:55.740 --> 01:21:01.200
The file specifies that SCP-3280 always prefers
live prey.

01:21:01.200 --> 01:21:06.360
“Well, at least that explains the dead D-Class
in Sub Level 2,” you think, hoping that

01:21:06.360 --> 01:21:11.400
it’ll somehow overwhelm the dizziness you’re
feeling, or the nagging pain in your gut.

01:21:11.400 --> 01:21:12.480
You read on.

01:21:12.480 --> 01:21:15.780
Somehow, the file’s tone becomes even more
severe.

01:21:15.780 --> 01:21:21.480
It says that failure to maintain the containment
of SCP-3280 will not only trigger a lockdown,

01:21:21.480 --> 01:21:27.420
it will always call in the intervention of
two different Mobile Task Forces: MTF Iota-12,

01:21:27.420 --> 01:21:32.640
“The Silencers”, and Tau-4, also known
as “Water, Water Everywhere.”

01:21:32.640 --> 01:21:37.500
If twelve hours pass from the point of initial
containment breach, and the O5 Council hasn’t

01:21:37.500 --> 01:21:41.880
been given the “all clear” signal by one
of these teams, preparation begins for an

01:21:41.880 --> 01:21:45.000
imminent XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

01:21:45.000 --> 01:21:48.060
Just reading the words sends you into a cold
sweat.

01:21:48.060 --> 01:21:48.900
“End of the World?

01:21:48.900 --> 01:21:50.760
What on Earth is this creature?”

01:21:50.760 --> 01:21:53.040
Finally, you reach the description.

01:21:53.040 --> 01:21:57.600
You get to find out what this horrifying entity
actually is.

01:21:57.600 --> 01:22:03.360
But the last thing you expect is for the first
sentence in the file to read, “SCP-3280

01:22:03.360 --> 01:22:09.600
is a sapient entity composed of a fluid physically
identical to water, capable of traveling roughly

01:22:09.600 --> 01:22:11.700
two and a half kilometers per hour.”

01:22:11.700 --> 01:22:12.840
It’s water.

01:22:12.840 --> 01:22:16.860
It’s literally a living, thinking blob of
water.

01:22:16.860 --> 01:22:23.580
As you read on, the concerning details pile
up: Any water that the anomalous SCP-3280

01:22:23.580 --> 01:22:27.300
water touches, it integrates into its own
mass.

01:22:27.300 --> 01:22:33.840
But any time water is separated from this
mass, it remains anomalous, and continues

01:22:33.840 --> 01:22:35.280
to act independently.

01:22:35.280 --> 01:22:40.200
When the creature was first discovered, it
was a mere 66.4 liters in volume.

01:22:40.200 --> 01:22:43.080
Now, it’s around twenty five hundred.

01:22:43.080 --> 01:22:49.260
The water infected by SCP-3280 is hostile
to all humans, and not just in a defensive

01:22:49.260 --> 01:22:49.680
manner.

01:22:49.680 --> 01:22:53.160
SCP-3280 will actively seek out human prey.

01:22:53.160 --> 01:22:58.380
And when it finds them, it forces its mass
into any available bodily orifice, including

01:22:58.380 --> 01:22:59.640
the victim’s pores.

01:22:59.640 --> 01:23:02.520
This can happen in such a subtle manner that&nbsp;

01:23:02.520 --> 01:23:05.160
you may not even notice&nbsp;
yourself being infiltrated.

01:23:05.160 --> 01:23:11.340
But below this, the file has a list of symptoms
for those experiencing 3280 infiltration:

01:23:11.340 --> 01:23:14.460
loss of motor control,&nbsp;
weakening of the micturition&nbsp;

01:23:14.460 --> 01:23:18.420
reflex, visual hallucinations, and abdominal

01:23:18.420 --> 01:23:18.780
pain.

01:23:18.780 --> 01:23:22.560
As you read the words, your stomach gives
another painful churn.

01:23:22.560 --> 01:23:26.040
Almost like something is moving around inside
you.

01:23:26.040 --> 01:23:27.480
It’s all coming together.

01:23:27.480 --> 01:23:28.800
You read on.

01:23:28.800 --> 01:23:35.100
The file states that SCP-3280 is so difficult
to contain because it exhibits claustrophobic

01:23:35.100 --> 01:23:35.760
tendencies.

01:23:35.760 --> 01:23:41.460
Any time it’s placed inside a container,
whether organic or inorganic, it escapes with

01:23:41.460 --> 01:23:45.720
pressurized water jets that travel at over
255 miles per hour.

01:23:45.720 --> 01:23:52.260
If the water is inside a human, it may literally
explode out of them, killing them in the process.

01:23:52.260 --> 01:23:56.400
Your jittering eyes turn to the gutted body
of Security Officer Nichols.

01:23:56.400 --> 01:23:58.020
It all makes sense now.

01:23:58.020 --> 01:24:02.820
Everything is becoming clear as the pain in
your stomach builds in its intensity.

01:24:02.820 --> 01:24:09.300
The file goes on to say that if ever SCP-3280
escapes Sub Level 2, it may be impossible

01:24:09.300 --> 01:24:10.320
to contain again.

01:24:10.320 --> 01:24:16.620
If 3280 ever escaped the site proper, it would
indeed cause an XK-Class End of the World

01:24:16.620 --> 01:24:22.680
Scenario to unfold, as 3280 merged with our
water cycle and destroyed all of humanity

01:24:22.680 --> 01:24:23.760
on a global scale.

01:24:23.760 --> 01:24:27.600
It would become truly impossible for anyone
to escape.

01:24:27.600 --> 01:24:29.220
You can’t read any more.

01:24:29.220 --> 01:24:31.740
The pain in your stomach is unbearable.

01:24:31.740 --> 01:24:36.600
You jerk from your seat and stumble out into
the hall, doubled over in agony.

01:24:36.600 --> 01:24:38.520
You can feel it pulsing in there.

01:24:38.520 --> 01:24:39.960
Fighting its way out.

01:24:39.960 --> 01:24:43.320
It must have gotten in through the filthy
mop water you were drinking.

01:24:43.320 --> 01:24:47.820
You didn’t even know it, but your fate has
been sealed for hours.

01:24:47.820 --> 01:24:49.980
You’ve been a dead man walking.

01:24:49.980 --> 01:24:53.820
The hum of pain builds in your ears and renders
you almost deaf.

01:24:53.820 --> 01:24:57.360
All you can hear is the patter of rain and
the distant thunder.

01:24:57.360 --> 01:25:02.460
You collapse against the glass, feeling the
coolness of it against the skin of your face.

01:25:02.460 --> 01:25:07.800
And in that moment, you see the water droplets
on the window pane reverse direction.

01:25:07.800 --> 01:25:12.240
They’re slithering up the glass towards
your face in defiance of gravity.

01:25:12.240 --> 01:25:17.820
Then, you realize it’s already over, and
not just for you.

01:25:17.820 --> 01:25:20.580
SCP-3280 has escaped.

01:25:20.580 --> 01:25:24.240
It’s out there, and it’s going to drown
the entire world.

01:25:24.240 --> 01:25:28.920
As you collapse to your knees and prepare
to be torn apart from the inside, your final

01:25:28.920 --> 01:25:32.580
thought is that at least you won’t be alive
to see it.

01:25:32.580 --> 01:25:35.880
Qinghai Lake, the largest lake in China, is&nbsp;

01:25:35.880 --> 01:25:38.880
one of the most secure&nbsp;
locations the SCP Foundation

01:25:38.880 --> 01:25:40.800
has ever taken control of.

01:25:40.800 --> 01:25:46.260
All available military assets have been gathered
at the site, including three of the most elite

01:25:46.260 --> 01:25:48.900
Mobile Task Force units with experimental
weaponry.

01:25:48.900 --> 01:25:55.800
SCP-4290 must not be allowed to open, and
the site has been surrounded by nuclear mines

01:25:55.800 --> 01:25:58.800
and targeted with the Dagaz-Break Orbital
Strike System.

01:25:58.800 --> 01:26:04.740
The perimeter cannot be breached, even if
it means the complete annihilation of the

01:26:04.740 --> 01:26:05.460
entire area.

01:26:05.460 --> 01:26:10.380
This is considered to be an acceptable loss
for the Foundation, since the destruction

01:26:10.380 --> 01:26:15.360
that would be caused by taking such an extreme
measure is far from the worst-case scenario

01:26:15.360 --> 01:26:18.420
when it comes to SCP-4290.

01:26:18.420 --> 01:26:23.880
That’s because the entity contained within
SCP-4290’s site has the potential to create

01:26:23.880 --> 01:26:26.160
a true end-of-the-world scenario.

01:26:26.160 --> 01:26:31.260
The Foundation, of course, is no stranger
to such situations, and even has a set of

01:26:31.260 --> 01:26:37.260
designations for the various types of apocalypses
like CK-Class restructuring scenarios and

01:26:37.260 --> 01:26:40.260
ZK-Class “End of Reality” scenarios.

01:26:40.260 --> 01:26:45.000
And since dealing with the end of the world
is nothing new for the Foundation, certain

01:26:45.000 --> 01:26:47.880
precautions have been taken at the 4290 site.

01:26:47.880 --> 01:26:53.100
If containment measures fail, selected Foundation
personnel and civilians will be taken into

01:26:53.100 --> 01:26:58.080
nearby emergency shelters that will hopefully
survive the chaos that would occur following

01:26:58.080 --> 01:26:58.620
a breach.

01:26:58.620 --> 01:27:03.180
And the Foundation assumed that there was
a good chance this plan would have to be used

01:27:03.180 --> 01:27:08.640
at some point, since at the time these precautions
were put in place, it was impossible to know

01:27:08.640 --> 01:27:11.460
the chance of successful long-term containment.

01:27:11.460 --> 01:27:18.420
But just what is the entity that is held within
the site of SCP-4290 that is capable of causing

01:27:18.420 --> 01:27:21.360
so much death and destruction on a major scale?

01:27:21.360 --> 01:27:23.040
They call it simply…

01:27:23.040 --> 01:27:24.180
“The Child”.

01:27:24.180 --> 01:27:26.400
No one has ever seen the child.

01:27:26.400 --> 01:27:28.800
No one knows what this entity is.

01:27:28.800 --> 01:27:34.380
That’s because even setting aside all the
Foundation security, the site itself is still

01:27:34.380 --> 01:27:36.420
deeply protected, literally.

01:27:36.420 --> 01:27:42.180
Over a hundred feet below the surface of Qinghai
lake, a stunning collection of relics can

01:27:42.180 --> 01:27:42.540
be found.

01:27:42.540 --> 01:27:48.120
The site is thaumaturgically sealed with eight
massive metal totems made of Beryllium and

01:27:48.120 --> 01:27:50.280
Bronze, that resemble armored warriors.

01:27:50.280 --> 01:27:55.920
The statues are inscribed with runes and arranged
in a pattern designed to banish the entity

01:27:55.920 --> 01:27:59.400
kept there and keep the seal on its prison
closed.

01:27:59.400 --> 01:28:04.020
Archaeological evidence indicates that the
site has been there for a very long time,

01:28:04.020 --> 01:28:09.300
and it is still active, with the center of
the site periodically emitting bursts of red

01:28:09.300 --> 01:28:09.600
light.

01:28:09.600 --> 01:28:13.320
But lately, the bursts have suddenly started
getting brighter.

01:28:13.320 --> 01:28:19.200
You may be wondering how we know so much about
SCP-4290, and that it’s a site designed

01:28:19.200 --> 01:28:23.220
to keep something sealed if it’s been deep
in a lake, quietly doing its job?

01:28:23.220 --> 01:28:30.900
The SCP Foundation has access to unusual sources,
including SCP-1726, and it’s from there

01:28:30.900 --> 01:28:35.040
that we learned the little we know about SCP-429.

01:28:35.040 --> 01:28:41.640
SCP-1726 is a library in China that appears
to only be one floor from the outside, but

01:28:41.640 --> 01:28:45.480
on the inside covers over fourteen square
kilometers in area.

01:28:45.480 --> 01:28:50.700
It’s full of a seemingly limitless amount
of texts, many of which describe ancient and

01:28:50.700 --> 01:28:55.860
lost civilizations, along with some clues
as to what led to the fall of these cultures.

01:28:55.860 --> 01:29:00.600
One text revealed the presence of a terrible
and apparently unstoppable enemy.

01:29:00.600 --> 01:29:05.100
It was called the Child - but it was anything
but innocent.

01:29:05.100 --> 01:29:10.440
When these texts were translated, what Foundation
researchers discovered terrified them.

01:29:10.440 --> 01:29:15.720
They described the emergence of a beast with
ten terrible mouths and twenty arms stretched

01:29:15.720 --> 01:29:16.200
wide.

01:29:16.200 --> 01:29:21.000
It was attacked by an army of warriors, but
they were quickly overwhelmed by what was

01:29:21.000 --> 01:29:24.840
described as “torrents of darkness” and
“Dead geometries”.

01:29:24.840 --> 01:29:30.540
They were killed, brutally, and the child
used its skeletal fingers to unleash a torrent

01:29:30.540 --> 01:29:31.200
of flame.

01:29:31.200 --> 01:29:37.560
Every soul in the vicinity was consumed, wax
rained from the sky, and the Child devoured

01:29:37.560 --> 01:29:42.780
everything around it for ten days - as the
whole world trembled.

01:29:42.780 --> 01:29:48.180
But then something sealed the Child away in
its prison which is now covered by the waters

01:29:48.180 --> 01:29:49.260
of Qinghai Lake.

01:29:49.260 --> 01:29:53.520
Soon ominous signs began to appear that the
Child would awaken again though.

01:29:53.520 --> 01:29:58.740
One day, televisions in the nearby area all
suddenly stopped playing their regular programming

01:29:58.740 --> 01:30:04.920
and began to show images of SCP-4290, with
a mysterious voice coming on over the images

01:30:04.920 --> 01:30:08.040
saying “Repair the Child’s Locks”.

01:30:08.040 --> 01:30:13.560
This became more and more frequent, and the
tone of the voice became more worried, eventually

01:30:13.560 --> 01:30:16.680
saying “There is little time left”.

01:30:16.680 --> 01:30:22.380
Further investigations of the location revealed
the location of the mysterious mechanism that

01:30:22.380 --> 01:30:27.720
kept the chamber sealed, which was designated
as SCP-4290-LOCK.

01:30:27.720 --> 01:30:31.080
But how do you repair a device that is eons
old?

01:30:31.080 --> 01:30:35.940
And should you even be fixing it when the
one telling you to do it is a mysterious,

01:30:35.940 --> 01:30:40.440
disembodied voice that only appears on pirated
television broadcasts?

01:30:40.440 --> 01:30:45.540
The Foundation scrambled to find any information
they could, and they were able to find clues

01:30:45.540 --> 01:30:49.860
about the history of SCP-4290 referenced in
other texts.

01:30:49.860 --> 01:30:55.440
Lost civilizations like the Xia Dynasty, the
Erikeshans, and the ancient Ortothans had

01:30:55.440 --> 01:31:00.360
apparently strengthened the seals during their
own reigns, but the most significant findings

01:31:00.360 --> 01:31:05.460
indicated a connection to one of the most
terrifying entities the SCP Foundation had

01:31:05.460 --> 01:31:08.640
ever contained - and one&nbsp;
of the most unpredictable.

01:31:08.640 --> 01:31:10.440
The Daevite Empire.

01:31:10.440 --> 01:31:17.160
This mysterious, warlike civilization has
only been known through one source - SCP-140,

01:31:17.160 --> 01:31:20.700
a single hardcopy book titled “A Chronicle
of the Daevas”.

01:31:20.700 --> 01:31:26.220
This is a strange, anomalous book that is
written in blood and is able to add more pages

01:31:26.220 --> 01:31:30.600
spontaneously to itself whenever it comes
in contact with any fluid that can be used

01:31:30.600 --> 01:31:34.320
for writing, but seems to especially prefer
human blood.

01:31:34.320 --> 01:31:39.060
It recounts the history of this civilization
and their many brutal conquests.

01:31:39.060 --> 01:31:43.620
While there was no proof of the Daevas before
this book was found, evidence paralleling

01:31:43.620 --> 01:31:47.460
the events written in the book is now being
found in archaeological digs.

01:31:47.460 --> 01:31:53.160
More dangerously, as more pages appear in
the book, the events of the Daeva empire are

01:31:53.160 --> 01:31:57.180
moving closer to the present day - with them
currently appearing in the book as having

01:31:57.180 --> 01:31:59.880
existed until 270 CE.

01:31:59.880 --> 01:32:05.559
The Daevas were a bloodthirsty, brutal race
of warriors, but there was one thing even

01:32:05.559 --> 01:32:06.960
that apparently even they were afraid of…

01:32:06.960 --> 01:32:08.100
The Child.

01:32:08.100 --> 01:32:13.620
The Daevas had performed the last successful
ritual of sacrifice needed to strengthen the

01:32:13.620 --> 01:32:18.180
lock not long before their currently described
destruction, and the book contained enough

01:32:18.180 --> 01:32:20.100
detail to recreate the ritual.

01:32:20.100 --> 01:32:24.660
But SCP researchers would find that performing
it would not be for the faint of heart.

01:32:24.660 --> 01:32:29.760
The ritual required three human cadavers,
not a problem for an organization that’s

01:32:29.760 --> 01:32:34.920
normal day to day operation results in the
loss of multiple lives, and the live heart

01:32:34.920 --> 01:32:36.120
of an angel.

01:32:36.120 --> 01:32:41.220
The description of the ritual said that the
materials would be presented, new runes should

01:32:41.220 --> 01:32:45.900
be carved into the totems, the items would
then vanish when the ritual was completed,

01:32:45.900 --> 01:32:48.600
and the lock would somehow be renewed by this.

01:32:48.600 --> 01:32:51.780
It wasn’t much to go on, but time was running
out.

01:32:51.780 --> 01:32:56.820
The Foundation’s Department of Occult Containment
quickly sprang into action, assembling the

01:32:56.820 --> 01:32:59.100
materials and placing them in the correct
formation.

01:32:59.100 --> 01:33:03.660
While it was not safe to descend that deep
underwater to perform the ritual manually,

01:33:03.660 --> 01:33:05.880
technology could fill the role.

01:33:05.880 --> 01:33:11.520
A fleet of remotely operated submersibles
equipped with carving material would perform

01:33:11.520 --> 01:33:14.036
the ritual without any human hands needed.

01:33:14.036 --> 01:33:14.124
The submersibles descended down into the deep,
darkness of the lake and began the ritual,

01:33:14.124 --> 01:33:14.160
but midway through, disaster struck.

01:33:14.160 --> 01:33:19.440
One of the red bursts occurred midway through
the ritual, causing radiation damage to the

01:33:19.440 --> 01:33:19.800
vehicles.

01:33:19.800 --> 01:33:24.720
Runes that had been carved in the past were
also damaged, and the ritual was interrupted.

01:33:24.720 --> 01:33:28.800
While it seemed like it might have been enough
to activate the site, it wasn’t perfect,

01:33:28.800 --> 01:33:33.000
and when the ritual was complete one of the
three cadavers and half of the angel heart

01:33:33.000 --> 01:33:34.680
were still present at the site.

01:33:34.680 --> 01:33:37.980
Had it been enough to satisfy the ritual and
re-seal the lock?

01:33:37.980 --> 01:33:40.740
There was nothing to do but wait and see.

01:33:40.740 --> 01:33:45.120
They wouldn’t have to wait long for their
answer, as the mysterious voice once again

01:33:45.120 --> 01:33:47.100
took over the televisions in the area.

01:33:47.100 --> 01:33:53.520
This time, its message was less friendly - “The
sacrifice did not reach the ten maws.

01:33:53.520 --> 01:33:54.540
Brace”.

01:33:54.540 --> 01:33:59.100
The Child, apparently, was not satisfied and
the lock was not sealed.

01:33:59.100 --> 01:34:03.540
Everyone feared it was too late to prevent
what was coming, and panic was starting to

01:34:03.540 --> 01:34:04.800
spread among the ranks.

01:34:04.800 --> 01:34:09.840
One day, several personnel stationed at the
Qinghai Lake site broke protocol and fled.

01:34:09.840 --> 01:34:15.480
None of them were ever found but one fugitive
staff member, an Agent Zenovia Marinos, left

01:34:15.480 --> 01:34:16.440
behind a note though.

01:34:16.440 --> 01:34:17.160
It read:

01:34:17.160 --> 01:34:19.200
“Do we think we can actually stop this?

01:34:19.200 --> 01:34:22.200
No civilization before us wanted to fight
the Child.

01:34:22.200 --> 01:34:23.100
None of them…

01:34:23.100 --> 01:34:27.360
The sacrifices won't work anymore — it refuses
to consume them.

01:34:27.360 --> 01:34:29.340
They aren't enough to satiate it.

01:34:29.340 --> 01:34:33.780
Once that seal breaks we'll have a world of
molten darkness and the Child will be all

01:34:33.780 --> 01:34:35.220
that's left, eating.

01:34:35.220 --> 01:34:36.060
Drinking…

01:34:36.060 --> 01:34:37.860
You're fools for staying.”

01:34:37.860 --> 01:34:40.620
Agent Marinos was apparently so scared, that&nbsp;

01:34:40.620 --> 01:34:43.200
she had fled through a&nbsp;
portal to an extradimensional

01:34:43.200 --> 01:34:44.700
space in order to escape.

01:34:44.700 --> 01:34:49.440
There would be no point in trying to track
her even if she was still alive.

01:34:49.440 --> 01:34:52.560
But in our own dimension, time was running
out.

01:34:52.560 --> 01:34:57.480
Foundation seismologists were brought to the
site and stationed outside, and began monitoring

01:34:57.480 --> 01:35:00.420
the high-energy pulses coming from behind
the lock.

01:35:00.420 --> 01:35:05.280
The energy was reportedly strong enough to
alter dimensions, and the pulsing red light

01:35:05.280 --> 01:35:11.220
now covered the entire sealing site, growing
stronger and stronger as the totems started

01:35:11.220 --> 01:35:12.840
degrading at an alarming rate.

01:35:12.840 --> 01:35:18.000
The Foundation stood on guard for whatever
was about to emerge - but no one knew if they

01:35:18.000 --> 01:35:20.040
had any chance against whatever it was.

01:35:20.040 --> 01:35:23.880
On August 18th, the totems fully disintegrated.

01:35:23.880 --> 01:35:28.860
Some of the Foundation’s best military forces
gathered on the shores of the lake and waited.

01:35:28.860 --> 01:35:34.260
Ten minutes later, something massive emerged
phased out of the lock and onto the seabed.

01:35:34.260 --> 01:35:35.580
And didn’t move.

01:35:35.580 --> 01:35:41.040
The assembled Foundation forces were confused,
and continued to observe the creature and

01:35:41.040 --> 01:35:46.020
after no activity was seen after three hours,
the authorization was given for submersibles

01:35:46.020 --> 01:35:51.600
and a small exploratory team to proceed down
to the sea bed for an up-close investigation.

01:35:51.600 --> 01:35:55.080
There, down on the floor of the lake, was
the Child.

01:35:55.080 --> 01:36:02.220
It was as terrifying as described, with countless
mouths and arms, and huge in size, over 40

01:36:02.220 --> 01:36:03.120
meters long.

01:36:03.120 --> 01:36:08.700
The signs of previous rituals were everywhere,
with angel hearts and human corpses littered

01:36:08.700 --> 01:36:10.860
around - some in the creature’s mouth.

01:36:10.860 --> 01:36:13.200
But none of them had been eaten.

01:36:13.200 --> 01:36:18.360
The ritual had apparently been performed many
times, but to no actual purpose.

01:36:18.360 --> 01:36:24.000
The massive being was scanned many times,
but no signs of psychic energy, radiation,

01:36:24.000 --> 01:36:26.280
or other life signs were detected.

01:36:26.280 --> 01:36:28.080
The Child was dead.

01:36:28.080 --> 01:36:32.040
And it had apparently been so for a very,
very long time.

01:36:32.040 --> 01:36:36.600
Once the area had been cleared, teams were
brought in to investigate the body in person

01:36:36.600 --> 01:36:38.460
and perform an autopsy on-site.

01:36:38.460 --> 01:36:43.920
No explanation of what exactly this creature
had been or what its origins were has ever

01:36:43.920 --> 01:36:47.040
been discovered, but they did get answers
for when it died.

01:36:47.040 --> 01:36:52.620
The time of death was roughly nine thousand
years ago, not long after its initial sealing.

01:36:52.620 --> 01:36:54.840
The cause of death was discovered too.

01:36:54.840 --> 01:37:00.360
The Child, the destroyer of worlds and scourge
of countless civilizations, had died from

01:37:00.360 --> 01:37:01.140
malnutrition.

01:37:01.140 --> 01:37:06.720
Whatever this thing had been, it had been
sealed away and had died from hunger not long

01:37:06.720 --> 01:37:07.020
after.

01:37:07.020 --> 01:37:12.540
One civilization after another had continued
to perform the rituals to keep it sealed,

01:37:12.540 --> 01:37:15.360
never aware that it was no longer a threat.

01:37:15.360 --> 01:37:22.140
With this new discovery, SCP-4290 was reclassified
as Neutralized, but The Child taught us all

01:37:22.140 --> 01:37:27.000
a valuable lesson about being prepared for
potential world ending scenarios, and the

01:37:27.000 --> 01:37:31.740
Foundation continues to stand on alert for
any more entities from the distant past that

01:37:31.740 --> 01:37:32.940
may pose a threat today.

01:37:32.940 --> 01:37:38.460
Because who knows what else is sealed away
at the bottom of a lake, abandoned mine, or

01:37:38.460 --> 01:37:40.140
in the ocean’s deepest trenches.

01:37:40.140 --> 01:37:45.360
There might just be another existential threat
to humanity that’s just waiting for its

01:37:45.360 --> 01:37:50.100
chance to emerge, and help us all if it remembered
to pack a lunch.

01:37:50.100 --> 01:37:55.680
A pickaxe shatters the rocky wall of a mineshaft,
hundreds of feet below the earth.

01:37:55.680 --> 01:38:00.660
It’s 1871, in a plane that will later be
known as Columbia County, Pennsylvania.

01:38:00.660 --> 01:38:06.780
Men perform back-breaking labor, their hands
and faces blackened with dirt, all working

01:38:06.780 --> 01:38:10.560
in pursuit of that immensely valuable rock
- coal.

01:38:10.560 --> 01:38:15.720
It’s the fuel for the booming industrial
revolution, and much like how dragons were

01:38:15.720 --> 01:38:21.420
said to guard gold, this more modern treasure
pointed to an even more terrifying monster.

01:38:21.420 --> 01:38:28.500
A monster that the SCP Foundation would someday
come to know as SCP - 1179.

01:38:28.500 --> 01:38:33.240
But these unfortunate and underpaid miners
had no idea what they were about to discover.

01:38:33.240 --> 01:38:38.100
One of the men working there that day, Rob
O’Dwyer, was hammering away at the wall

01:38:38.100 --> 01:38:40.680
in front of him when he heard something strange.

01:38:40.680 --> 01:38:42.840
Was that an echo behind the rocks?

01:38:42.840 --> 01:38:45.180
This could mean only one thing.

01:38:45.180 --> 01:38:47.280
The rocks in front of them were hollow.

01:38:47.280 --> 01:38:50.400
There had to be some kind of space hiding
behind them.

01:38:50.400 --> 01:38:55.500
O’Dwyer struck again and again at the rocks
in front of him, until the barrier finally

01:38:55.500 --> 01:38:56.220
tumbled away.

01:38:56.220 --> 01:39:02.280
He and the other miners suddenly felt a gust
of cool, ancient air from the vast and darkened

01:39:02.280 --> 01:39:04.680
cavern in front of them sweep through the
mine.

01:39:04.680 --> 01:39:08.700
They felt like they were standing on the edge
of something truly otherworldly.

01:39:08.700 --> 01:39:13.680
As they lifted their safety lamps high and
crept carefully into the dark, it dawned on

01:39:13.680 --> 01:39:17.280
them that they were likely the first human
beings to ever set foot here.

01:39:17.280 --> 01:39:21.180
But that didn't mean something non human hadn’t
gotten there first.

01:39:21.180 --> 01:39:23.880
O’Dwyer’s lamp soon found something in
the dark.

01:39:23.880 --> 01:39:28.680
A huge figure, curled into a crouching position,
hiding its face.

01:39:28.680 --> 01:39:34.320
It was made from stone, like an enormous yet
incredibly detailed statue of something almost

01:39:34.320 --> 01:39:36.000
human but not quite.

01:39:36.000 --> 01:39:42.120
The petrified thing had two great horns on
either side of its head, twisting into spirals

01:39:42.120 --> 01:39:43.620
like that of a huge ram.

01:39:43.620 --> 01:39:48.660
Word of the giant, frozen monster hidden in
the bottom of the mine soon made its way back

01:39:48.660 --> 01:39:52.680
to the Foreman, and then back to the mine’s
owner, one Sean O’Malley.

01:39:52.680 --> 01:39:57.660
If it were anyone else, perhaps this news
would have been taken to the press immediately,

01:39:57.660 --> 01:40:02.220
and the Foundation would have taken control
of the situation just as quickly.

01:40:02.220 --> 01:40:07.860
But Mr. O’Malley was no ordinary mining
magnate - he was a member of the Molly Maguires,

01:40:07.860 --> 01:40:13.320
an Irish-American secret society, whose members
were predominantly coal miners in Pennsylvania.

01:40:13.320 --> 01:40:19.080
Sean and the other Molly Maguires dubbed this
anomaly the “sleeping stone giant”, and

01:40:19.080 --> 01:40:24.060
conspired to keep it a secret between them
- as secret societies have a habit of doing.

01:40:24.060 --> 01:40:29.100
Though the Molly Maguires were disbanded less
than a decade later, they were all sworn to

01:40:29.100 --> 01:40:31.080
secrecy on the giant’s resting place.

01:40:31.080 --> 01:40:37.140
Until, of course, a descendant of Sean O’Malley
- his grandson, Iain O’Malley - was chosen

01:40:37.140 --> 01:40:39.900
as a prospective agent of the SCP Foundation.

01:40:39.900 --> 01:40:45.180
The Foundation doesn’t just let anyone join
their ranks; they perform an extensive background

01:40:45.180 --> 01:40:49.860
check on all prospective agents, both to find
out that they’re capable of rising to the

01:40:49.860 --> 01:40:54.660
challenges of the job, and also to detect
any affiliation to enemy Groups of Interest.

01:40:54.660 --> 01:40:57.540
It was during this background&nbsp;
check that O’Malley’s&nbsp;

01:40:57.540 --> 01:41:00.060
subterranean family secret was discovered,

01:41:00.060 --> 01:41:04.500
and the land above the old mine shaft was
bought up by a front company owned by the

01:41:04.500 --> 01:41:04.860
Foundation.

01:41:04.860 --> 01:41:10.620
The sleeping stone giant was finally in capable
hands, and in keeping with standard procedure,

01:41:10.620 --> 01:41:15.000
a research site was built above the giant
to gather data and keep an eye on things.

01:41:15.000 --> 01:41:18.840
At the time, the anomaly was considered extremely
low-risk.

01:41:18.840 --> 01:41:25.260
Its containment file read: “SCP-1179 is
apparently dormant, encased in the bedrock

01:41:25.260 --> 01:41:26.400
under Research Site.

01:41:26.400 --> 01:41:28.740
Apart from simple monitoring and standard&nbsp;

01:41:28.740 --> 01:41:31.800
research safety protocols,&nbsp;
no additional containment

01:41:31.800 --> 01:41:33.900
is deemed necessary at this time.”

01:41:33.900 --> 01:41:39.420
But of course, those simple containment procedures
would soon need updating.

01:41:39.420 --> 01:41:44.160
In 1962, the town of Centralia, Pennsylvania,
had a trash problem.

01:41:44.160 --> 01:41:48.840
There were eight illegal trash dumping sites
across the town, and to combat this issue,

01:41:48.840 --> 01:41:52.920
the town council opened up a huge landfill
in an abandoned mineshaft.

01:41:52.920 --> 01:41:57.600
You’d think this would be enough for the
moderately sized town, but humans have a tendency

01:41:57.600 --> 01:42:02.040
to produce a lot of trash, and they soon filled
up the new landfill too.

01:42:02.040 --> 01:42:07.080
In order to address the issue, the town decided
to do a controlled burn of some of the garbage.

01:42:07.080 --> 01:42:11.820
It should have been simple enough, but those
who lit this garbage fire didn’t follow

01:42:11.820 --> 01:42:15.000
proper safety procedures,&nbsp;
and ended up accidentally&nbsp;

01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:17.580
igniting a seam of anthracite coal.

01:42:17.580 --> 01:42:23.220
This was like lighting the fuse to the world’s
largest stick of dynamite and fire soon coursed

01:42:23.220 --> 01:42:25.200
through the long abandoned mine tunnels.

01:42:25.200 --> 01:42:30.780
When the fireball finally reached the sleeping
stone giant in his dark pit, the beast woke

01:42:30.780 --> 01:42:30.900
up.

01:42:30.900 --> 01:42:36.480
In that instant, an otherwise uneventful day
quickly became a brutal bloodbath.

01:42:36.480 --> 01:42:40.260
Researchers walking through the base felt
a monstrous rumbling beneath them.

01:42:40.260 --> 01:42:44.220
Heat sensors were burning up and seismic readings
were off the scale.

01:42:44.220 --> 01:42:46.920
Something was climbing up towards them.

01:42:46.920 --> 01:42:51.840
Suddenly, an impossibly large sword speared
its way out of the floor, killing everyone

01:42:51.840 --> 01:42:54.120
around it with an immense blast of heat.

01:42:54.120 --> 01:42:59.760
The newly-awakened monster went on an underground
rampage, almost completely destroying the

01:42:59.760 --> 01:43:04.380
research base and killing nearly everyone
inside, before retreating into the honeycomb

01:43:04.380 --> 01:43:10.080
of coal mines and caverns in the area, igniting
even more anthracite coal fires.

01:43:10.080 --> 01:43:13.680
The Foundation needed to step in before things
really got out of control.

01:43:13.680 --> 01:43:18.540
At present, the Foundation couldn’t properly
administer standard area construction protocols

01:43:18.540 --> 01:43:24.420
for Keter-Class SCPs, so they instead designated
the mines, caverns, and surrounding countryside

01:43:24.420 --> 01:43:30.480
as Area-179, and dispatched Mobile Task Forces
to try and contain the beast rampaging in

01:43:30.480 --> 01:43:31.680
the Centralia mines.

01:43:31.680 --> 01:43:37.020
But much like the fire that started this whole
mess, the beast proved much harder to control

01:43:37.020 --> 01:43:38.640
than initially imagined.

01:43:38.640 --> 01:43:43.800
All five of the expeditionary teams sent to
apprehend the monster failed, and many team

01:43:43.800 --> 01:43:45.720
members were slaughtered in the process.

01:43:45.720 --> 01:43:50.460
From the terrified accounts of the survivors,
we have a vague idea of the nature of the

01:43:50.460 --> 01:43:51.180
beast below.

01:43:51.180 --> 01:43:55.200
No pictures of the creature exist and exact
descriptions on the beast can vary.

01:43:55.200 --> 01:43:59.760
Whether this is because the beast frequently
shapeshifts or because it has some kind of

01:43:59.760 --> 01:44:03.420
cognitohazardous effects on those who view
it is unclear.

01:44:03.420 --> 01:44:07.920
The most frequently reported characteristics
of the creature are its immense height and

01:44:07.920 --> 01:44:10.320
the extreme heat that its body exudes.

01:44:10.320 --> 01:44:15.300
Many report that the creature’s body seems
to be formed of a mix of hardening lava, pure

01:44:15.300 --> 01:44:16.860
fire, and burning smoke.

01:44:16.860 --> 01:44:23.160
The beast measures over 30 meters from head
to toe, with shoulders over 8 meters wide.

01:44:23.160 --> 01:44:28.740
It’s commonly said to have two huge, ram-like
horns, and a weathered, bearded face.

01:44:28.740 --> 01:44:33.720
The beast has been compared by some to the
Norse mythological figure Surtr, the giant

01:44:33.720 --> 01:44:36.960
guarding the frontier of the Norse fire realm
of Múspell.

01:44:36.960 --> 01:44:42.180
However, the actual age of the creature seems
to predate these legends by a considerable

01:44:42.180 --> 01:44:42.840
margin.

01:44:42.840 --> 01:44:49.140
Dating of the stratum encasing SCP-1179 indicates
it dates to the Mississippian subperiod of

01:44:49.140 --> 01:44:56.220
the Carboniferous period, approximately 359.2
to 318.1 million years ago.

01:44:56.220 --> 01:45:01.740
This age is consistent with the geological
age of this region, so it may have literally

01:45:01.740 --> 01:45:03.240
come with the territory.

01:45:03.240 --> 01:45:08.580
Less common descriptions of the beast claim
that it has huge wings, eyes made of hellfire,

01:45:08.580 --> 01:45:11.220
and fangs as long as a man’s arm.

01:45:11.220 --> 01:45:17.520
Some say the beast has neither horns nor fangs,
and its face is encircled by flames which

01:45:17.520 --> 01:45:20.100
reach down into a long beard of fire.

01:45:20.100 --> 01:45:25.500
And like a certain creature known as the Balrog
that Lord of the Rings fans will be very familiar

01:45:25.500 --> 01:45:28.080
with, this beast comes with weapons.

01:45:28.080 --> 01:45:33.060
In one hand, the beast wields a giant, burning
sword, around five meters in length.

01:45:33.060 --> 01:45:36.960
In the other, it wields a huge, multi-tailed
whip made out of fire.

01:45:36.960 --> 01:45:42.180
It’s incredibly proficient with these weapons,
too, and has a serious strategic advantage

01:45:42.180 --> 01:45:43.920
in its underground environment.

01:45:43.920 --> 01:45:48.540
Foundation researchers have determined that
some of the wounds the beast gained from its

01:45:48.540 --> 01:45:52.890
first confrontation haven’t fully healed,
implying that the beast could - in theory

01:45:52.890 --> 01:45:54.900
- be destroyed with enough firepower.

01:45:54.900 --> 01:45:59.820
However, given that the beast has killed almost
everyone who faced it, and its mere presence

01:45:59.820 --> 01:46:05.940
can start almost uncontrollable fires, direct
engagement would only be used as a last resort.

01:46:05.940 --> 01:46:09.120
Even the creature’s breath can be extremely
dangerous.

01:46:09.120 --> 01:46:14.760
Chemical analysis of air samples taken from
SCP-1179’s breath have shown exceptionally

01:46:14.760 --> 01:46:18.660
high concentrations of carbon monoxide and
sulfur dioxide.

01:46:18.660 --> 01:46:24.420
The very presence of this creature creates
a real and active danger to everyone around

01:46:24.420 --> 01:46:24.720
it.

01:46:24.720 --> 01:46:28.740
And the beast’s presence was beginning to
have seriously negative effects on the people

01:46:28.740 --> 01:46:29.520
up above.

01:46:29.520 --> 01:46:35.040
By the 1970s, the Foundation had given up
on sending Mobile Task Forces into the caverns,

01:46:35.040 --> 01:46:37.800
and instead began to focus on depopulating&nbsp;

01:46:37.800 --> 01:46:40.680
the town of Centralia to&nbsp;
prevent further fatalities

01:46:40.680 --> 01:46:43.740
from the presence of SCP - 1179.

01:46:43.740 --> 01:46:48.840
The subterranean activities of the creature
were causing collapses in some areas, and

01:46:48.840 --> 01:46:52.260
noxious fumes were beginning to rise up from
cracks in the ground.

01:46:52.260 --> 01:46:57.540
As the constantly raging fires burned beneath
the earth, they were causing everything above

01:46:57.540 --> 01:46:59.700
to slowly melt or bake.

01:46:59.700 --> 01:47:03.960
A Foundation geologist determined that the
fires created by the beast would likely remain

01:47:03.960 --> 01:47:09.960
active for 250 years, and any attempts to
put out the fires or contain the beast would

01:47:09.960 --> 01:47:11.340
ultimately be futile.

01:47:11.340 --> 01:47:17.640
This led to the formation of Project Tartarus,
a concerted effort to cover up SCP - 1179

01:47:17.640 --> 01:47:20.640
and fully evacuate the citizens of Centralia.

01:47:20.640 --> 01:47:25.200
They pushed the narrative that the mine fires,
while deadly, were merely the\ result of the

01:47:25.200 --> 01:47:30.060
failed garbage burning plan, and little by
little, the people of Centralia began to move

01:47:30.060 --> 01:47:30.360
away.

01:47:30.360 --> 01:47:36.000
By 1984, the United States Government finally
caved to secret lobbying from the Foundation,

01:47:36.000 --> 01:47:42.120
and allocated funds in excess of $42 million
to relocate the remaining civilian residents

01:47:42.120 --> 01:47:42.660
from the area.

01:47:42.660 --> 01:47:47.700
Any legal complaints from Centralia residents
were quietly crushed by the Foundation, and

01:47:47.700 --> 01:47:51.540
efforts to remove pretty much all residents
from the area were successful.

01:47:51.540 --> 01:47:57.180
This allowed the Foundation to finally cast
a wider net and administer Keter-Class containment

01:47:57.180 --> 01:48:03.000
protocols around the two-kilometer underground
zone where SCP - 1179 resides.

01:48:03.000 --> 01:48:07.920
The Foundation has continued studies on the
beast from below in the decades since, with

01:48:07.920 --> 01:48:12.720
some scientists even suggesting it could be
used to produce geothermal energy, but whether

01:48:12.720 --> 01:48:16.500
or not that would actually be feasible remains
unknown.

01:48:16.500 --> 01:48:23.340
For now SCP-1179 seems content to stay within
its zone, and hopefully it stays that way.

01:48:23.340 --> 01:48:27.780
But as we’re forced to dig deeper and deeper
for the remaining precious metals here on

01:48:27.780 --> 01:48:33.360
earth, there’s no telling what new dangers
we might find lurking far below the ground.

01:48:33.360 --> 01:48:37.620
It was 1948, in Villa Blanca, Guatemala.

01:48:37.620 --> 01:48:43.200
As night fell, two young boys - Carlos and
Miguel - played a game of soccer in the street.

01:48:43.200 --> 01:48:48.900
It was a quiet town full of humble, hard-working
people, and they were about to come face to

01:48:48.900 --> 01:48:50.160
face with a monster.

01:48:50.160 --> 01:48:55.320
Typically, when something like this happened,
you’d know exactly who to call: The SCP

01:48:55.320 --> 01:48:55.860
Foundation.

01:48:55.860 --> 01:49:01.500
Problem is, while these days we can generally
depend on the hard-working agents and researchers

01:49:01.500 --> 01:49:04.320
of the Foundation to save us from any anomalous,&nbsp;

01:49:04.320 --> 01:49:07.560
supernatural threats with&nbsp;
their tactics, expertise,

01:49:07.560 --> 01:49:10.920
and equipment, it wasn’t always this way.

01:49:10.920 --> 01:49:17.040
There was a time before the SCP Foundation
became the titan of anomaly-combatting prowess

01:49:17.040 --> 01:49:21.120
it is today, and it’s that time that we’re
focusing on today.

01:49:21.120 --> 01:49:26.100
It all comes back to a strange and violent
creature wandering the darkened streets of

01:49:26.100 --> 01:49:26.820
Guatemala.

01:49:26.820 --> 01:49:34.500
Or, as Dr. Charles Odgen Gears proposed we
call it, SCP-001 - The Prototype.

01:49:34.500 --> 01:49:40.740
SCP-001 is a topic we’ve covered in a number
of videos, but even then, we can never quite

01:49:40.740 --> 01:49:43.500
capture the full scope of this wily designation.

01:49:43.500 --> 01:49:48.540
“What is SCP-001?” is probably one of
the most loaded questions you can possibly

01:49:48.540 --> 01:49:54.120
ask as a member of the SCP Foundation, and
it may be your last, as the majority of the

01:49:54.120 --> 01:49:58.920
files under the SCP-001 umbrella are highly
classified for pretty much everyone under

01:49:58.920 --> 01:50:00.180
Level 5 clearance.

01:50:00.840 --> 01:50:06.600
001 covers a large number of potentially anomalous
items, entities, and concepts, from the dreaded

01:50:06.600 --> 01:50:12.900
Scarlet King, to the awe-inspiring Gate Guardian,
to the very SCP Foundation itself, through

01:50:12.900 --> 01:50:17.760
the eyes of the charmingly incompetent Unusual
Incidents Unit of the FBI.

01:50:17.760 --> 01:50:23.100
Perhaps they’re all real, perhaps only one
of them is, and the rest are in there as a

01:50:23.100 --> 01:50:23.580
smokescreen.

01:50:23.580 --> 01:50:28.740
Perhaps they’re all fake, red herrings laid
down to hide the trail to something even more

01:50:28.740 --> 01:50:30.180
secretive and fantastic.

01:50:30.180 --> 01:50:36.180
All we know is that 001s seem to be gathered
around a collection of loose themes - The

01:50:36.180 --> 01:50:41.100
beginnings of the Foundation, events or entities
that could end the Foundation or even the

01:50:41.100 --> 01:50:44.220
world, and key formative moments in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:44.220 --> 01:50:45.060
Foundation’s
history.

01:50:45.060 --> 01:50:50.760
Dr. Gears’ proposal for SCP-001 lies firmly
in the latter camp.

01:50:50.760 --> 01:50:55.680
And if you keep watching and listening closely,
you’ll see exactly why.

01:50:55.680 --> 01:50:59.520
Back to Carlos and Miguel,&nbsp;
the pair of eleven-year-olds&nbsp;

01:50:59.520 --> 01:51:01.980
playing soccer on the quiet back streets of

01:51:01.980 --> 01:51:02.820
Villa Blanca.

01:51:02.820 --> 01:51:07.080
They were kicking the ball back and forth
when they heard a strange screeching noise

01:51:07.080 --> 01:51:07.740
in the distance.

01:51:07.740 --> 01:51:12.900
At first, they thought it was some kind of
injured bird, squawking desperately for help.

01:51:12.900 --> 01:51:17.700
Being good kids, they didn’t waste a second
running into the action, heading further into

01:51:17.700 --> 01:51:18.960
the outskirts of town.

01:51:18.960 --> 01:51:23.940
However, the creature they encountered on
that rural road was certainly no bird.

01:51:23.940 --> 01:51:28.260
When they first saw it, hunched over a few
meters in front of them, they thought it must

01:51:28.260 --> 01:51:29.940
have been a horribly injured man.

01:51:29.940 --> 01:51:35.340
He was deathly thin, with gray-brown skin
that looked either bruised or burned.

01:51:35.340 --> 01:51:40.320
It was twitching and weeping, its chest heaving
in heavy, labored pants.

01:51:40.320 --> 01:51:45.180
Its limbs were jerking wildly, as though the
creature was being electrocuted.

01:51:45.180 --> 01:51:46.620
“Hey mister, are you okay?”

01:51:46.620 --> 01:51:48.360
Carlos called out in Spanish.

01:51:48.360 --> 01:51:54.000
In that moment, what they had wrongly thought
was a man just froze up, finally registering

01:51:54.000 --> 01:51:54.720
their presence.

01:51:54.720 --> 01:52:00.540
Immediately, the two boys knew something was
wrong, as the creature slowly rose to its

01:52:00.540 --> 01:52:06.720
full height: Well over six feet, towering
over the two of them, even at a distance.

01:52:06.720 --> 01:52:12.540
They noticed something was wrong with its
limbs: They were too long, well out of proportion

01:52:12.540 --> 01:52:14.460
with its human-sized torso.

01:52:14.460 --> 01:52:19.380
It didn’t have hands and feet - At least,
not in the way that humans do.

01:52:19.380 --> 01:52:25.560
Instead, its slender ankles terminated in
long, black spikes, and its wrists each split

01:52:25.560 --> 01:52:28.260
off into three equally black claws.

01:52:28.260 --> 01:52:35.280
But worst of all was its face, if you could
even call what that monster had a face.

01:52:35.280 --> 01:52:38.280
Its head was split in the middle by a huge
mouth.

01:52:38.280 --> 01:52:44.580
At first, its gnarly lips were pursed, but
they soon slid open with a low, rumbling roar.

01:52:44.580 --> 01:52:49.020
The boys could feel their knees shaking as
they saw the monster’s mouthful of long,

01:52:49.020 --> 01:52:50.340
rotten fangs.

01:52:50.340 --> 01:52:55.440
Something started sliding up the dark passage
of the monster’s throat: A translucent,

01:52:55.440 --> 01:52:56.820
milky-blue sphere.

01:52:56.820 --> 01:52:58.680
Was that thing an eye?

01:52:58.680 --> 01:53:01.740
It made the two boys feel sick to even look
at it.

01:53:01.740 --> 01:53:06.300
That’s when the “eye” started to glow,
and the space around the monster began to

01:53:06.300 --> 01:53:09.600
shimmer slightly, like some kind of terrible
sorcery.

01:53:09.600 --> 01:53:14.700
As the two boys felt a strange force pulling
at them, trying to tug them into the creature’s

01:53:14.700 --> 01:53:19.080
embrace, they were suddenly jogged from their
frightened paralysis and decided to finally

01:53:19.080 --> 01:53:20.160
make a run for it.

01:53:20.160 --> 01:53:25.980
There was no doubt about what had just happened:
They’d encountered a demon in the flesh,

01:53:25.980 --> 01:53:29.460
intent on taking their souls straight to hell.

01:53:29.460 --> 01:53:33.720
When the two of them told their parents, they
were met at first with disbelief.

01:53:33.720 --> 01:53:38.760
Two young boys saw something that frightened
them in the dark - perhaps an animal, if anything

01:53:38.760 --> 01:53:42.000
at all - and they’d let their imaginations
run wild.

01:53:42.000 --> 01:53:43.800
It was typical of children.

01:53:43.800 --> 01:53:48.300
However, things didn’t seem quite so simple
when more sightings started popping up.

01:53:48.300 --> 01:53:53.880
People all across the town of Villa Blanca
started seeing this monster, all with matching

01:53:53.880 --> 01:54:00.600
descriptions: A huge, emaciated beast with
a mouth for a face, its glowing blue eye nested

01:54:00.600 --> 01:54:01.080
inside.

01:54:01.080 --> 01:54:06.960
The natural excuses circulated at first: Perhaps
the creature was a local prankster in a costume?

01:54:06.960 --> 01:54:11.580
This would be comforting to believe, but how
many pranksters in costumes can completely

01:54:11.580 --> 01:54:13.380
disappear before your very eyes.

01:54:13.380 --> 01:54:18.180
The monster’s eye would glow, and just like
that, it would simply vanish.

01:54:18.180 --> 01:54:23.160
As fear and paranoia began spreading through
the town, people suggested that perhaps it

01:54:23.160 --> 01:54:27.600
was a case of mass hysteria - Fear and panic
taking over rationality.

01:54:27.600 --> 01:54:32.820
But by this point, things had gotten worse:
Carlos and Miguel, the two boys who’d first

01:54:32.820 --> 01:54:35.580
discovered the demon on the back road, had
become sick.

01:54:35.580 --> 01:54:39.900
They were experiencing severe nausea, vomiting,
headaches, and diarrhea.

01:54:39.900 --> 01:54:41.400
Their bodies weakened.

01:54:41.400 --> 01:54:43.860
Lesions began developing on their skin.

01:54:43.860 --> 01:54:49.020
As their conditions deteriorated, and it seemed
as though nobody was capable of helping them,

01:54:49.020 --> 01:54:53.100
a rumor spread that the monster was somehow
inducing this sickness.

01:54:53.100 --> 01:54:57.780
The town doctor didn’t have the expertise
to diagnose it, but the boys were suffering

01:54:57.780 --> 01:54:59.880
from acute radiation sickness.

01:54:59.880 --> 01:55:03.060
And they wouldn’t be the only ones.

01:55:03.060 --> 01:55:07.320
Many of the people who’d reported sightings
and close encounters with the monster started

01:55:07.320 --> 01:55:09.720
coming down with severe radiation sickness.

01:55:09.720 --> 01:55:14.640
To the townspeople, it just seemed to be a
demon spreading some invisible plague among

01:55:14.640 --> 01:55:14.820
them.

01:55:14.820 --> 01:55:17.280
But the horrors wouldn’t stop there.

01:55:17.280 --> 01:55:22.320
It seemed that this demon also liked to take
a more direct approach to harming the townsfolk,

01:55:22.320 --> 01:55:26.820
because not long after the sickness broke
out, people started disappearing.

01:55:26.820 --> 01:55:28.680
There were never any bodies.

01:55:28.680 --> 01:55:32.820
The most that would ever be found were tattered
items of clothing left at the site of the

01:55:32.820 --> 01:55:36.240
disappearances, or blood smeared across the
walls or ground.

01:55:36.240 --> 01:55:40.320
Before they knew it, seven of their people
were gone.

01:55:40.320 --> 01:55:44.880
It seemed that, for all intents and purposes,
God had abandoned them.

01:55:44.880 --> 01:55:47.820
They were playthings of the demon now.

01:55:47.820 --> 01:55:52.500
Thankfully for the townsfolk who weren’t
yet irradiated or vanished, an organization

01:55:52.500 --> 01:55:53.340
was forming.

01:55:53.340 --> 01:55:55.920
One that might be their only chance at salvation.

01:55:55.920 --> 01:56:01.320
Someday in the future, it would become known
as The SCP Foundation, but it had a lot to

01:56:01.320 --> 01:56:02.460
learn before it got there.

01:56:02.460 --> 01:56:08.220
You see, the reason that this iteration of
SCP-001 is known as The Prototype is that

01:56:08.220 --> 01:56:14.100
- if Dr. Gears is to be believed - it may
be the first anomalous entity that they ever

01:56:14.100 --> 01:56:15.300
truly faced.

01:56:15.300 --> 01:56:19.620
So naturally, getting the creature captured
and contained didn’t go quite as smoothly

01:56:19.620 --> 01:56:24.600
as most of their modern jobs, despite the
comparative simplicity of this old threat.

01:56:24.600 --> 01:56:29.400
General Machoi, an ex-military operator that
became part of what we’ll once again call

01:56:29.400 --> 01:56:34.980
The Precursors to the Foundation, led a research
and recovery team into Villa Blanca to hunt

01:56:34.980 --> 01:56:39.360
down and retrieve the beast that’d been
causing all this misery and death among the

01:56:39.360 --> 01:56:40.080
townsfolk.

01:56:40.080 --> 01:56:43.140
However, this proved to be easier said than
done.

01:56:43.140 --> 01:56:47.580
While its bestial appearance might fool people
into thinking the monster was just a mindless

01:56:47.580 --> 01:56:52.140
animal, later writings on the creature would
describe it as both incredibly cunning and

01:56:52.140 --> 01:56:53.280
terrifyingly fast.

01:56:53.280 --> 01:56:57.780
When a group of armed personnel first tried
to engage the creature directly, they had

01:56:57.780 --> 01:57:01.560
no idea that they were walking right into
the middle of a bloodbath.

01:57:01.560 --> 01:57:07.140
They believed they had it surrounded on another
rural back road, advancing with assault rifles,

01:57:07.140 --> 01:57:10.020
when the creature flipped out and started
killing them.

01:57:10.020 --> 01:57:13.140
The Prototype proved to have frightening offensive
capabilities.

01:57:13.140 --> 01:57:17.640
Its three dark claws easily carved through
the armor of the soldiers trying desperately

01:57:17.640 --> 01:57:18.480
to contain it.

01:57:18.480 --> 01:57:23.820
The creature moved so fast that none of them
could reliably draw a bead on it, and if any

01:57:23.820 --> 01:57:28.260
of them could, it was holding their severed
head before they had a chance to squeeze the

01:57:28.260 --> 01:57:28.620
trigger.

01:57:28.620 --> 01:57:32.880
But death by the creature’s claws was one
of the more pleasant ways it could kill its

01:57:32.880 --> 01:57:33.240
victims.

01:57:33.240 --> 01:57:38.280
At one point during an engagement with Precursor
troops, it opened its mouth and unveiled its

01:57:38.280 --> 01:57:39.300
glowing, blue eye.

01:57:39.300 --> 01:57:43.680
At this point, one of the soldiers screamed,
and suddenly seemed to be sucked inside of

01:57:43.680 --> 01:57:45.720
himself, completely disappearing.

01:57:45.720 --> 01:57:50.640
The Prototype’s blue eye glowed again, and
it once again just teleported away from the

01:57:50.640 --> 01:57:50.820
scene.

01:57:50.820 --> 01:57:54.900
A number of the soldiers who survived this
altercation later needed to be treated for

01:57:54.900 --> 01:57:56.520
acute radiation sickness.

01:57:56.520 --> 01:58:00.960
Researchers eventually managed to figure out
what was actually happening with the creature:

01:58:00.960 --> 01:58:06.900
It had the ability to manifest microsingularities
- tiny black holes that it used to both teleport

01:58:06.900 --> 01:58:10.560
from place to place, and defend itself from
attacks when necessary.

01:58:10.560 --> 01:58:16.140
These singularities wouldn’t stick around
for long, a few seconds at most, but they

01:58:16.140 --> 01:58:19.800
had the terrifying side effect of putting
out massive amounts of radiation.

01:58:19.800 --> 01:58:26.160
This is why it was making so much of the town
and the recovery team sick via mere proximity.

01:58:26.160 --> 01:58:30.600
Thankfully, in finding out the creature’s
strength, they also managed to find out its

01:58:30.600 --> 01:58:31.140
weaknesses.

01:58:31.140 --> 01:58:36.780
Its powers were dampened by high humidity,
bright lights, and especially intense strobing

01:58:36.780 --> 01:58:37.080
lights.

01:58:37.080 --> 01:58:41.760
It was through the use of these lights that
the creature was finally captured and brought

01:58:41.760 --> 01:58:47.040
into ADRX-19 - a complex that would later
become Site-19 - for containment.

01:58:47.040 --> 01:58:51.240
There, its containment procedures were devised
by one of the burgeoning organization’s

01:58:51.240 --> 01:58:54.000
top minds: Dr. Hermann Keter.

01:58:54.000 --> 01:58:58.920
However, Dr. Keter would sadly never actually
live to see the duration of the Prototype’s

01:58:58.920 --> 01:59:04.140
containment at ADRX-19 - He was tragically
killed by the monster, though his name would

01:59:04.140 --> 01:59:08.340
live on as the designation for anomalies that
were particularly difficult to contain.

01:59:08.340 --> 01:59:13.560
It was thanks to him that his coworkers realized
lead-lined walls, a reinforced steel door,

01:59:13.560 --> 01:59:18.900
a 100% humidity environment, and the frequent
application of high-intensity strobe lights

01:59:18.900 --> 01:59:21.900
were the best way to keep the Prototype locked
up for good.

01:59:21.900 --> 01:59:28.140
To this day, this iteration of SCP-001 is
a fascinating reminder that the SCP Foundation

01:59:28.140 --> 01:59:30.660
wasn’t always the juggernaut it is today.

01:59:30.660 --> 01:59:36.000
There was once a time when they had as little
idea of what they were doing as the rest of

01:59:36.000 --> 01:59:36.120
us.

01:59:36.120 --> 01:59:40.740
There’s no better representation of this
than the file itself: It was an era before

01:59:40.740 --> 01:59:43.440
object classes and conventional designation
numbers.

01:59:43.440 --> 01:59:48.720
The file is written in a sketchy, disorganized
manner, and arranged into “Item designation

01:59:48.720 --> 01:59:52.380
number”, “Warning”, “Description of
item”, “Detail of current containment”,

01:59:52.380 --> 01:59:54.060
“Report”, and “addendum.”

01:59:54.060 --> 02:00:00.300
As with any experience in life, it’s always
worth asking: What can we learn from the SCP

02:00:00.300 --> 02:00:05.160
Foundation’s experience with its possible
first anomaly, a monster that seems almost

02:00:05.160 --> 02:00:07.860
nostalgically quaint by today’s standards?

02:00:07.860 --> 02:00:12.300
Perhaps the greatest message is that everything
is a work in progress.

02:00:12.300 --> 02:00:17.580
It was only by determination and persistence
that the Foundation could go from an organization

02:00:17.580 --> 02:00:22.500
challenged by a monster like The Prototype
to going toe to toe with real heavy hitters

02:00:22.500 --> 02:00:23.760
like the Scarlet King.

02:00:23.760 --> 02:00:26.040
How very inspirational.

02:00:26.040 --> 02:00:28.800
We have always been afraid of the dark.

02:00:28.800 --> 02:00:34.920
Ancient ancestors of mankind built fires to
chase the shadows away, to keep the thick,

02:00:34.920 --> 02:00:40.140
black mystery of night from encroaching on
their fragile little homes with all of the

02:00:40.140 --> 02:00:42.780
teeth and claws it hid within its depths.

02:00:42.780 --> 02:00:47.640
From the time we were small children, we knew
to be nervous when the lights went out.

02:00:47.640 --> 02:00:52.980
We beg our parents to leave the hall light
on or plug in a nightlight, praying that a

02:00:52.980 --> 02:00:58.500
tiny sliver of illumination will protect us
from the monsters we just know are salivating

02:00:58.500 --> 02:01:05.160
beneath the bed, scratching against the closet
door, waiting for us to close our eyes.

02:01:05.160 --> 02:01:10.440
We pull the blankets tight over our heads,
heating the air with our panicked breaths

02:01:10.440 --> 02:01:15.060
and reminding ourselves that the shadow in
the corner of the room was just a rocking

02:01:15.060 --> 02:01:16.680
chair or a coat rack.

02:01:16.680 --> 02:01:19.200
We pretend it’s the truth.

02:01:19.200 --> 02:01:22.980
But there’s a reason we fear the darkness
as much as we do.

02:01:22.980 --> 02:01:24.360
It’s inherent.

02:01:24.360 --> 02:01:30.300
It’s a memory passed down from generation
to generation ever since we first learned

02:01:30.300 --> 02:01:31.260
how to scream.

02:01:31.260 --> 02:01:36.300
As adults, we try to tell ourselves we’ve
outgrown those childish fears and night terrors.

02:01:36.300 --> 02:01:37.620
We know better now.

02:01:37.620 --> 02:01:43.200
But you still run up the darkened staircase
as if something’s chasing you and your heart

02:01:43.200 --> 02:01:46.380
jumps into your throat when you hear a sound
after midnight.

02:01:46.380 --> 02:01:54.060
Call it el cucuy, the kludde, the boogeyman,
or a thousand other names; we all know there

02:01:54.060 --> 02:01:55.680
is something lurking in the dark.

02:01:55.680 --> 02:01:58.740
And it knows us too.

02:01:58.740 --> 02:02:05.220
D-Class 080-1 was pulled from his cell one
afternoon and brought to a containment chamber.

02:02:05.220 --> 02:02:06.660
He knew the drill by now.

02:02:06.660 --> 02:02:11.700
They would send him in and he would encounter
something bizarre, horrible, and potentially

02:02:11.700 --> 02:02:12.240
deadly.

02:02:12.240 --> 02:02:17.760
Maybe he would emerge traumatized, maybe he
would lose a limb, or maybe he would never

02:02:17.760 --> 02:02:18.900
come back out at all.

02:02:18.900 --> 02:02:22.680
A security guard opened the door and instructed
him to enter.

02:02:22.680 --> 02:02:27.540
It wasn’t an ideal situation, but he really
didn’t have much of a choice.

02:02:27.540 --> 02:02:29.940
And so, he walked inside.

02:02:29.940 --> 02:02:34.860
Dr. Smith called to him from outside the room,
asking him what he could see inside.

02:02:34.860 --> 02:02:39.720
It was pitch black, and he couldn’t see
a thing, and he told the doctor as much.

02:02:39.720 --> 02:02:43.740
But then…the hairs on the back of his neck
prickled.

02:02:43.740 --> 02:02:46.620
A chill rippled down his spine.

02:02:46.620 --> 02:02:51.420
He had the distinct feeling that something
was looking right at him.

02:02:51.420 --> 02:02:52.500
Watching.

02:02:52.500 --> 02:02:53.700
Waiting.

02:02:53.700 --> 02:02:55.980
“Did you just let something in here?”

02:02:55.980 --> 02:02:56.880
He asked.

02:02:56.880 --> 02:02:59.340
“It feels like something’s watching me.”

02:02:59.340 --> 02:03:01.620
“No, D-080-1.”

02:03:01.620 --> 02:03:03.840
Dr. Smith responded.

02:03:03.840 --> 02:03:06.480
“We did not let anything into the room.”

02:03:06.480 --> 02:03:11.580
The man’s hands were shaking, and he could
feel sweat beading on his forehead.

02:03:11.580 --> 02:03:13.080
That couldn’t be true.

02:03:13.080 --> 02:03:15.120
He wasn’t alone in here.

02:03:15.120 --> 02:03:16.800
There, in the corner!

02:03:16.800 --> 02:03:21.780
There was a black mass, large and somehow
even darker than the rest of the room.

02:03:21.780 --> 02:03:26.340
He could feel its eyes on his, boring into
him.

02:03:26.340 --> 02:03:30.540
His heart thudded in his chest and he felt
like he might be sick.

02:03:30.540 --> 02:03:35.460
He tried to take a step back but his ankle
folded under him and he collapsed to the floor.

02:03:35.460 --> 02:03:36.600
“What do you see?”

02:03:36.600 --> 02:03:38.100
Dr. Smith asked.

02:03:38.100 --> 02:03:39.660
The man struggled to find the words.

02:03:39.660 --> 02:03:45.240
“This giant blackness, like someone just
standing in the corner.

02:03:45.240 --> 02:03:47.520
Oh God, it’s looking right at me!

02:03:47.520 --> 02:03:48.060
Let me out!”

02:03:48.060 --> 02:03:53.160
He climbed to his feet and felt his way along
the wall until he reached the door, and began

02:03:53.160 --> 02:03:54.960
to pound against it with his fists.

02:03:54.960 --> 02:03:58.860
The Doctor refused to let him out until he
described the being’s appearance.

02:03:58.860 --> 02:04:01.860
“It looks like a figure, hunched in the
corner.”

02:04:01.860 --> 02:04:03.000
“Is it a human?”

02:04:03.000 --> 02:04:04.680
Dr. Smith asked.

02:04:04.680 --> 02:04:08.520
Though he knew it was too dark for the doctor
to see, he shook his head.

02:04:09.720 --> 02:04:11.280
“It’s too big to be a human.

02:04:11.280 --> 02:04:14.280
It’s still looking at me, Doc, still staring.”

02:04:14.280 --> 02:04:20.400
Though he should have had adrenaline pumping
through his body, he felt suddenly sleepy,

02:04:20.400 --> 02:04:22.560
almost unable to keep his eyes open.

02:04:22.560 --> 02:04:24.180
“Move closer to it.”

02:04:24.180 --> 02:04:25.620
Dr. Smith ordered.

02:04:25.620 --> 02:04:29.580
The D-class obeyed, though he swayed on his
feet as he walked.

02:04:29.580 --> 02:04:35.160
“Its eyes look like vapor, just staring
at me.

02:04:36.240 --> 02:04:37.560
Like it wants me to do someth-“

02:04:37.560 --> 02:04:41.520
At this point, he fell to the ground again,
suddenly silent.

02:04:41.520 --> 02:04:46.320
Dr. Smith called out to him again and again,
but the man did not respond.

02:04:46.320 --> 02:04:52.620
When the research team opened the containment
chamber several minutes later, D-080-1 was

02:04:52.620 --> 02:04:52.860
gone.

02:04:52.860 --> 02:04:56.460
He was lost to the thing that waits for us
in the dark.

02:04:56.460 --> 02:05:00.000
He was lost to SCP-080.

02:05:00.000 --> 02:05:06.180
This was the first in a series of tests that
a Foundation research team, headed by Dr.

02:05:06.180 --> 02:05:11.160
Smith, performed in order to better understand
this shadowy figure and determine whether

02:05:11.160 --> 02:05:13.620
or not it has a physical body of any kind.

02:05:13.620 --> 02:05:16.620
When the results were&nbsp;
determined to be unsatisfactory,&nbsp;

02:05:16.620 --> 02:05:18.840
another experiment was conducted.

02:05:18.840 --> 02:05:24.120
A woman referred to as D-080-2 was selected
and sent into the room.

02:05:24.120 --> 02:05:28.020
This time, they would attempt to have the
D-class touch the entity.

02:05:28.020 --> 02:05:35.280
Upon entering the chamber, D-080-2 remarked
on how dark it was, and how difficult it was

02:05:35.280 --> 02:05:36.660
to see anything inside.

02:05:36.660 --> 02:05:40.320
After several minutes, however, she noticed
something standing in the room.

02:05:40.320 --> 02:05:46.680
When prompted, the only descriptor she could
give was that the entity had two eyes.

02:05:46.680 --> 02:05:50.880
Dr. Smith asked her to approach the entity
and report any changes.

02:05:50.880 --> 02:05:55.560
As she got closer, she became increasingly
drowsy and exhausted.

02:05:55.560 --> 02:06:02.700
When she reached out to touch SCP-080, she
went quiet and did not respond to any additional

02:06:02.700 --> 02:06:03.120
questions.

02:06:03.120 --> 02:06:08.220
She was found asleep in the corner of the
containment room, and was immediately examined

02:06:08.220 --> 02:06:09.120
by medical staff.

02:06:09.120 --> 02:06:14.580
No adverse physical effects were found, and
an interview was conducted to determine if

02:06:14.580 --> 02:06:16.980
there was any residual psychological impact.

02:06:16.980 --> 02:06:24.480
In her interview, D-080-2 was noticeably distant,
her expression and tone of voice both described

02:06:24.480 --> 02:06:26.040
as “spaced out.”

02:06:26.040 --> 02:06:31.020
When asked about her encounter with the entity,
she became increasingly upset and began to

02:06:31.020 --> 02:06:31.740
hyperventilate.

02:06:31.740 --> 02:06:37.320
She screamed: “It just stared and stared,
not moving but I felt something!

02:06:37.320 --> 02:06:39.660
I was on the floor and they were all over
me.

02:06:39.660 --> 02:06:40.740
They’re here!

02:06:40.740 --> 02:06:44.100
No, they’re trying to take me away, back
to that thing.

02:06:44.100 --> 02:06:45.540
I won’t go back!

02:06:45.540 --> 02:06:47.520
You can’t make me go back in there!”

02:06:47.520 --> 02:06:51.540
At this point, she lunged across the table
and attempted to attack Dr. Smith.

02:06:51.540 --> 02:06:55.320
She was removed from the interview room and
later terminated.

02:06:55.320 --> 02:07:01.020
A third experiment was conducted, using a
man referred to as D-080-3.

02:07:01.020 --> 02:07:06.420
In order to counteract the entity’s tranquilizing
effects, he was given a powerful amphetamine

02:07:06.420 --> 02:07:11.940
at a dose that would keep a person under ordinary
circumstances awake for at least 36 hours.

02:07:11.940 --> 02:07:18.480
When he entered the room, like all the others,
D-080-3 saw a shadowy figure standing in the

02:07:18.480 --> 02:07:19.200
middle of the room.

02:07:19.200 --> 02:07:24.780
He was told to stand still and watch the figure,
and report anything unusual that he might

02:07:24.780 --> 02:07:25.200
notice.

02:07:25.200 --> 02:07:30.420
After ten minutes, the subject became frightened
and demanded to be let out of the room.

02:07:30.420 --> 02:07:33.900
He pounded on the door, and attempted to wedge
it open.

02:07:33.900 --> 02:07:39.780
When he failed to open the door, he lunged
at SCP-080 and attempted to hit it with his

02:07:39.780 --> 02:07:40.260
fists.

02:07:40.260 --> 02:07:43.080
He promptly slumped to the floor and went
silent.

02:07:43.080 --> 02:07:47.820
His dead body was found in the room after
the experiment, and an autopsy determined

02:07:47.820 --> 02:07:50.220
the cause of death to be a severe heart attack.

02:07:50.220 --> 02:07:55.440
The researchers who entered to retrieve the
body felt unsettled as they did so, reporting

02:07:55.440 --> 02:08:00.240
a feeling that SCP-080 was looking directly
at them the entire time.

02:08:00.240 --> 02:08:05.280
Following the conclusion of these experiments,
the research team was able to draw several

02:08:05.280 --> 02:08:07.380
conclusions about SCP-080.

02:08:07.380 --> 02:08:12.480
It causes debilitating drowsiness in anyone
who enters its containment chamber.

02:08:12.480 --> 02:08:17.400
After thirty minutes of exposure, anyone who
is observing the entity will involuntarily

02:08:17.400 --> 02:08:18.720
fall into REM sleep.

02:08:18.720 --> 02:08:22.800
If there is any light in the room brighter
than a standard children’s night light,

02:08:22.800 --> 02:08:24.660
the entity will disappear.

02:08:24.660 --> 02:08:29.340
This should be treated as a containment breach
if and when it occurs.

02:08:29.340 --> 02:08:34.560
After conducting their experiments, Dr. Smith
and his research team began to experience

02:08:34.560 --> 02:08:36.240
highly upsetting dreams.

02:08:36.240 --> 02:08:38.940
While many of the staff&nbsp;
began requesting appointments&nbsp;

02:08:38.940 --> 02:08:41.700
with the medical team, Dr. Smith refused to

02:08:41.700 --> 02:08:47.040
discuss the nature of his dreams with any
on-site psychologists, insisting that he wasn’t

02:08:47.040 --> 02:08:49.620
going to let some silly nightmares get the
better of him.

02:08:49.620 --> 02:08:51.900
As the weeks wore on, however, he became&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:51.900 --> 02:08:53.220
increasingly
withdrawn.

02:08:53.220 --> 02:08:58.440
His colleagues noted dark circles under his
eyes, and noticed his near-constant consumption

02:08:58.440 --> 02:09:02.160
of coffee that far surpassed anything they
had seen from him before.

02:09:02.160 --> 02:09:06.180
He seemed as if he was terrified of falling
asleep.

02:09:06.180 --> 02:09:10.380
One day, the exhaustion caught up to him and
he fell asleep at his desk.

02:09:10.380 --> 02:09:15.780
Everyone in the building heard his screams,
and when a security guard eventually shook

02:09:15.780 --> 02:09:21.000
him awake, his throat was so raw from crying
out in terror that he was coughing up globs

02:09:21.000 --> 02:09:21.420
of blood.

02:09:21.420 --> 02:09:26.040
Dr. Smith begged to be given an amnestic,
to help him forget what he had dreamed about,

02:09:26.040 --> 02:09:29.760
forget all of his dreams, but the request
was denied.

02:09:29.760 --> 02:09:33.960
He was placed on an indefinite leave of absence
and sent home.

02:09:33.960 --> 02:09:39.720
Two days later, the research team was given
a somber report: Dr. Smith had leapt off a

02:09:39.720 --> 02:09:39.900
bridge.

02:09:39.900 --> 02:09:45.060
Following Dr. Smith’s tragic demise, the
rest of his staff were given notebooks and

02:09:45.060 --> 02:09:49.140
encouraged to keep dream journals during the
course of their research in order to track

02:09:49.140 --> 02:09:52.500
the psychological impact of studying SCP-080.

02:09:52.500 --> 02:09:57.720
Additionally, they were required to turn these
journals in to the site psychologists for

02:09:57.720 --> 02:10:01.980
review, particularly if the dreams became
especially disturbing or violent.

02:10:01.980 --> 02:10:05.340
The following are excerpts from some of these
dream journals.

02:10:05.340 --> 02:10:07.500
Research Assistant Megan Vaughn:

02:10:07.500 --> 02:10:09.900
“Last night I dreamt I was lying in my bed.

02:10:09.900 --> 02:10:15.900
Not my bed now, in my apartment, but my childhood
bed with the baby pink sheets and the quilt

02:10:15.900 --> 02:10:16.740
my grandmother made.

02:10:16.740 --> 02:10:19.320
It felt so real, every detail.

02:10:19.320 --> 02:10:24.600
My dollhouse in the corner, my big teddy bear,
my tea set, and my closet.

02:10:24.600 --> 02:10:27.780
I was lying on my side, with my head facing
my closet.

02:10:27.780 --> 02:10:30.600
I used to be so scared of that closet.

02:10:30.600 --> 02:10:34.140
Every night I would sob until my dad checked
it for monsters.

02:10:34.140 --> 02:10:36.060
I couldn’t go to sleep until he did.

02:10:36.060 --> 02:10:38.880
But in my dream, I knew he hadn’t checked.

02:10:38.880 --> 02:10:42.660
And I just knew there was something in there
waiting for me to close my eyes.

02:10:42.660 --> 02:10:46.920
So I didn’t, I just stared at that closet
door and I waited for it to open.

02:10:46.920 --> 02:10:52.860
I started to hear this scraping noise, like
dragging something sharp across a wooden surface.

02:10:52.860 --> 02:10:55.980
Over and over again.

02:10:55.980 --> 02:10:59.940
But the door didn’t budge, no matter how
long I stared at it.

02:10:59.940 --> 02:11:02.280
All the while the noise just kept going.

02:11:02.280 --> 02:11:03.480
Scrape.

02:11:03.480 --> 02:11:04.380
Scrape.

02:11:04.380 --> 02:11:06.900
And the sound of soft, raspy breathing.

02:11:06.900 --> 02:11:08.640
But the closet stayed shut.

02:11:08.640 --> 02:11:11.460
Eventually, I rolled onto my back, and there
it was.

02:11:11.460 --> 02:11:15.120
On my ceiling, hanging over&nbsp;
me with its upside-down&nbsp;

02:11:15.120 --> 02:11:18.300
head and round, open mouth, an old woman with

02:11:18.300 --> 02:11:21.660
long stringy hair and fingernails as long
as my arms.

02:11:21.660 --> 02:11:25.140
She was scratching on the ceiling, and waiting
for me to look.

02:11:25.140 --> 02:11:28.020
I couldn’t move, I could just stare up at&nbsp;

02:11:28.020 --> 02:11:30.960
her as she took two of&nbsp;
those long, long fingernails

02:11:30.960 --> 02:11:34.860
and slowly inched them toward my eyes…and
then I woke up.

02:11:34.860 --> 02:11:38.700
I’m scared if I go back to sleep, she’ll
pick up right where she left off.”

02:11:38.700 --> 02:11:40.320
Dr. Owen Kohli:

02:11:40.320 --> 02:11:44.640
“I’m swimming in my family’s pond, and
it’s a beautiful sunny day outside.

02:11:44.640 --> 02:11:49.920
I can feel the sun’s heat on my skin, and
the crisp cold water cooling it every time

02:11:49.920 --> 02:11:51.120
I dip under the surface.

02:11:51.120 --> 02:11:55.920
I decide to swim down toward the bottom and
dive for rocks, and when I come back up, suddenly

02:11:55.920 --> 02:11:56.460
it’s dark.

02:11:56.460 --> 02:11:59.460
It’s the middle of the night, and the water
doesn’t look so clear anymore.

02:11:59.460 --> 02:12:01.200
I can’t see the bottom.

02:12:01.200 --> 02:12:03.180
I can’t see anything around me at all.

02:12:03.180 --> 02:12:06.060
And I feel something slither against my leg.

02:12:06.060 --> 02:12:09.120
I kick it away, but I just feel something
else on my other side.

02:12:09.120 --> 02:12:10.680
Slimy and quick.

02:12:10.680 --> 02:12:14.100
I can’t see it, but I can feel that it's
much bigger than me.

02:12:14.100 --> 02:12:17.700
So I start swimming toward the edge, trying
to get out before something worse happens.

02:12:17.700 --> 02:12:22.140
Then I feel this sharp pain, like a hundred
needles stabbing into my back.

02:12:22.740 --> 02:12:25.140
It hurts so bad I see red, but I keep swimming.

02:12:25.140 --> 02:12:29.880
I reached the edge and I try to pull myself
out but I can’t, there’s something on

02:12:29.880 --> 02:12:31.740
me and it’s so heavy I can’t get out.

02:12:31.740 --> 02:12:36.240
I look over my shoulder and I can now make
it out: it’s the biggest leech I’ve ever

02:12:36.240 --> 02:12:38.100
seen, and it’s latched on to me.

02:12:38.100 --> 02:12:40.620
I can see it pulsating, swallowing.

02:12:40.620 --> 02:12:41.880
It’s draining me.

02:12:41.880 --> 02:12:46.920
And I feel so weak all of a sudden, dizzy,
and I look down at my hands and they’re

02:12:46.920 --> 02:12:50.820
shriveling up right there, my fingers pruning
as I feel the blood being pulled out of me.

02:12:50.820 --> 02:12:56.580
My vision blurs and my head tips back and
I’m sinking down into the water as the leech

02:12:56.580 --> 02:12:57.300
keeps sucking.

02:12:57.300 --> 02:13:01.140
It pulls down into the muck at the bottom,
and everything goes dark.”

02:13:01.140 --> 02:13:03.480
Researcher Kathy Levine:

02:13:03.480 --> 02:13:07.440
“Okay, in my dream I was in my old house,
back when I lived out in the woods.

02:13:07.440 --> 02:13:09.600
No cell reception and no neighbors.

02:13:09.600 --> 02:13:12.300
I was in the shower, washing my hair I think?

02:13:12.300 --> 02:13:14.280
It’s hard to remember the details.

02:13:14.280 --> 02:13:17.880
I don’t remember the details of dreams very
well, but I’ll do my best.

02:13:17.880 --> 02:13:24.660
This part I do remember: I heard this sound,
like footsteps coming from the floor above

02:13:24.660 --> 02:13:28.680
me, that quiet thudding sound coming down
through the ceiling.

02:13:28.680 --> 02:13:31.800
I turned off the water to listen better, and
there it was again.

02:13:31.800 --> 02:13:33.660
Definitely footsteps.

02:13:33.660 --> 02:13:36.240
Someone was in my house.

02:13:36.240 --> 02:13:40.560
I threw on my clothes and slowly snuck out
of the bathroom, and made my way to the front

02:13:40.560 --> 02:13:40.860
door.

02:13:40.860 --> 02:13:44.220
I don’t know why, I just knew I needed to
get out of there.

02:13:44.220 --> 02:13:48.360
Just when I opened it, I heard the footsteps
behind me and I turned around, and there was

02:13:48.360 --> 02:13:49.440
this man there.

02:13:49.440 --> 02:13:54.900
Huge, like seven feet tall, massive tangled
beard, wild eyes, and holding an axe.

02:13:54.900 --> 02:13:58.740
We stared at each other for a long time, and
he just smiled.

02:13:58.740 --> 02:14:02.880
Like he was so sure he was going to kill me,
and have a lovely time doing it.

02:14:02.880 --> 02:14:07.800
I ran out of the house and into the woods,
and I could hear him coming after me.

02:14:07.800 --> 02:14:12.660
Branches hit me in the face and cut up my
arms as I ran, and I just knew I had to get

02:14:12.660 --> 02:14:12.840
away.

02:14:12.840 --> 02:14:17.700
But then I started to get that feeling you
get when you run in dreams, like your legs

02:14:17.700 --> 02:14:18.120
don’t work.

02:14:18.120 --> 02:14:19.740
Like you’re pushing through water.

02:14:19.740 --> 02:14:23.100
I was running as fast as I could, but I wasn’t
going forward at all.

02:14:23.100 --> 02:14:29.100
And then I felt a hand grabbing my hair, yanking
my head back, and the blade of the axe slicing

02:14:29.100 --> 02:14:30.060
across my cheek.

02:14:30.060 --> 02:14:33.540
He whispered in my ear, and his breath smelled
like rotting flesh.

02:14:33.540 --> 02:14:38.880
And I’ll never forget this next part, he
said “We’re not done playing yet.

02:14:38.880 --> 02:14:46.500
I’m going to take you apart in tiny pieces,
and save your head for last.”

02:14:46.500 --> 02:14:48.240
Dr. Robert Gray:

02:14:48.240 --> 02:14:50.880
“I was sitting on the couch, next to my
wife.

02:14:50.880 --> 02:14:52.440
We were watching television.

02:14:52.440 --> 02:14:57.360
I turned to ask her a question, and she was
staring at me with these dilated pupils, so

02:14:57.360 --> 02:14:59.100
big her eyes looked all black.

02:14:59.700 --> 02:15:02.160
Then she opened her mouth, to speak to me,
I thought.

02:15:02.160 --> 02:15:08.580
But it got wider and wider, and it had no
teeth, just this expanding tunnel of pink

02:15:08.580 --> 02:15:13.080
flesh that started to suck me inside until
my head disappeared into her mouth and I began

02:15:13.080 --> 02:15:13.680
to suffocate.

02:15:13.680 --> 02:15:16.500
I haven’t been able to look my wife in the
eye all day today.”

02:15:16.500 --> 02:15:18.660
Other dream journals were less detailed.

02:15:18.660 --> 02:15:23.880
Research Assistant Matt Guerrero simply wrote
“My dog ate me,” while Senior Researcher

02:15:23.880 --> 02:15:28.860
Barbara Bradley wrote: “I was stuck inside
my fish tank, and my fish were feeding me

02:15:28.860 --> 02:15:29.700
human flakes.”

02:15:29.700 --> 02:15:32.100
No matter how frightening or absurd the dreams&nbsp;

02:15:32.100 --> 02:15:35.040
detailed were, all the&nbsp;
staff reporting experiencing

02:15:35.040 --> 02:15:39.840
feelings of intense stress and panic while
having them, and after waking up.

02:15:39.840 --> 02:15:47.400
SCP-080 is contained in a 4m x 4m room with
a small antechamber on the south wall, providing

02:15:47.400 --> 02:15:49.320
researchers with access to the space.

02:15:49.320 --> 02:15:53.820
On the other side of the north wall, there
is an observation room where researchers can

02:15:53.820 --> 02:15:55.680
view the containment room through a window.

02:15:55.680 --> 02:16:00.480
The window is outfitted with thin blackout
curtains, which release when the observation

02:16:00.480 --> 02:16:02.340
room door has fully closed.

02:16:02.340 --> 02:16:05.880
No one may attempt to remove SCP-080 from&nbsp;

02:16:05.880 --> 02:16:09.180
its containment at any time,&nbsp;
under any circumstances.

02:16:09.180 --> 02:16:15.540
No light sources may be brought into the room,
and no more than one seven watt incandescent

02:16:15.540 --> 02:16:17.280
lightbulb may be lit inside.

02:16:17.280 --> 02:16:23.100
Additionally, no objects may be brought into
the room that can be used to hide SCP-080

02:16:23.100 --> 02:16:24.240
in any way.

02:16:24.240 --> 02:16:29.640
Anyone who breaks these rules will be swiftly
and strictly disciplined, and may be subject

02:16:29.640 --> 02:16:30.480
to termination.

02:16:30.480 --> 02:16:37.020
Following Incident 080-1, the containment
measures have been reevaluated and additional

02:16:37.020 --> 02:16:38.640
measures have been proposed.

02:16:38.640 --> 02:16:43.440
During this incident, two senior researchers
entered the observation room and released

02:16:43.439 --> 02:16:44.580
the blackout curtains.

02:16:44.580 --> 02:16:50.460
Certain that this was a safe way to observe
SCP-080 without being influenced by its adverse

02:16:50.460 --> 02:16:53.160
effects, the two remained in the room for
forty minutes.

02:16:53.160 --> 02:16:55.139
At this point, the two fell asleep.

02:16:55.140 --> 02:16:57.960
It is unknown what exactly happened after
this.

02:16:57.960 --> 02:17:02.580
However, after this incident, all staff suffering
from anomalous nightmares reported having

02:17:02.580 --> 02:17:06.300
their first restful night of sleep since the
research had begun.

02:17:06.300 --> 02:17:12.300
It was as if the entity’s appetite had been
temporarily sated, and it had released the

02:17:12.300 --> 02:17:14.040
rest of the team from its influence.

02:17:14.040 --> 02:17:20.040
In light of Incident 080-1, a member of the
research team suggested that a D Class be

02:17:20.040 --> 02:17:25.740
left in SCP-080’s room once a month in order
to feed it, and protect the rest of the team

02:17:25.740 --> 02:17:27.120
from psychological harm.

02:17:27.120 --> 02:17:32.340
After some debate, and opposition from the
ethics committee, this proposal was approved

02:17:32.340 --> 02:17:33.660
by the O5 Council.

02:17:33.660 --> 02:17:38.340
Now, the entity is kept on a regular feeding
schedule, and the staff’s dream journals

02:17:38.340 --> 02:17:40.620
have been relatively uneventful ever since.

02:17:40.620 --> 02:17:46.140
It turns out that sometimes the price for
a good night’s sleep is just a little bit

02:17:46.140 --> 02:17:48.000
of human sacrifice.

02:17:48.000 --> 02:17:54.600
Who doesn’t love a walk through a dark forest? The&nbsp;
sight of branches set against the low moonlight&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:54.600 --> 02:18:00.241
looking like all manner of dark and twisted claws&nbsp;
reaching out of the night to grab at you. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:00.240 --> 02:18:06.120
step brings with it the snap of a broken twig&nbsp;
that practically echoes around you. Whenever a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:06.120 --> 02:18:12.359
breeze rustles the leaves on the trees, you feel&nbsp;
like something might just be following you, moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:12.359 --> 02:18:18.479
through the forest towards you. It’s easy to get&nbsp;
lost in a forest at night, after all, that’s why&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:18.479 --> 02:18:24.839
the children’s song warns us that “if you go down&nbsp;
to the woods today, you’d better not go alone.”&nbsp;

02:18:24.840 --> 02:18:31.620
The image of a forest in the darkness has inspired&nbsp;
fear for generations, from fireside folktales&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:31.620 --> 02:18:36.780
telling of wolves and monsters lurking among&nbsp;
the trees, to modern horror games about a tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:36.780 --> 02:18:43.679
faceless man in a suit stalking you through the&nbsp;
woods. And then, of course, there’s SCP-060,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:43.680 --> 02:18:52.080
otherwise known as the Infernal Occult Skeleton.
Now, despite its name, SCP-060 is, in actual fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:52.080 --> 02:18:58.140
a forest. Or at least, it’s a forest to begin&nbsp;
with. A picturesque grove of seventeen tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:58.140 --> 02:19:04.500
white oak trees, spread out across eight acres&nbsp;
of land in rural northeast Minnesota. It almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:04.500 --> 02:19:09.359
looks like something out of a tourist brochure,&nbsp;
a beautiful stretch of forest sitting under clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:09.359 --> 02:19:14.820
skies, well, during the daytime anyway.
If you ever find yourself hiking through&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:14.820 --> 02:19:19.620
a corner of Minnesotan forest that isn’t in&nbsp;
any of the guidebooks, then tread carefully.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:19.620 --> 02:19:25.620
You might just stumble upon the demolished ruins&nbsp;
of a house that used to stand among the trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:25.620 --> 02:19:32.880
out in seclusion. And a word of advice to you if&nbsp;
you happen across this place, do not, under any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:32.880 --> 02:19:39.420
circumstances, stop walking for a smoke break.
Of course, thanks to the good folks at the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:39.420 --> 02:19:46.020
Foundation, you’re unlikely to ever just wander&nbsp;
your way into SCP-060. More likely, they’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:46.020 --> 02:19:51.720
administer you with amnestics – the Foundation’s&nbsp;
patented memory-altering drugs – and send you on&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:51.720 --> 02:19:57.960
your merry way, totally oblivious to the huge,&nbsp;
hard-to-miss greenhouses containing SCP-060.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:57.960 --> 02:20:03.600
Beyond those glass walls, you might have caught&nbsp;
glimpses of Foundation personnel watering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:03.600 --> 02:20:11.040
trees, carefully tending to each SCP-060 specimen.
Maybe you saw them gathering up leaves and pruning&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:11.040 --> 02:20:16.080
each tree individually, composting every part&nbsp;
of dead plant matter instead of leaving the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:16.080 --> 02:20:21.359
white oaks to grow freely. And perhaps you&nbsp;
even noticed that not one member of personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:21.359 --> 02:20:27.479
was carrying a lighter on their person, nor a&nbsp;
taser, or so much as a small box of matches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:27.479 --> 02:20:33.120
nothing that can start a fire. Or rather,&nbsp;
you would remember seeing all that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:33.120 --> 02:20:39.479
if the amnestics hadn’t already made you forget.
But what’s so special about these trees? Why would&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:39.479 --> 02:20:44.459
the SCP Foundation go to the extent of housing&nbsp;
a collection of white oaks in greenhouses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:44.460 --> 02:20:50.220
and meticulously oversee their growth? What&nbsp;
is it about these particular specimens that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:50.220 --> 02:20:56.940
make personnel so cautious about fire&nbsp;
safety? And why on earth is SCP-060,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:56.939 --> 02:21:03.179
a collection of trees, referred to by the&nbsp;
nickname ‘the Infernal Occult Skeleton’?&nbsp;

02:21:03.180 --> 02:21:07.140
Well, the answer to all those questions&nbsp;
becomes pretty apparent the moment any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:07.140 --> 02:21:14.161
of the SCP-060 oak trees catch fire, and&nbsp;
something comes hurtling out of the forest.&nbsp;

02:21:14.160 --> 02:21:20.220
That something is known as SCP-060-Alpha.&nbsp;
Standing at just over two meters tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:20.220 --> 02:21:25.500
the entity takes the form of an adult human&nbsp;
skeleton. Much more than just a spooky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:25.500 --> 02:21:31.800
scary collection of bones, SCP-060-Alpha is&nbsp;
fully animate, capable of moving of its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:31.800 --> 02:21:37.860
accord without the aid of muscles or a nervous&nbsp;
system. Oh, and it also happens to be on fire.&nbsp;

02:21:37.859 --> 02:21:45.179
Move aside Ghost Rider, SCP-060-Alpha is engulfed&nbsp;
from skull to toe bones in bright white flames,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:45.180 --> 02:21:50.281
burning at a temperature of approximately&nbsp;
fifteen-hundred degrees Celsius, or almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:50.280 --> 02:21:55.200
three thousand degrees Fahrenheit. For reference,&nbsp;
that’s just shy of the melting point of iron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:55.200 --> 02:22:00.120
and hot enough to grant a human being&nbsp;
a quick, but agonizingly painful death.&nbsp;

02:22:00.120 --> 02:22:05.220
Granted after a few seconds of that heat your&nbsp;
nerve endings would be scalded, so maybe you&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:05.220 --> 02:22:10.440
wouldn’t feel that much pain. But fifteen-hundred&nbsp;
Celsius is enough to burn the moisture right out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:10.439 --> 02:22:15.419
of your skin, melt your eyeballs, and generally&nbsp;
fry you to a crisp in a matter of minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:15.420 --> 02:22:21.840
if not seconds. Good thing SCP-060-Alpha isn’t&nbsp;
known for being highly aggressive and hostile.&nbsp;

02:22:21.840 --> 02:22:27.900
Oh, wait, it is? Ah, not good.
Upon manifestation, the burning&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:27.899 --> 02:22:32.639
skeleton will attempt to do as much damage as&nbsp;
possible, and usually to whoever is closest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:32.640 --> 02:22:39.060
It can appear at any time, and after as little as&nbsp;
twenty grams worth of one of the SCP-060 trees is&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:39.060 --> 02:22:44.100
burned. As if being actively hostile and burning&nbsp;
hot enough to reshape metal wasn’t bad enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:44.100 --> 02:22:51.241
SCP-060-Alpha has also shown itself to be fiercely&nbsp;
intelligent. The entity seems to retain knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:51.240 --> 02:22:55.559
whenever it manifests and has gained a&nbsp;
growing familiarity with the layout of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:55.560 --> 02:23:02.161
Foundation site that contains the SCP-060 oaks.
The Infernal Occult Skeleton’s methods of attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:02.160 --> 02:23:06.899
tend to include throwing its entire body at&nbsp;
flammable materials; however, it will avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:06.899 --> 02:23:13.620
causing any damage to specimens of SCP-060. The&nbsp;
skeletal entity can run at speeds of up to fifty&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:13.620 --> 02:23:19.200
miles per hour, now that’s almost the same speed&nbsp;
as a gazelle. Just picturing anything traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:19.200 --> 02:23:23.580
towards you at that speed is horrifying, let&nbsp;
alone something heading straight for you at&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:23.580 --> 02:23:29.100
gazelle levels of speed while also on fire!
It’s this combination of speed and heat that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:29.100 --> 02:23:35.580
means SCP-060-Alpha poses such a threat to anyone&nbsp;
close whenever it appears; if left unchecked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:35.580 --> 02:23:40.620
the entity could easily cause colossal and&nbsp;
widespread forest fires and property damage.&nbsp;

02:23:40.620 --> 02:23:46.439
Interestingly, any areas that SCP-060-Alpha&nbsp;
does burn with its flames, will start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:46.439 --> 02:23:52.620
yield saplings of the SCP-060 oaks, around&nbsp;
six weeks after the fire has stopped. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:52.620 --> 02:23:57.000
Foundation doesn’t allow these saplings to grow&nbsp;
to full size, and instead pulls them from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:57.000 --> 02:24:03.180
ground and disposes of them, composting the&nbsp;
saplings to feed the other SCP-060 specimens.&nbsp;

02:24:03.180 --> 02:24:09.480
Luckily, the biggest strength of SCP-060-Alpha,&nbsp;
its flames, also happens to be its greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:09.479 --> 02:24:14.099
weakness. It is possible to fight the fires&nbsp;
of the Infernal Occult Skeleton by dousing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:14.100 --> 02:24:19.500
it with water or any other materials capable of&nbsp;
dousing flames, whether it’s sand or foam from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:19.500 --> 02:24:24.660
a fire extinguisher. Of course, this is a lot&nbsp;
hotter and harder to put out than any ordinary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:24.660 --> 02:24:30.059
smaller-scale fire, but despite being&nbsp;
a difficult task, it’s not impossible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:30.060 --> 02:24:34.980
About five hundred liters of water should do the&nbsp;
trick if you’ve got a big enough bucket nearby.&nbsp;

02:24:34.979 --> 02:24:41.099
After that, SCP-060-Alpha will be weakened,&nbsp;
gradually collapsing and turning into dust.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:41.100 --> 02:24:47.460
However, if another part of an SCP-060 tree is&nbsp;
burned and the entity reappears, it is believed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:47.460 --> 02:24:52.560
that this will be the same Infernal Occult&nbsp;
Skeleton, rather than a new version of the bone&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:52.560 --> 02:24:57.900
burning being. So, we have a grove of oak trees&nbsp;
that manifest a flaming skeleton if they are ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:57.899 --> 02:25:02.879
burned. Maybe that’s not the weirdest thing you’d&nbsp;
see in a Minnesotan forest, but wait, there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:02.880 --> 02:25:07.740
something else. Cast your mind back a few minutes,&nbsp;
and you’ll remember that we mentioned some ruins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:07.740 --> 02:25:14.760
the remains of a demolished house that used to&nbsp;
stand secluded among the SCP-060 white oak trees.&nbsp;

02:25:14.760 --> 02:25:18.600
Knowing that the Infernal Occult Skeleton&nbsp;
can appear from the oaks might make it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:18.600 --> 02:25:22.800
obvious what happened to this house, but&nbsp;
there’s still a story to be told here.&nbsp;

02:25:22.800 --> 02:25:28.080
The house’s owner was a man by the name of&nbsp;
Johnathan Corhill. Now, Johnathan was something&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:28.080 --> 02:25:34.620
of an odd man, considered a bit of an eccentric to&nbsp;
some. He preferred to spend his time in solitude,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:34.620 --> 02:25:40.140
alone with his own thoughts for company, rather&nbsp;
than mingling among the rest of the world. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:40.140 --> 02:25:44.701
his own family noticed that Mr. Corhill was&nbsp;
drifting away from them, becoming a more bitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:44.700 --> 02:25:50.760
nihilistic person in his old age, and choosing&nbsp;
isolation over human connection. Now, sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:50.760 --> 02:25:54.781
loneliness doesn’t hold much appeal&nbsp;
to everyone, but sometimes there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:54.780 --> 02:25:59.519
people who just prefer being alone. That&nbsp;
might be what drew Johnathan Corhill to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:59.520 --> 02:26:04.500
his secluded little house in the forests of&nbsp;
Minnesota, somewhere no one would bother him.&nbsp;

02:26:04.500 --> 02:26:09.359
For the most part, the rest of the Corhill family&nbsp;
adjusted to their eccentric relative’s behavior.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:09.359 --> 02:26:13.080
Johnathan would have rarely accepted&nbsp;
visitors to his house in the forest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:13.080 --> 02:26:18.660
but he still kept in contact with those he’d been&nbsp;
close with. Most notably, he’d regularly share&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:18.660 --> 02:26:24.359
phone calls with his brother, one Christopher&nbsp;
Corhill. That is... Until something seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:24.359 --> 02:26:30.780
to change unexpectedly, in the year 1996.
On one of their calls, Johnathan outright&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:30.780 --> 02:26:35.639
told Christopher to never contact him again,&nbsp;
severing all ties with any remaining family&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:35.640 --> 02:26:40.980
members and friends in the outside world.&nbsp;
Johnathan cut everyone off, living within&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:40.979 --> 02:26:46.139
his own bubble where he could immerse himself in&nbsp;
his unusual interests. According to Christopher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:46.140 --> 02:26:51.480
his brother had seemed otherwise normal up until&nbsp;
a certain phone conversation, but Johnathan had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:51.479 --> 02:26:56.519
become obsessed with the occult. Specifically,&nbsp;
he had embroiled himself in the history of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:56.520 --> 02:27:02.041
Victorian-era, and certain supernatural practices&nbsp;
that had been undertaken in that time period.&nbsp;

02:27:02.040 --> 02:27:07.800
Now whether Christopher honored his brother’s&nbsp;
wish to sever ties is unknown. A mail carrier&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:07.800 --> 02:27:12.960
would visit Johnathan’s home in the woods not long&nbsp;
after their phone call. Maybe among the envelopes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:12.960 --> 02:27:17.580
this courier was delivering what could have been&nbsp;
a letter from Christopher, or other members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:17.580 --> 02:27:22.740
the Corhill family, begging their estranged&nbsp;
relative to come back to the world. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:22.740 --> 02:27:27.960
even people who claim to prefer being on their&nbsp;
own sometimes need human interaction. Talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:27.960 --> 02:27:32.700
to people, being in the presence of friends&nbsp;
and family, are hugely important factors in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:32.700 --> 02:27:37.380
maintaining a positive state of mental health.
But what happens when someone rejects that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:37.380 --> 02:27:42.180
entirely and instead becomes lost in&nbsp;
their obsessive study of the occult? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:42.180 --> 02:27:47.701
the mail carrier was the first to find out.
Arriving at Johnathan Corhill’s woodland house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:47.700 --> 02:27:52.679
the courier found the place looking almost&nbsp;
skeletal, a shell of the building that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:52.680 --> 02:27:58.140
once stood in the forest. According to the locals,&nbsp;
the carrier had been sent to deliver a notice to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:58.140 --> 02:28:02.880
Mr Corhill, explaining that his house was&nbsp;
being foreclosed. But it seemed someone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:03.540 --> 02:28:08.939
or something, had beaten them to it. A&nbsp;
fire had spread from the house’s fireplace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:08.939 --> 02:28:14.639
quickly engulfing the entire structure,&nbsp;
presumably with Johnathan still inside.&nbsp;

02:28:14.640 --> 02:28:18.960
It wasn’t until later that very same year&nbsp;
that Johnathan Corhill was officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:18.960 --> 02:28:24.480
reported as a missing person case with local&nbsp;
authorities. Any search that was undertaken&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:24.479 --> 02:28:29.219
in an attempt to find him uncovered&nbsp;
next to no evidence of his whereabouts.&nbsp;

02:28:29.220 --> 02:28:34.920
To this day, nobody knows for certain if&nbsp;
Johnathan Corhill is dead or alive, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:34.920 --> 02:28:40.319
whereabouts are unknown. On the surface, it might&nbsp;
be easy to make the assumption that the Infernal&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:40.319 --> 02:28:46.319
Occult Skeleton reduced the reclusive old man to&nbsp;
nothing more than a cinder. It definitely seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:46.319 --> 02:28:51.359
plausible that Johnathan, collecting firewood to&nbsp;
keep himself warm in his isolation, accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:51.359 --> 02:28:58.439
chopped down part of an SCP-060 oak, put it in his&nbsp;
fireplace, and called forth the vengeful flaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:58.439 --> 02:29:05.460
bones. But perhaps we shouldn’t be so certain.
After all, Corhill’s house wasn’t entirely burned&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:05.460 --> 02:29:10.920
down, despite the entity normally trying to cause&nbsp;
as much damage as possible whenever it appears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:10.920 --> 02:29:18.060
And on top of that, no human remains were found&nbsp;
in the house. And the skeleton of SCP-060-Alpha&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:18.060 --> 02:29:24.600
had to have come from somewhere, right?
SCP-060 offers a few warnings, and not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:24.600 --> 02:29:29.281
about the dangers of traveling through the forest&nbsp;
alone. The appearance of the flaming skeleton&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:29.280 --> 02:29:34.740
whenever the SCP-060 white oaks are burned&nbsp;
could serve as a reminder that we need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:34.740 --> 02:29:40.319
vigilant in protecting the forests of this world.&nbsp;
Trees are one of our few sustainable resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:40.319 --> 02:29:46.139
but for every one we cut down or that catches&nbsp;
fire, it takes years to regrow a replacement.&nbsp;

02:29:46.140 --> 02:29:51.180
And perhaps the third and final warning&nbsp;
of the Infernal Occult Skeleton is simply:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:51.180 --> 02:29:57.300
don’t play with matches, especially around&nbsp;
trees. Otherwise, you might get burned.

02:29:57.300 --> 02:30:00.120
Imagine if you could predict the future.

02:30:00.120 --> 02:30:06.240
Not perfectly, mind you, but with enough accuracy
that brilliant enough minds - say, the best

02:30:06.240 --> 02:30:11.519
and brightest of the SCP Foundation - could
plausibly reverse-engineer the main determinative

02:30:11.520 --> 02:30:14.760
factors that caused a certain timeline to
form.

02:30:14.760 --> 02:30:20.760
Imagine if, through carefully studying these
determinative factors, the Foundation could

02:30:20.760 --> 02:30:25.500
carefully shape the future into one that’s
more favorable for the human race than all

02:30:25.500 --> 02:30:26.280
the alternatives.

02:30:26.280 --> 02:30:29.399
The “Preferred Option”, if you will.

02:30:29.399 --> 02:30:31.500
Would this not be advantageous?

02:30:31.500 --> 02:30:37.080
Your next question is a very natural one,
given the circumstances: How does one predict

02:30:37.080 --> 02:30:38.760
the future in such a manner?

02:30:38.760 --> 02:30:45.060
Well, the answer is uncomplicated, but that
doesn’t by any means make it easy: You go

02:30:45.060 --> 02:30:49.081
there, spend a few months looking around,
and then come back to report your findings.

02:30:49.080 --> 02:30:52.920
That’s right, folks - We’re not talking
psychics and seers here.

02:30:52.920 --> 02:30:57.480
Prepare to expand your mind and please don’t
worry if it all gets a little…

02:30:57.479 --> 02:30:58.919
timey wimey.

02:30:58.920 --> 02:31:04.800
Because SCP-2003 is the SCP Foundation’s
self-made time machine.

02:31:04.800 --> 02:31:11.400
Even most of the staff at the SCP Foundation
itself don’t know about SCP-2003, given

02:31:11.399 --> 02:31:14.339
the highly sensitive nature of the projects
surrounding it.

02:31:14.340 --> 02:31:20.400
Much like SCP-2000 is a trump card securing
our present in the case of a catastrophic

02:31:20.399 --> 02:31:26.879
XK-Class End of the World Scenario, SCP-2003
is our prophylactic for such a thing happening

02:31:26.880 --> 02:31:28.440
in the foreseeable future.

02:31:28.439 --> 02:31:34.919
What’s far more unique about SCP-2003 is
that the SCP Foundation created this ace in

02:31:34.920 --> 02:31:36.359
the hole from scratch.

02:31:36.359 --> 02:31:43.200
The SCP-2003 Time Machine was invented over
a 25 year period by reverse-engineering the

02:31:43.200 --> 02:31:48.899
anomalous technology of three different classified
anomalies and retrofitting them into our own

02:31:48.899 --> 02:31:50.580
non-anomalous framework.

02:31:50.580 --> 02:31:56.640
The massive machine is housed in Armed Site
47, a remote and well-guarded facility disguised

02:31:56.640 --> 02:31:57.720
as an oil refinery.

02:31:57.720 --> 02:32:04.320
While extensive records of SCP-2003’s construction
have been made by the Foundation, and it stands

02:32:04.319 --> 02:32:09.000
to reason that the machine could be reliably
and successfully reproduced in a different

02:32:09.000 --> 02:32:14.040
context, even the most intelligent scientists
taking part in the project couldn’t explain

02:32:14.040 --> 02:32:16.500
how or why it actually operates.

02:32:16.500 --> 02:32:20.100
In the words of another mad inventor, “It
just works.”

02:32:20.100 --> 02:32:23.640
The operating principles&nbsp;
of SCP-2003 are relatively&nbsp;

02:32:23.640 --> 02:32:26.100
simple to understand: It is able to break

02:32:26.100 --> 02:32:29.040
the laws of the space-time&nbsp;
continuum by immediately&nbsp;

02:32:29.040 --> 02:32:32.280
transporting anything or anyone placed in

02:32:32.280 --> 02:32:34.319
its central chamber to some point in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:34.319 --> 02:32:35.280
chronological
future.

02:32:35.280 --> 02:32:38.160
The subjects transported forwards will remain&nbsp;

02:32:38.160 --> 02:32:41.340
in this future for several&nbsp;
months before instantaneously

02:32:41.340 --> 02:32:45.240
being transported back to the exact location
they were standing in the future.

02:32:45.240 --> 02:32:50.580
In order to prevent some kind of unfortunate
accident, like phasing back halfway through

02:32:50.580 --> 02:32:55.740
a wall and becoming unpleasant modern art,
the Foundation has established a secure facility

02:32:55.740 --> 02:32:59.880
for travelers to head and wait out the rest
of their time when their mission is complete.

02:32:59.880 --> 02:33:04.260
Through extensive testing, including that
which was performed under the purview of Project

02:33:04.260 --> 02:33:09.240
XN-SHEPHERD, the Foundation has discovered
a great deal about the nature of time travel

02:33:09.240 --> 02:33:11.280
via SCP-2003.

02:33:11.280 --> 02:33:16.380
We’ll outline the most crucial caveats here,
so what happens next makes a lot more sense

02:33:16.380 --> 02:33:16.800
to you.

02:33:16.800 --> 02:33:20.700
After all, if time travel was easy, everyone
would do it.

02:33:20.700 --> 02:33:26.040
First, as we alluded to earlier, the data
collected by SCP-2003 on the nature of the

02:33:26.040 --> 02:33:29.939
future is often unclear,&nbsp;
imprecise, and unreliable.

02:33:29.939 --> 02:33:35.879
For example, the data collected from 2003
did prove extremely useful in predicting and

02:33:35.880 --> 02:33:40.500
preventing a massive security breach over
at Site-19 in 1997.

02:33:40.500 --> 02:33:45.180
So naturally, when it predicted a devastating
series of earthquakes off the West Coast of

02:33:45.180 --> 02:33:51.241
the United States in 1999 - an event that
several agents sent through SCP-2003 observed

02:33:51.240 --> 02:33:55.260
directly - it came as a shock to everyone
when nothing happened.

02:33:55.260 --> 02:34:00.300
The Foundation discovered, following this,
that all predictions needed to be contextualized

02:34:00.300 --> 02:34:05.880
through heaps of metadata for it to be of
any real use in predicting or preventing our

02:34:05.880 --> 02:34:06.900
specific future.

02:34:06.899 --> 02:34:12.240
The Foundation also discovered that certain
individuals had a strangely disproportionate

02:34:12.240 --> 02:34:14.700
effect on the unfolding of future events.

02:34:14.700 --> 02:34:19.920
Let’s say, for example, SCP-2003 discovers
that a new type of nuclear weapon will be

02:34:19.920 --> 02:34:24.780
invented in 2028 and quickly adopted by a
number of leading nations by 2030.

02:34:24.780 --> 02:34:30.420
And by 2035, tensions will rise, sabers will
rattle, and this nuclear weapon will be used

02:34:30.420 --> 02:34:33.660
en masse to destroy human society as we know
it.

02:34:33.660 --> 02:34:36.359
Naturally, in order to&nbsp;
prevent this, the Foundation&nbsp;

02:34:36.359 --> 02:34:38.759
might see to it that certain groups of nuclear

02:34:38.760 --> 02:34:42.720
scientists, certain generals, and certain
world leaders get liquidated.

02:34:42.720 --> 02:34:47.880
And yet, another trip into the future shows
that this massive nuclear war was not averted.

02:34:47.880 --> 02:34:48.660
But why?

02:34:48.660 --> 02:34:53.760
Because, it just so happened that this event
was inexplicably tied to the birth of a little

02:34:53.760 --> 02:35:00.360
boy named James Hoskins in Saskatoon circa
2025, despite little Jimmy Hoskins seemingly

02:35:00.359 --> 02:35:04.979
having nothing to do with the actual development
of the technology - Seeing as he’s only

02:35:04.979 --> 02:35:07.319
ten years old when the bombs start falling.

02:35:07.319 --> 02:35:12.479
The Foundation scientists working under Project
XN-SHEPHERD keep a database of all of these

02:35:12.479 --> 02:35:18.419
highly determinative individuals, also known
as Magnifier Individuals, so they can keep

02:35:18.420 --> 02:35:21.359
tabs on how they’re affecting any future
timelines.

02:35:21.359 --> 02:35:26.939
Speaking of future timelines, we’re afraid
to tell you that this penultimate caveat isn’t

02:35:26.939 --> 02:35:32.819
exactly a pleasant one: There are few to any
cohesive future timelines where humanity survives

02:35:32.819 --> 02:35:33.479
long term.

02:35:33.479 --> 02:35:34.740
Bummer, right?

02:35:34.740 --> 02:35:39.840
The Foundation calls these loose timelines
“Determinative Sets”, and in the majority

02:35:39.840 --> 02:35:46.260
of them, human civilization collapses, all
humans die, and in some cases, the earth becomes

02:35:46.260 --> 02:35:49.140
completely uninhabitable to all forms of life.

02:35:49.140 --> 02:35:54.180
The Foundation is currently seeking a more
optimistic option through controlled manipulations

02:35:54.180 --> 02:36:00.781
of the causal stream in our time, but currently,
all we have is the preferred option: Option

02:36:00.780 --> 02:36:01.800
XN.

02:36:01.800 --> 02:36:06.720
And if you’re someone who would jump at
the chance to travel into the future and take

02:36:06.720 --> 02:36:11.400
a gander at all the wondrous or terrifying
sights, there’s actually one pretty major

02:36:11.399 --> 02:36:17.519
caveat of SCP-2003 that we’ve been playing
rather close to the chest: Early Foundation

02:36:17.520 --> 02:36:23.460
tests found out that the time travel process
via SCP-2003 is extremely damaging to plant

02:36:23.460 --> 02:36:24.600
and animal tissue.

02:36:24.600 --> 02:36:29.760
Rather than just going on a wacky time travel
adventure like Doctor Who or Austin Powers,

02:36:29.760 --> 02:36:34.500
it’d be a little more like stepping into
a giant microwave while dressed in a spacesuit

02:36:34.500 --> 02:36:37.500
made of aluminum foil: You’re gonna die
a horrible death.

02:36:37.500 --> 02:36:42.840
But there is one silver lining - well, maybe
not “silver” from your perspective, probably

02:36:42.840 --> 02:36:48.360
more like pewter - the Foundation has discovered
a way to viably send human-adjacent subjects

02:36:48.359 --> 02:36:52.500
through time with SCP-2003 without instantaneous
death…

02:36:52.500 --> 02:36:55.439
We just can’t promise that you’re going
to like it.

02:36:55.439 --> 02:37:00.120
You see, the one kind of organic tissue that
seems to survive the SCP-2003 time travel

02:37:00.120 --> 02:37:03.000
process is the human brain and nervous system.

02:37:03.600 --> 02:37:08.220
Due to the highly controlled nature of Project
XN-SHEPHERD, the Foundation can’t just send

02:37:08.220 --> 02:37:13.980
in D-Classes to do the job, they instead use
actual agents - though mostly ones who are

02:37:13.979 --> 02:37:17.879
nearing or beyond retirement or are suffering
from a terminal illness.

02:37:17.880 --> 02:37:21.120
These Agents are dosed on&nbsp;
a course of anti-anxiety,&nbsp;

02:37:21.120 --> 02:37:24.300
anti-depressant, and antipsychotic chemotherapy

02:37:24.300 --> 02:37:26.640
to toughen their minds for the horrors to
come.

02:37:26.640 --> 02:37:31.440
Though the exact nature of these horrors is
kept secret from them until it’s already

02:37:31.439 --> 02:37:31.859
happened.

02:37:31.859 --> 02:37:37.799
You may be familiar with one of the Foundation’s
most well-known front companies: Boston Dynamics,

02:37:37.800 --> 02:37:43.140
as well as one of their most famous products,
the robotic, quadrupedal probe known as BigDog.

02:37:43.140 --> 02:37:47.760
Well, in order to send a sentient being through
time without them being completely destroyed

02:37:47.760 --> 02:37:53.340
by SCP-2003, the agent’s brain and nervous
system are entirely removed from their body,

02:37:53.340 --> 02:37:56.700
and transplanted into the body of a modified
BigDog.

02:37:56.700 --> 02:37:58.559
Still think it’d be fun to time travel?

02:37:58.560 --> 02:38:04.380
Hey, don’t look so nervous - For everyone
who agrees to be part of an SCP-2003 mission

02:38:04.380 --> 02:38:07.500
and survives, you’ll get one hell of a pension.

02:38:07.500 --> 02:38:11.340
Or, at least, your family will, if that’s
any consolation.

02:38:11.340 --> 02:38:15.600
Now that you understand all this, let’s
come clean about this mysterious “Project

02:38:15.600 --> 02:38:18.480
XN-SHEPHERD” we’ve been alluding to throughout
the video.

02:38:18.479 --> 02:38:24.120
It all started with a letter to the heads
of the SCP-2003 research project from O5-7,

02:38:24.120 --> 02:38:29.280
a member of the legendary O5 Council that
instructs the Foundation in all that it does.

02:38:29.280 --> 02:38:30.359
The letter read:

02:38:30.359 --> 02:38:36.540
“Up until this point, all attempts at future
intervention using SCP-2003 have been limited

02:38:36.540 --> 02:38:38.519
in scope and scattershot in nature.

02:38:38.520 --> 02:38:44.281
I have seen the wisdom in this approach; it
is informed by painstaking contingency planning

02:38:44.280 --> 02:38:45.899
and risk/benefit evaluation.

02:38:45.899 --> 02:38:51.479
The past 18 months of reports, however, have
promise if we are bold enough to seize the

02:38:51.479 --> 02:38:51.899
initiative.

02:38:51.899 --> 02:38:54.359
We may have found a way out, here.

02:38:54.359 --> 02:38:55.559
The price, though.

02:38:55.560 --> 02:38:57.360
There's always a price.

02:38:57.359 --> 02:38:58.319
As you well know.

02:38:58.319 --> 02:39:01.319
Consider this note an official change in policy.

02:39:01.319 --> 02:39:06.660
As of today, all efforts at intervention are
now aimed at bringing about and preserving

02:39:06.660 --> 02:39:07.380
XN.

02:39:07.380 --> 02:39:10.200
Designated Magnifier Individuals associated&nbsp;

02:39:10.200 --> 02:39:13.559
with XN are to be protected&nbsp;
from undue interference

02:39:13.560 --> 02:39:15.960
at the expense of all other priorities.

02:39:15.960 --> 02:39:22.140
In particular, Nuru Diagne must be allowed
to die in the manner most observations have

02:39:22.140 --> 02:39:23.100
predicted for her.

02:39:23.100 --> 02:39:26.760
If anything at all changes in that regard,
make it happen.

02:39:26.760 --> 02:39:31.260
I trust that you're familiar enough with the
rest of the Determinative Sets to understand

02:39:31.260 --> 02:39:32.700
why we're going this way.”

02:39:32.700 --> 02:39:39.720
So, in short, of all the potential timelines,
O5-7 wants the researchers assigned to SCP-2003

02:39:39.720 --> 02:39:45.781
to ensure that timeline XN is the one that
actually comes to be, seeing as it’s preferable

02:39:45.780 --> 02:39:46.800
to the alternatives.

02:39:46.800 --> 02:39:49.500
Hence, Project XN-SHEPHERD.

02:39:49.500 --> 02:39:54.180
You’re probably wondering: What happens
in timeline XN that makes it the most desirable

02:39:54.180 --> 02:39:55.201
outcome possible?

02:39:55.200 --> 02:39:57.479
Well, things continue as normal.

02:39:57.479 --> 02:40:02.639
Everything from anomalous activity to social
unrest to environmental factors stays pretty

02:40:02.640 --> 02:40:08.701
much the same as time goes on, until 2349
when a giant, 22-kilometer asteroid strikes

02:40:08.700 --> 02:40:12.300
the earth and wipes out the majority of humanity
in an instant.

02:40:12.300 --> 02:40:16.020
Following this, the world becomes unfit for
human habitation.

02:40:16.020 --> 02:40:20.701
Hey, don’t look so glum, you’ll all be
dead by then - Well, except Dr. Bright.

02:40:20.700 --> 02:40:22.200
Sorry again, Jack.

02:40:22.200 --> 02:40:26.700
We at least get a nice three centuries before
we’re wiped from the cosmic table.

02:40:26.700 --> 02:40:32.160
Your next question is probably: If the preferred
option has humanity being wiped out by a giant

02:40:32.160 --> 02:40:35.819
asteroid in a little over 300 years, what
are the other ones?

02:40:35.819 --> 02:40:39.840
Aren’t we entitled to a multiple-choice
future if we don’t feel comfortable with

02:40:39.840 --> 02:40:44.160
being completely annihilated by an asteroid
before we’re even halfway to the year 3000?

02:40:44.160 --> 02:40:49.200
Well, we’ll give you a little tasting platter
of potential timelines, and you can take your

02:40:49.200 --> 02:40:49.439
pick.

02:40:49.439 --> 02:40:54.419
There was the narrowly avoided Scenario XB,
where things progressed in a similar fashion

02:40:54.420 --> 02:40:59.700
to Scenario XN, except a massive gamma-ray
burst from the sun in April 2017 wiped out

02:40:59.700 --> 02:41:01.740
all life on earth within 38 seconds.

02:41:01.740 --> 02:41:06.780
Then there’s Scenario XE, where the birth
of an unnamed boy in Turkmenistan combined

02:41:06.780 --> 02:41:12.120
with the election of Sir William Entwistle
as Prime Minister of New Zealand in 2049 leads

02:41:12.120 --> 02:41:16.680
to a world-destroying nuclear exchange between
Israel and Greater Indonesia in 2058.

02:41:16.680 --> 02:41:19.741
Any attempts to stop it just make it happen
sooner.

02:41:19.740 --> 02:41:21.840
Or what about Scenario XH.

02:41:21.840 --> 02:41:26.640
Here, a deadly, mutated form of influenza
causes the deaths of over a billion people

02:41:26.640 --> 02:41:27.360
worldwide.

02:41:27.359 --> 02:41:30.120
Combatting this threat&nbsp;
caused increased cooperation&nbsp;

02:41:30.120 --> 02:41:32.519
between world governments that actually resulted

02:41:32.520 --> 02:41:35.460
in a huge net improvement for global peace
and quality of life.

02:41:35.460 --> 02:41:39.840
It seems unrealistic, we know, but SCP-2003
doesn’t lie.

02:41:39.840 --> 02:41:45.420
However, despite things going well, all known
life on earth just vanishes on July 29th,

02:41:45.420 --> 02:41:46.500
2059.

02:41:46.500 --> 02:41:51.300
It’s a hell of an unpleasant twist after
things started going so well for once.

02:41:51.300 --> 02:41:56.700
In Scenario XO, the anomalous increases in
frequency and magnitude in 2037.

02:41:56.700 --> 02:42:01.439
This leads to a Broken Masquerade scenario
where the Foundation’s web of secrecy collapses,

02:42:01.439 --> 02:42:04.559
and anomalous chaos reigns across the globe.

02:42:04.560 --> 02:42:08.640
The Foundation’s members are hunted and
killed, and world governments attempting to

02:42:08.640 --> 02:42:14.100
weaponize the anomalous leads to a new arms
race that wipes out all of humanity by 2048.

02:42:14.100 --> 02:42:18.060
Or maybe Scenario XU is more your cup of tea.

02:42:18.060 --> 02:42:23.100
In this one, the sun collapses, leading to
eternal darkness and massive temperature drops.

02:42:23.100 --> 02:42:28.500
Inexplicably, humans still survive but are
in a state of constant, unmoving agony.

02:42:28.500 --> 02:42:34.319
And maybe if you just really love spiders,
you’ll get a kick out of Scenario XX, where

02:42:34.319 --> 02:42:39.059
a mysterious pathogenic protist causes the
majority of humanity to fall in love with

02:42:39.060 --> 02:42:43.980
the Brazilian Wandering Spider - One of the
few spiders that pose an actual threat to

02:42:43.979 --> 02:42:44.459
humans.

02:42:44.460 --> 02:42:49.140
The diverting of all resources meant to keep
humans alive to instead breeding the spiders,

02:42:49.140 --> 02:42:55.680
combined with many, many people being killed
by the resulting spiders, leads to six billion

02:42:55.680 --> 02:42:57.720
deaths in the early 2030s.

02:42:57.720 --> 02:43:02.281
But hey, you’ll get to see some pretty great
spiders, if that’s your thing, I guess.

02:43:02.280 --> 02:43:05.340
Scenario XN is hardly a picnic.

02:43:05.340 --> 02:43:10.380
Nobody likes the idea of facing an armageddon
straight out of Armageddon when that asteroid

02:43:10.380 --> 02:43:12.420
kills all life on earth in 300 years.

02:43:12.420 --> 02:43:17.399
But while it undeniably isn’t perfect, it
may just be the best option we’ve got.

02:43:18.600 --> 02:43:20.220
Isn’t the future amazing?

02:43:20.220 --> 02:43:25.680
Are you afraid of haunted houses? What&nbsp;
about haunted castles, or prisons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:25.680 --> 02:43:32.640
or mental asylums? We’ve all seen or heard tales&nbsp;
of terrible, tortured souls walking down long and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:32.640 --> 02:43:39.480
lonely hallways, looking for people to pass their&nbsp;
ancient pain onto. But what about something a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:39.479 --> 02:43:46.259
more subtle. Perhaps as humble and unassuming&nbsp;
as a cozy little woodshed. An adventurer&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:46.260 --> 02:43:52.020
named Cait would find that, sometimes,&nbsp;
terrible things hide in simple places.&nbsp;

02:43:52.020 --> 02:43:57.541
With every step, twigs broke under the sole&nbsp;
of her boot, their snaps echoing around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:57.540 --> 02:44:02.880
emptiness of the surrounding forest. Birds&nbsp;
cawed down at her from their perches up above,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:02.880 --> 02:44:09.300
a grave omen, a warning not to tread further…&nbsp;
well, at least to anyone who actually bought&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:09.300 --> 02:44:14.820
into all that superstitious stuff. Cait was far&nbsp;
from a believer in that sort of thing, although,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:14.819 --> 02:44:20.759
at the same time, she had more than a passing&nbsp;
interest in all things occult and unnatural.&nbsp;

02:44:20.760 --> 02:44:25.980
For her, it was less about the actual practice&nbsp;
of certain things, the appeal was more about&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:25.979 --> 02:44:32.399
the stories that those practices inspired.&nbsp;
Legends and myths, spooky tales of ghosts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:32.399 --> 02:44:38.219
or the dead rising from their graves and,&nbsp;
of course, the magical mother of them all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:38.220 --> 02:44:44.340
witchcraft. Although her fascination with&nbsp;
the inexplicable and macabre rarely, if ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:44.340 --> 02:44:50.160
overlapped with her other big passion: hiking.
Until, of course, today.&nbsp;

02:44:50.160 --> 02:44:55.019
She could trek anywhere and wanted to aim&nbsp;
for everywhere. Through sprawling national&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:55.020 --> 02:44:59.880
parks filled with vibrant greenery, up the&nbsp;
sides of mountains climbing up to the peaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:59.880 --> 02:45:05.819
to across deserts, following the almost empty&nbsp;
highways to get from one tiny rural town to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:05.819 --> 02:45:09.840
next. There was something about getting&nbsp;
to not just know about the world but to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:09.840 --> 02:45:17.280
actively go and see it with her own two eyes, to&nbsp;
actually be out there in it, that felt so right.&nbsp;

02:45:17.280 --> 02:45:22.259
On her current journey, Cait had taken herself&nbsp;
on a long trail through the heart of the American&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:22.260 --> 02:45:27.840
Midwest. Lugging a heavy pack over her shoulders,&nbsp;
filled with her tent, sleeping bag, outdoor&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:27.840 --> 02:45:33.600
cooking supplies, and all manner of camping gear,&nbsp;
she had set off following the winding path of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:33.600 --> 02:45:39.661
Patoka River, which ran around or adjacent to a&nbsp;
few of the major cities in the state of Indiana.&nbsp;

02:45:39.660 --> 02:45:44.939
Cait was hoping to follow the flow of its main&nbsp;
body of water all the way through to the city&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:44.939 --> 02:45:50.879
of Jasper. From there, it would be a straight&nbsp;
shot over to the similarly named Patoka Lake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:50.880 --> 02:45:54.900
and after she had walked around the entire&nbsp;
circumference of that, it would be a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:54.899 --> 02:46:00.780
hike East towards West Virginia, home of the&nbsp;
Blue Ridge Mountains. Sure, it was one hell of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:00.780 --> 02:46:06.120
an ambitious trip for one person traveling alone,&nbsp;
but Cait liked to keep her journeys unencumbered;&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:06.120 --> 02:46:10.620
having someone else coming with her would just&nbsp;
slow her down, or they wouldn’t be able to keep up&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:10.620 --> 02:46:15.660
with her at all. There’s no fun at all in that.
Stopping for the night, Cait lit herself a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:15.660 --> 02:46:20.040
campfire. She had to make sure to keep it far&nbsp;
enough from the trees to avoid starting any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:20.040 --> 02:46:25.500
potential catastrophes, but also not too close&nbsp;
to the wet bank of the Patoka, otherwise, her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:25.500 --> 02:46:30.479
kindling wouldn’t catch alight. There were so many&nbsp;
variables to consider for any aspiring camper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:30.479 --> 02:46:35.160
Sparks from the flint that she always took on her&nbsp;
travels struck the dry twigs she had collected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:35.160 --> 02:46:40.920
and soon, a gentle orange glow and wave of low&nbsp;
heat were radiating from it. The fire provided&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:40.920 --> 02:46:46.800
Cait with just enough light to unfold and peg down&nbsp;
her tent as the diminishing visibility of the dusk&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:46.800 --> 02:46:51.780
gave way to the encroaching nighttime darkness.
Before getting comfortable in her sleeping bag,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:51.780 --> 02:46:57.059
she put out her campfire using water from the&nbsp;
Patoka, then zipped up the front of her tent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:57.060 --> 02:47:02.520
keeping a flimsy cloth barrier between herself&nbsp;
and the local wildlife. Not everyone found&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:02.520 --> 02:47:07.020
it as easy to sleep in the woods as Cait did.&nbsp;
She couldn’t remember a time when the noise&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:07.020 --> 02:47:12.000
of breaking twigs or the sounds of movement&nbsp;
outside had ever kept her awake. Even now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:12.000 --> 02:47:16.979
the rustle of leaves and branches did little to&nbsp;
disturb her, regardless of whether it was just the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:16.979 --> 02:47:22.439
wind… or something else moving through the bushes.
Woken up by the sun rising, its warm light&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:22.439 --> 02:47:27.839
breaking through the trees, Cait readied herself&nbsp;
to leave. She never stopped at the same place for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:27.840 --> 02:47:32.819
more than one night, and rarely slept for any&nbsp;
longer than she needed to. A nice, eight-hour&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:32.819 --> 02:47:38.219
recharge of her energy reserves, and then it was&nbsp;
back to the open road. After a quick breakfast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:38.220 --> 02:47:43.860
she packed up her single-person campsite, folded&nbsp;
up her tent, and stuffed it back into her bag.&nbsp;

02:47:43.859 --> 02:47:48.299
Cait had been just about to leave when she&nbsp;
noticed something was missing. Her compass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:48.300 --> 02:47:52.920
it had been in her backpack, which she kept in&nbsp;
the tent with her all night. Quickly scanning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:52.920 --> 02:47:57.780
ground around her, she couldn’t see it. Weird, but&nbsp;
she figured she had obviously dropped it at some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:57.780 --> 02:48:02.399
point during her hike and would have to pick up a&nbsp;
new one when she got to Jasper. It didn’t matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:02.399 --> 02:48:06.299
she could just follow the Patoka River&nbsp;
as planned, although it didn’t quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:06.300 --> 02:48:11.640
sit easily with her the rest of the day’s trek.
She’d packed the compass, that she was absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:11.640 --> 02:48:16.320
certain of; after all, she knew it wasn’t&nbsp;
like her to leave it behind. But then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:16.319 --> 02:48:22.559
had she… could she have forgotten it entirely?&nbsp;
Over the next few hours, the question went round&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:22.560 --> 02:48:27.180
and round in Cait’s head. As she walked along&nbsp;
the bank of the river, silently starting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:27.180 --> 02:48:32.701
doubt herself, she drifted a little deeper into&nbsp;
the woods until, out of the corner of her eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:32.700 --> 02:48:39.720
she spotted something standing among the trees.
It wasn’t an animal or even a figure, but a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:39.720 --> 02:48:45.060
structure. Spending so much time out in nature,&nbsp;
anything man-made usually stuck out as an obvious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:45.060 --> 02:48:50.040
unignorable eyesore to Cait. She looked at it&nbsp;
from a distance; it looked like an old house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:50.040 --> 02:48:55.979
isolated out in the woods, a short walk from the&nbsp;
Patoka River. Checking the sky over her shoulder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:55.979 --> 02:49:00.419
Cait noticed it was getting late again, the&nbsp;
daylight having gradually lowered while she’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:00.420 --> 02:49:06.720
been wondering about why she had left her compass&nbsp;
behind… or if it had been taken. Deciding to set&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:06.720 --> 02:49:11.281
up camp closer to the little house, she&nbsp;
turned and headed in to inspect it closer.&nbsp;

02:49:11.280 --> 02:49:16.080
The place was far from the lap of modern&nbsp;
luxury. Not that Cait couldn’t live without&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:16.080 --> 02:49:21.120
running water or electricity for long stints&nbsp;
of time. But it wasn’t a house that had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:21.120 --> 02:49:26.580
built recently. Although she was no expert&nbsp;
in either archaeology or architecture, Cait&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:26.580 --> 02:49:32.700
didn’t think anyone had lived there for decades,&nbsp;
possibly even centuries. It was almost medieval,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:32.700 --> 02:49:38.280
a single room that was completely ramshackle,&nbsp;
practically falling apart at the seams. Everywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:38.280 --> 02:49:43.319
she looked, the wood that had originally been&nbsp;
used to build it was either rotting away or&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:43.319 --> 02:49:47.939
had been broken into splintered remains. Plants&nbsp;
from the forest had started growing through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:47.939 --> 02:49:52.559
floors and the walls as if nature was trying&nbsp;
to reclaim this spot of land where someone had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:52.560 --> 02:49:57.900
once come to get away from the rest of the world.
Sighing, Cait shook her head as she looked at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:57.899 --> 02:50:03.540
dilapidated house; there was no way even she could&nbsp;
sleep there. It was too much of a safety risk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:03.540 --> 02:50:07.620
parts of the ceiling could easily fall on her&nbsp;
during the night if the wind picked up enough.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:07.620 --> 02:50:13.380
Turning to leave, she stopped in her tracks as&nbsp;
she noticed another structure, much smaller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:13.380 --> 02:50:18.780
behind the house. It had been so dwarfed in&nbsp;
size by the slightly bigger building that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:18.780 --> 02:50:23.340
was completely obscured from view. But it&nbsp;
looked to be in much better shape in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:23.340 --> 02:50:29.520
of its structural integrity. It was a woodshed,&nbsp;
its front door hanging lazily open. While not&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:29.520 --> 02:50:34.500
exactly brand new by anyone’s standards, it was&nbsp;
at least far more intact than the main house.&nbsp;

02:50:34.500 --> 02:50:40.620
Taking a few steps forward, Cait felt something&nbsp;
glass crunch under the heel of her boot. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:40.620 --> 02:50:45.599
scanned the floor, instinctively checking for&nbsp;
any more so as not to injure herself. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:45.600 --> 02:50:50.340
with the low amount of sunlight fading ever&nbsp;
rapidly, it didn’t look like more. Kicking&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:50.340 --> 02:50:54.480
her boot to loosen the shards, she made her&nbsp;
way towards the woodshed, not noticing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:54.479 --> 02:51:00.359
what she’d been standing on had been a compass.
Reaching the shed, she peered inside. It was pitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:00.359 --> 02:51:05.339
black within, almost as dark as the rest of the&nbsp;
forest would be in a few minutes. Taking off her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:05.340 --> 02:51:10.500
backpack and setting it down, she searched inside&nbsp;
for her flashlight. Retrieving it and flipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:10.500 --> 02:51:15.720
the on switch, she looked back into the shed…&nbsp;
and that was when she saw it. Taking a step back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:15.720 --> 02:51:19.800
Cait tripped over her bag, scrabbling back up&nbsp;
to her feet to make sure she had seen what she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:19.800 --> 02:51:25.740
thought she had. It was just lying there, still&nbsp;
and lifeless. For a split second, she had hoped it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:25.740 --> 02:51:31.319
was a trick of the light, just an old, decaying&nbsp;
lump of wood. But it wasn’t… it was a body.&nbsp;

02:51:31.319 --> 02:51:37.559
The remains were charred, reduced to little more&nbsp;
than bones some time ago. Even the ground next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:37.560 --> 02:51:42.781
it looked like it had been scorched, blackened&nbsp;
by some intense fire damage. Cait’s eyes were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:42.780 --> 02:51:48.719
so transfixed on the burned mass of bones that a&nbsp;
sudden sound startled her. Thunder growled above,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:48.720 --> 02:51:53.820
immediately telling her she had little choice&nbsp;
in what to do next. Her options were she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:53.819 --> 02:51:58.200
could either sleep outdoors and get drenched by&nbsp;
the rain, and possibly catch hypothermia from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:58.200 --> 02:52:04.319
being cold and wet. Or she could spend a night in&nbsp;
the cramped confines of this woodshed, which she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:04.319 --> 02:52:10.259
would have to share with a long dead body. Walking&nbsp;
back outside to retrieve her bag, she pulled out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:10.260 --> 02:52:15.900
a groundsheet and used it to cover up the bones.
It was a mostly sleepless night, and those were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:15.899 --> 02:52:21.359
a rarity for Cait. Any sleep she did get was&nbsp;
light, easily interrupted by as little as her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:21.359 --> 02:52:26.519
own movements, and offered her no actual rest.&nbsp;
But for the next few hours, she just lay awake&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:26.520 --> 02:52:31.980
on the wooden floor. It wasn’t the sounds of rain&nbsp;
drumming against the shed’s ceiling or the booming&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:31.979 --> 02:52:36.419
of thunderclaps that were keeping her awake.
Thoughts of what she was going to do about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:36.420 --> 02:52:41.100
bones kept coming to the forefront of Cait’s mind,&nbsp;
should she report it to the police when she got to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:41.100 --> 02:52:46.440
Jasper? Was there even any point if she had no&nbsp;
idea where on the map this abandoned place was?&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:46.439 --> 02:52:52.439
Frustrated, she tossed and turned, eventually&nbsp;
sitting up as something made a sound. It was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:52.439 --> 02:52:58.559
low creaking, rusty metal hinge screeching for&nbsp;
a lack of any oiling over the years. The door&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:58.560 --> 02:53:03.900
was open, swinging lazily in the decreasing&nbsp;
winds, its lock having long since broken.&nbsp;

02:53:03.899 --> 02:53:08.580
Grumbling to herself, Cait reached for an old&nbsp;
shovel that had been left in the shed and went&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:08.580 --> 02:53:12.960
to grab the open door. As her head poked out&nbsp;
from the shed, she looked around. It was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:12.960 --> 02:53:18.600
middle of the night, nothing to be seen anywhere&nbsp;
around. Yet she couldn’t escape the feeling she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:18.600 --> 02:53:23.640
was being watched. Taking the shovel, she jammed&nbsp;
it underneath the doorframe, keeping it closed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:23.640 --> 02:53:29.220
At last, there was quiet. Maybe now she’d be&nbsp;
able to get some much needed sleep, and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:29.220 --> 02:53:35.100
did… but that’s when the nightmare started.
The dream was bizarre, unlike any Cait had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:35.100 --> 02:53:40.800
ever experienced before. She instantly recognized&nbsp;
the warm, flickering orange glow of a large fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:40.800 --> 02:53:45.960
before her. Naturally, she started to pace her&nbsp;
way towards it, the fire’s heat washing over her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:45.960 --> 02:53:50.819
the closer she got. But as she approached,&nbsp;
Cait noticed something… moving amongst the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:50.819 --> 02:53:56.580
flames. Arms flailed, trying desperately&nbsp;
to extinguish the blaze, legs kicking and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:56.580 --> 02:54:02.220
writhing. And that was on top of the screaming.
Another figure was standing facing the bonfire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:02.220 --> 02:54:07.920
their back to Cait as she walked closer still.&nbsp;
With every step, the sound of insects buzzing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:07.920 --> 02:54:13.260
could be heard, getting louder and louder. But it&nbsp;
wasn’t until she stepped near enough that she saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:13.260 --> 02:54:18.780
where the noise was coming from. A swarm of bugs&nbsp;
was darting through the air, hovering around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:18.779 --> 02:54:23.279
other figure; there were enough of the insects&nbsp;
that they formed what looked like a cloak, every&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:23.279 --> 02:54:28.859
part of it moving and buzzing of its own accord.
The whole nightmare was so vivid, Cait had no idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:28.859 --> 02:54:33.899
if it had been brought on by her exhaustion, or&nbsp;
that her mind was still fixated on the bones she’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:33.899 --> 02:54:39.960
found in the woodshed, dehydration, lack of food,&nbsp;
or even some other influence. It could have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:39.960 --> 02:54:45.300
any one of those factors that had caused her to&nbsp;
have a dream like this… or a combination of all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:45.300 --> 02:54:50.820
them. Nonetheless, she could feel the bugs tapping&nbsp;
at her skin as she walked up to the other figure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:50.819 --> 02:54:56.580
still unable to see them clearly. The noise of&nbsp;
insect wings whizzed past her ears, louder than&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:56.580 --> 02:55:01.740
ever, loud enough to be real. Putting a hand on&nbsp;
the figure’s shoulder, Cait turned them around.&nbsp;

02:55:01.740 --> 02:55:08.819
It was a woman, or what was left of her. She had&nbsp;
huge, gaping wounds left by something that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:08.819 --> 02:55:10.715
been cruelly buried in her face, with similar&nbsp;
injuries lower down at her neck, and on her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:10.716 --> 02:55:12.300
chest. There were gaps in her skin, as if chunks&nbsp;
of her flesh had been hacked away. Yet somehow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:12.300 --> 02:55:19.560
she was still standing, dead but also alive at the&nbsp;
same time. The swarm of bugs around her moved with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:19.560 --> 02:55:24.840
her body as she turned and faced Cait, a pair of&nbsp;
glassy eyes staring at her. They were both blank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:24.840 --> 02:55:30.240
completely empty, each one missing its pupil.
Opening her mouth, the woman let out a piercing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:30.240 --> 02:55:35.519
blood curdling shriek. All around her,&nbsp;
the sound of the bugs got louder, almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:35.520 --> 02:55:41.041
deafening. And as she screamed… so did Cait.
Panting and shuddering, she sat bolt upright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:41.040 --> 02:55:46.380
shock wracking her whole body, heart&nbsp;
thudding against her ribcage. Instantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:46.380 --> 02:55:51.359
the exact moment she woke up, Cait realized that&nbsp;
feeling was back. She had spent so much of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:51.359 --> 02:55:55.200
time hiking through the woods on her own that&nbsp;
she could tell when someone was watching her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:55.200 --> 02:56:00.960
In the dark, she fumbled for her flashlight,&nbsp;
and clicked it on to reveal… the door was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:00.960 --> 02:56:06.480
jammed shut. Apart from her, there was no one&nbsp;
else inside the shed… no one alive, at least.&nbsp;

02:56:06.479 --> 02:56:11.399
Looking over her shoulder, she could see the bones&nbsp;
behind her and immediately backed away from them;&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:11.399 --> 02:56:16.500
as far as she could in the tiny wooden hut.&nbsp;
She had covered them before going to bed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:16.500 --> 02:56:21.240
she was certain of it. Hadn’t she? All of&nbsp;
a sudden, Cait felt her skin start to itch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:21.240 --> 02:56:25.920
an intense, irritating feeling. She had&nbsp;
experienced the effects of poison ivy and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:25.920 --> 02:56:30.600
sorts of plants that cause similar reactions,&nbsp;
but this was easily a thousand times worse.&nbsp;

02:56:30.600 --> 02:56:35.640
Her skin felt like it was burning; she scraped&nbsp;
her fingernails down her exposed arm, trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:35.640 --> 02:56:40.440
suppress the itching even for a moment but it&nbsp;
did nothing. She scratched at the other arm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:40.439 --> 02:56:47.939
over and over again in one spot until her flesh&nbsp;
was pink and raw. Still no change. Cait raked her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:47.939 --> 02:56:53.700
nails over her own body, this time leaving a deep&nbsp;
scratch trailing over her arm. Under the light of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:53.700 --> 02:56:58.500
her torch, she realized that she’d drawn blood.
She looked back at the bones in the scorched&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:58.500 --> 02:57:02.700
corner of the shed. The skull was facing&nbsp;
straight towards her, hollowed-out eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:02.700 --> 02:57:08.760
sockets staring as empty as the pupilless eyes&nbsp;
of the woman in her nightmare. It had done this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:08.760 --> 02:57:12.780
it must have done, she thought. Reaching&nbsp;
towards the door, dropping her flashlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:12.779 --> 02:57:18.179
she wrenched the shovel out from where she’d used&nbsp;
it to wedge the entrance closed. She stood up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:18.180 --> 02:57:22.980
kicking her sleeping bag and backpack to the&nbsp;
side. As hard as she could, desperate to make the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:22.979 --> 02:57:27.359
itching stop, Cait brought the shovel downwards.
The head of it snapped the already weakened&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:27.359 --> 02:57:32.460
floorboards of the shed, exposing the soft dry&nbsp;
earth beneath. Maybe if she buried those charred&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:32.460 --> 02:57:37.740
remains, whatever was happening to her would stop.
Frantically, she started digging, hurling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:37.740 --> 02:57:43.260
shovelfuls of dirt out through the shed door.&nbsp;
It listed further open, creaking loudly on its&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:43.260 --> 02:57:48.060
rusted hinges again, causing Cait to turn,&nbsp;
startled at the sound of it knocking against&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:48.060 --> 02:57:53.820
the outer wall of the shed. Someone was looking&nbsp;
right at her, she could feel it as real and as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:53.819 --> 02:57:59.040
persistent as the itching feeling that crawled&nbsp;
over her skin like the tiny legs of an army of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:59.040 --> 02:58:03.660
insects. She dug further, eventually throwing&nbsp;
the shovel to one side and dragging her hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:03.660 --> 02:58:08.639
through the exposed earth below, desperately&nbsp;
burrowing through and only stopping to use any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:08.640 --> 02:58:13.020
rocks she found to try and stop the itch.
All she achieved was drawing more blood.&nbsp;

02:58:13.020 --> 02:58:18.241
Her fingers touched something soft, but solid,&nbsp;
and Cait brushed away to clear more of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:18.240 --> 02:58:23.580
excess dirt, trying to uncover what it was. It&nbsp;
felt like a long mass just beneath the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:23.580 --> 02:58:28.979
with a second similar object parallel to it. But&nbsp;
the further along with it she reached, the quicker&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:28.979 --> 02:58:34.379
she realized what it was… a leg. Clearing more&nbsp;
of the dirt higher up, Cait could feel more. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:34.380 --> 02:58:40.500
stomach, ribs, shoulders… and a head. Reaching for&nbsp;
her flashlight, buried under some of the dirt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:40.500 --> 02:58:46.620
had been dug up, she pointed it at the thing she’d&nbsp;
found: the woman, the same one from the nightmare.&nbsp;

02:58:46.620 --> 02:58:52.080
Something inside her chest moved, scratching&nbsp;
sharply, causing Cait to cough. And once she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:52.080 --> 02:58:56.640
started, she couldn’t stop. It was like the&nbsp;
itching she’d felt on the outside had now&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:56.640 --> 02:59:04.020
worked its way inside and it was spreading… no,&nbsp;
moving. In fact, not just moving but crawling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:04.020 --> 02:59:09.960
Through her lungs, burrowing down into her&nbsp;
stomach and, at the same time, upwards. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:09.960 --> 02:59:14.939
clawing of tiny legs, digging their way up her&nbsp;
windpipe, blocking it. Cait couldn’t breathe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:14.939 --> 02:59:19.379
she dropped to her knees retching as she&nbsp;
struggled for air, spluttering as she felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:19.380 --> 02:59:23.160
something move at the back of her throat.&nbsp;
That was when she heard the buzzing again.&nbsp;

02:59:23.160 --> 02:59:26.340
Locusts.
A swarm of them came spilling out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:26.340 --> 02:59:31.140
of Cait’s mouth. She couldn’t scream, let alone&nbsp;
catch her breath. They filled the shed in seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:31.140 --> 02:59:36.540
engulfing her entire body as more and more of the&nbsp;
desert bugs still came pouring from her mouth.&nbsp;

02:59:36.540 --> 02:59:40.800
Outside, the wind kicked up again, with&nbsp;
enough force to blow the door to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:40.800 --> 02:59:45.900
woodshed closed again, trapping Cait inside as&nbsp;
the bugs tore at her. There was a single word on&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:45.899 --> 02:59:51.359
the wooden surface of the door, written in deep,&nbsp;
black charcoal. She’d missed it, the door had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:51.359 --> 02:59:54.839
open when she found the shed.
The word was ‘Witch’.&nbsp;

02:59:54.840 --> 02:59:59.640
The SCP Foundation would later find this&nbsp;
cursed cabin, and would naturally lose a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:59.640 --> 03:00:03.960
number of D-Classes to a horrific form of&nbsp;
locust-based suffocation. While there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:03.960 --> 03:00:08.939
clues as to what exactly is going on in this&nbsp;
terrible place - from the malice of a long dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:08.939 --> 03:00:14.519
sorceress to the lingering revenge of a woman&nbsp;
wrongly persecuted - definitive answers as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:14.520 --> 03:00:21.000
the anomalous mechanisms of the shed known as&nbsp;
SCP-4595 still elude even the Foundation’s finest&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:21.000 --> 03:00:25.800
minds. It’s a place so mysterious and dangerous&nbsp;
that the special containment procedures read:&nbsp;

03:00:25.800 --> 03:00:33.180
“For safety purposes, no personnel are&nbsp;
permitted to enter SCP-4595. SCP-4595&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:33.180 --> 03:00:38.580
should only be entered by authorized testing&nbsp;
personnel under the supervision of the SCP-4595&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:38.580 --> 03:00:45.540
research lead. Under no circumstances is&nbsp;
SCP-4595-A to be disturbed in any way.”&nbsp;

03:00:45.540 --> 03:00:50.160
So perhaps we’ll never truly know why a&nbsp;
humble wooden shed in Jasper, Indiana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:50.160 --> 03:00:56.160
causes such horrifying effects for its victims.&nbsp;
The SCP Foundation thinks it’s safer to just&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:56.160 --> 03:01:00.720
lock it away and forget about it, letting&nbsp;
its ancient wood and old bones rot in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:00.720 --> 03:01:05.820
dark. But if you really are curious about the&nbsp;
truth, you can always take a walk down the side&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:05.819 --> 03:01:11.700
of the Patoka River and pay the Witch a visit.&nbsp;
If you’re lucky, you might even get to leave…

03:01:12.420 --> 03:01:16.080
Step right up, folks! We’ve got all kinds&nbsp;
of refreshing and tasty treats here for&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:16.080 --> 03:01:20.880
you today! Popcorn, peanuts, cotton&nbsp;
candy, and even fried dough! Yessiree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:20.880 --> 03:01:24.120
here at SCP Explained, we’re&nbsp;
offering the top-of-the-line&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:24.120 --> 03:01:28.019
anomalous delectable foodstuffs for all&nbsp;
of your circus-themed funtime occasions.

03:01:28.020 --> 03:01:33.840
And that’s because today - Yes! Today! On&nbsp;
this Youtube Platform! - Our infamous acronym&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:33.840 --> 03:01:39.720
doesn’t stand for Secure Contain Protect:&nbsp;
it stands for Sweet Confectionary Products.

03:01:39.720 --> 03:01:43.800
And let me tell you, dear viewer, the&nbsp;
SCP we’re looking at today just might&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:43.800 --> 03:01:48.180
be the most decadent, durable, and dangerous&nbsp;
dessert that’s ever desired to be devoured.

03:01:48.180 --> 03:01:55.020
We’re talking about SCP-3077, or as&nbsp;
they are better known, The Sugar Golems!

03:01:55.020 --> 03:01:59.220
These little fellas are Safe class and&nbsp;
also totally harmless - so long as you&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:59.220 --> 03:02:02.100
take the proper precautions! What’s the matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:02.100 --> 03:02:06.900
don’t ya believe me? Don’t you think it’s&nbsp;
nice of us to cover a safe SCP now and again?&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:06.899 --> 03:02:11.399
And hey now! Why all this dull talk about&nbsp;
rules and regulations in the first place?

03:02:11.399 --> 03:02:17.160
You don’t go out to the carnival to not take&nbsp;
wild and exciting risks! Every spinny, twirly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:17.160 --> 03:02:20.399
and whirly ride on the fairgrounds&nbsp;
comes with a statistically higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:20.399 --> 03:02:25.679
chance of a tragic mishap befalling you&nbsp;
and any other thrill-seekers around you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:25.680 --> 03:02:31.201
but we all take that chance anyway for&nbsp;
the extraordinary rush of the experience!

03:02:31.200 --> 03:02:37.260
And such is the wacky and wonderful ways of&nbsp;
our adorable and questionably edible chums:&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:37.260 --> 03:02:41.880
The Sugar Golems! Don’t you just love ‘em,&nbsp;
folks? Ain’t they a sight for sore eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:41.880 --> 03:02:47.460
and a pang for sweet teeth? Well, we’ve only&nbsp;
just gotten started! The best is yet to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:47.460 --> 03:02:52.500
ladies and non-ladies! So pull up a chair and&nbsp;
be sure to watch what we’ve got in store! You&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:52.500 --> 03:02:59.279
can make like a piece of old candy and “stick&nbsp;
around!” Now that’s a knee-slapper, ain’t it? Sit&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:59.279 --> 03:03:02.279
back, relax and make sure to enjoy the show!

03:03:02.279 --> 03:03:06.540
You should also subscribe to SCP Explained if&nbsp;
you’d like to continue to be entertained. Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:06.540 --> 03:03:10.560
that rhymed! Whaddaya know? I’m a poet,&nbsp;
and I didn’t even know it! How droll!

03:03:10.560 --> 03:03:15.840
While SCP-3077 refers to the anomalous&nbsp;
substance contained in Site-81,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:15.840 --> 03:03:19.680
the semi-humanoid instances,&nbsp;
which are nicknamed sugar golems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:19.680 --> 03:03:24.360
are themselves an animate and independent&nbsp;
by-product that naturally spawns from&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:24.359 --> 03:03:29.580
SCP-3077 whenever it is allowed to&nbsp;
exist outside of containment procedures.

03:03:29.580 --> 03:03:35.700
The most important of these containment procedures&nbsp;
being that SCP-3077 must remain at a constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:35.700 --> 03:03:41.580
temperature of well below its freezing point and&nbsp;
only be stored in containers full to capacity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:41.580 --> 03:03:45.779
lest its aforementioned by-products&nbsp;
attempt to breach containment. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:45.779 --> 03:03:52.679
total volume of SCP-3077 within the cryogenic&nbsp;
containment unit equals almost 2280 liters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:52.680 --> 03:03:57.720
and it is believed to be the only known quantity&nbsp;
of the anomalous substance in existence.

03:03:57.720 --> 03:04:03.241
For the sake of clarity in distinguishing&nbsp;
between SCP-3077 and its byproducts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:03.240 --> 03:04:07.559
we’ll be referring to the main object&nbsp;
contained by the Foundation as SCP-3077,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:07.560 --> 03:04:12.420
while the gooey little guys who we know to&nbsp;
spontaneously split off from the source of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:12.420 --> 03:04:21.420
SCP-3077 will be regarded as SCP-3077-1. As&nbsp;
mentioned before, SCP-3077-1 instances have&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:21.420 --> 03:04:29.220
been affectionately dubbed The Sugar Golems. Every&nbsp;
instance of SCP-3077-1 resembles an approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:29.220 --> 03:04:36.540
one-meter tall gaunt humanoid composed of a pure&nbsp;
sugar-derived substance commonly known as treacle.

03:04:36.540 --> 03:04:40.800
And that’s molasses for all of y’all -&nbsp;
yeehaw! - cowboys over there in the U S of A!

03:04:40.800 --> 03:04:45.720
If you’ve ever played the classic board game&nbsp;
Candyland, you’ll have some idea of what an&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:45.720 --> 03:04:51.900
individual instance of SCP-3077 looks like from&nbsp;
the beloved and often remembered character of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:51.899 --> 03:04:57.599
Gloppy, who lives in the molasses swamp section&nbsp;
of the board and is also fittingly made out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:57.600 --> 03:05:03.780
molasses himself. Yes, indeed, Gloppy is truly&nbsp;
a delight for a weary CandyLand player to meet.

03:05:03.779 --> 03:05:08.399
What did you say? Are you folks too young to know&nbsp;
about CandyLand? Well, that factoid certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:08.399 --> 03:05:13.439
makes this narrator feel pretty old. Then again,&nbsp;
I am taking on the mannerisms and attire of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:13.439 --> 03:05:18.299
old-fashioned carnival barker, so I suppose a&nbsp;
bit of novel antiquity comes with the territory.

03:05:18.300 --> 03:05:24.060
Regardless, the golems are each composed of&nbsp;
roughly 7 liters of sweet syrupy goodness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:24.060 --> 03:05:29.400
and very much like everyone's favorite character&nbsp;
Gloppy they all lack defined lower bodies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:29.399 --> 03:05:34.979
can all emote through crude yet oddly endearing&nbsp;
vocalizations in the place of intelligible speech.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:34.979 --> 03:05:39.779
While their facial features are simplistic&nbsp;
and misshapen, the contours of concave eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:39.779 --> 03:05:44.700
and a gaping mouth are usually present. The exact&nbsp;
number of these eyes and mouths is subject to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:44.700 --> 03:05:50.639
variation, much like the color of the board spaces&nbsp;
in a wonderful wholesome family game of CandyLand.

03:05:50.640 --> 03:05:57.180
While every SCP-3077-1 instance is around the&nbsp;
same size, the body proportions and overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:05:57.180 --> 03:06:03.840
shape of each instance are rather fluid - pun&nbsp;
fully intended! Some possess oversized arms or&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:03.840 --> 03:06:09.840
bulbous heads, while others might be conjoined to&nbsp;
an adjacent sugar golem as if to show that the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:09.840 --> 03:06:16.290
are as inseparable as a pair of best buddies. Or,&nbsp;
as some others might put it, a couple of B.F.F.F.s&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:16.290 --> 03:06:22.081
- Best Friends for Fancy Frolicking. They&nbsp;
really are quite friendly-looking, aren’t they?

03:06:22.080 --> 03:06:27.180
And aren’t they, they sure are! For the&nbsp;
only thing that these sugary sweet SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:27.180 --> 03:06:31.560
instances want is to be in the company&nbsp;
of human beings just like you. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:31.560 --> 03:06:36.241
you! Who else would I be talking to? It’s a hard&nbsp;
life for this worn-down carnie, let me tell ya!

03:06:36.240 --> 03:06:41.460
These little sugar golems love what they do and do&nbsp;
what they love, but that doesn’t mean that it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:41.460 --> 03:06:47.939
time for fun and games! Even though SCP-3077-1&nbsp;
instances want to hang around human beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:47.939 --> 03:06:51.960
they don’t tend to stop at “hey” and “hello”&nbsp;
or whatever those appropriate greetings sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:51.960 --> 03:06:56.880
like when they are being gurgled by a diminutive&nbsp;
molten sugar monster! Things can get out of hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:06:56.880 --> 03:07:02.400
real fast - just like an orange cream popsicle&nbsp;
melting in the sun of a late summer’s day!

03:07:02.399 --> 03:07:06.660
Now listen up, it’s important that you&nbsp;
pay attention to what I say next! I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:06.660 --> 03:07:11.340
about to book-learn you about what to&nbsp;
do if an instance of SCP-3077-1 enters&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:11.340 --> 03:07:16.980
your personal space! The results of prolonged&nbsp;
contact with this SCP can end badly if you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:16.979 --> 03:07:17.560
not careful, much like a certain dessert that&nbsp;
contains the words “by chocolate” and nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:17.560 --> 03:07:21.779
good proceeding it! I’m not going to sugarcoat&nbsp;
any of the chewy details of your “gristly” fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:21.779 --> 03:07:25.500
and I promise you that it won’t be a&nbsp;
cakewalk, so don’t be a nerd and listen up!

03:07:25.500 --> 03:07:30.600
Yes, that’s right, I called you a nerd. You know,&nbsp;
like nerds? The candy? How do you folks seriously&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:30.600 --> 03:07:34.380
not know nerds? They were a classic Halloween&nbsp;
candy from the Wonka company and they were very&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:34.380 --> 03:07:38.940
popular back in the day! Oh? What’s that you&nbsp;
say? How long ago was back in the day for me?&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:38.939 --> 03:07:44.219
That’s a bit of a rude question, wouldn't&nbsp;
you say? Oooh…! Why I oughta…! Won’t you&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:44.220 --> 03:07:48.000
go ahead and knock it off with the wise guy&nbsp;
questions! What are you, a pack of smarties?

03:07:48.000 --> 03:07:53.040
Ha! I said Smarties! Get it?&nbsp;
It’s just like the—ah, nevermind.

03:07:53.040 --> 03:07:56.939
Let’s just move on to the explanation&nbsp;
of how to survive a close encounter&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:07:56.939 --> 03:08:00.779
with this SCP. That was the main&nbsp;
reason you came all the way to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:00.779 --> 03:08:04.800
here educational and entertaining&nbsp;
video presentation, after all!

03:08:04.800 --> 03:08:11.340
To pick up where I left off, instances&nbsp;
of SCP-3077-1 have a tendency to seek&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:11.340 --> 03:08:18.120
out nearby human life. The reason for doing so is&nbsp;
surprisingly simple and alarmingly well… alarming!&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:18.120 --> 03:08:24.120
These sticky saccharine simulacra are solely&nbsp;
set on slithering into people’s mouths for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:24.120 --> 03:08:29.220
purpose of gaining total control of their bodies!&nbsp;
Yes, you heard that right! Believe it or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:29.220 --> 03:08:34.680
the same anomalous property which animates the&nbsp;
sugar golems’ treacle bodies is apparently capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:34.680 --> 03:08:40.620
of overriding the human nervous system&nbsp;
from inside. And that’s no joke, folks!

03:08:40.620 --> 03:08:44.939
While these tasty treats might sound sweet&nbsp;
to eat, you’ll be a puppet of meat from your&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:44.939 --> 03:08:51.960
head to feet if you don’t complete the tasks I&nbsp;
entreat. If an instance of SCP-3077-1 attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:51.960 --> 03:08:57.060
to enter your mouth, you must remember first&nbsp;
and foremost to keep your trap shut - blocking&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:08:57.060 --> 03:09:02.161
it with a mask or similar article of clothing&nbsp;
if need be! Next, you must use your limbs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:02.160 --> 03:09:06.359
all available implements to batter the&nbsp;
attacking golem away while doing your&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:06.359 --> 03:09:10.979
best to keep a distance of at least arm’s&nbsp;
reach between yourself and the instance.

03:09:10.979 --> 03:09:18.540
It should come as a relief to all rational people&nbsp;
that SCP-3077-1 instances are severely limited in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:18.540 --> 03:09:24.060
their physical capabilities, and an adult human&nbsp;
of average fitness can easily hold one off if&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:24.060 --> 03:09:29.701
they know what to expect. The tricky part comes&nbsp;
from the amorphous properties of the instances’&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:29.700 --> 03:09:35.639
viscous treacle bodies, as well as their anomalous&nbsp;
ability to regenerate from any physical trauma.

03:09:35.640 --> 03:09:41.580
The only way to permanently destroy an&nbsp;
instance of SCP-3077-1 is to expose it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:41.580 --> 03:09:45.660
to temperatures above its melting point&nbsp;
– which for you sticklers out there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:45.660 --> 03:09:52.920
approximately 176 degrees celsius. The&nbsp;
most effective weapons against SCP-3077-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:09:52.920 --> 03:09:58.380
instances include fire bombs, flamethrowers,&nbsp;
and your run-of-the-mill convection ovens.

03:09:58.380 --> 03:10:03.840
If it is at all possible to contain the instance&nbsp;
within a sealed vessel such as a large Tupperware&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:03.840 --> 03:10:09.540
or wooden barrel, then you oughta do whatever you&nbsp;
can to prevent the candy creeps from running amok.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:09.540 --> 03:10:15.840
While ordinary below-zero temperatures are unable&nbsp;
to destroy the anomalous treacle of SCP-3077,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:15.840 --> 03:10:23.940
instances of SCP-3077-1 can effectively be slowed&nbsp;
down or stopped completely if you put them on ice.

03:10:23.939 --> 03:10:26.700
Whether it's the hot foot or the cold shoulder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:26.700 --> 03:10:31.679
some form of extreme temperature should&nbsp;
always be weaponized when defending oneself&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:31.680 --> 03:10:39.300
from an SCP-3077-1 instance. Any attempt to&nbsp;
crush or smash an SCP-3077-1 instance will&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:39.300 --> 03:10:44.220
only result in the bad bonbon breaking apart&nbsp;
and reforming into several more belligerent&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:44.220 --> 03:10:49.080
bite-sized blighters. A human under siege&nbsp;
by the sugar golems might find themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:10:49.080 --> 03:10:53.580
quickly outnumbered if they foolishly attempt&nbsp;
to use a melee weapon against the anomalies.

03:10:53.580 --> 03:10:58.500
Basically, it’s like a more delicious version&nbsp;
of the popular arcade video game Asteroids!

03:10:58.500 --> 03:11:02.880
No? Ehh. I guess that reference&nbsp;
was from even before my time.

03:11:02.880 --> 03:11:09.300
At any rate, instances of SCP-3077-1 are&nbsp;
difficult to destroy without access to heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:09.300 --> 03:11:14.520
or freezing. The tendency of the molasses&nbsp;
menaces to increase in number is made even&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:14.520 --> 03:11:20.581
worse because of the fact that any amount of&nbsp;
SCP-3077 outside of containment can generate a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:20.580 --> 03:11:28.979
nearly infinite number of SCP-3077-1. While even&nbsp;
an army of SCP-3077-1 instances is far weaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:28.979 --> 03:11:34.319
than an equivalent pack of hunting animals, the&nbsp;
ability to continuously multiply and physiology&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:34.319 --> 03:11:38.880
that doesn’t experience the consequences&nbsp;
of fatigue means that given enough time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:38.880 --> 03:11:45.120
the sugar golems can outlast any amount of human&nbsp;
resistance until they roll over their preferred&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:45.120 --> 03:11:52.080
prey like a slow insurmountable syrupy tsunami of&nbsp;
surrender. Seriously scary stuff, some would say.

03:11:52.080 --> 03:11:57.120
But what happens next is the real kicker,&nbsp;
folks! Mind this ballyhoo’s somber spiel!&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:11:57.120 --> 03:12:03.479
If an instance of SCP-3077-1 manages to, against&nbsp;
all odds, clamber its way into a human chatterbox&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:03.479 --> 03:12:09.660
and hijack the poor sap’s nervous system, the&nbsp;
victim is immediately classified as SCP-3077-2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:09.660 --> 03:12:18.240
SCP-3077-2 instances are easily distinguished from&nbsp;
unaffected humans on sight alone. Dark tendrils of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:18.240 --> 03:12:23.880
SCP-3077 can be seen visibly moving beneath&nbsp;
the skin and often emerge from the mouth to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:23.880 --> 03:12:28.620
criss-cross the instance’s face like makeup,&nbsp;
the world’s most disturbing circus clown.

03:12:28.620 --> 03:12:34.260
That’s not all! After the tragic treacly&nbsp;
transformation takes place, the movements&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:34.260 --> 03:12:40.140
exhibited by the instance of SCP-3077-2 will&nbsp;
become crooked and jerky like a marionette&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:40.140 --> 03:12:45.661
puppeteered by a frustrated chimpanzee! During&nbsp;
this time, the instance remains fully conscious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:45.660 --> 03:12:50.880
retaining whatever cognitive faculties it&nbsp;
had possessed previous to its classification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:50.880 --> 03:12:56.640
but it is unable to attempt speech or&nbsp;
exert autonomy over its own actions. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:12:56.640 --> 03:13:02.701
fun fact was discovered by studying the EEG&nbsp;
recordings of several SCP-3077-2 instances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:02.700 --> 03:13:07.139
and is brought to you by the United&nbsp;
Guild of the Existentially Terrified!

03:13:07.140 --> 03:13:13.741
If an instance of SCP-3077-2 happens to wander&nbsp;
its way into the vicinity of any humans that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:13.740 --> 03:13:19.620
haven’t succumbed to the process of consuming&nbsp;
SCP-3077-1, it will proceed to put on a jaunty&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:19.620 --> 03:13:24.540
performance for its newfound audience. This&nbsp;
peculiar display involves clumsy efforts at&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:24.540 --> 03:13:29.880
dance choreography and the throaty singing of&nbsp;
unsettling atonal melodies that would make your&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:29.880 --> 03:13:34.680
annoying cousin’s road trip songs sound like&nbsp;
they’re in tune. These awkward performances&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:34.680 --> 03:13:40.380
continue until the audience departs from the&nbsp;
view of the SCP-3077-2 instance or the instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:40.380 --> 03:13:46.140
expires. This confirms that the point of the&nbsp;
gesture is to entertain, as without an audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:46.140 --> 03:13:52.260
the SCP-3077-2 instance is not compelled&nbsp;
to make any noises of its own accord and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:52.260 --> 03:13:55.560
in general, doesn’t do anything&nbsp;
other than move around aimlessly.

03:13:55.560 --> 03:14:03.241
In the event that any number SCP-3077-1 instances&nbsp;
escapes from containment and cause the creation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:03.240 --> 03:14:09.599
SCP-3077-2, members of the mobile task force are&nbsp;
instructed to never stray from the line of sight&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:09.600 --> 03:14:16.800
of a currently performing SCP-3077-2 instance&nbsp;
and to approach steadily before restraining&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:16.800 --> 03:14:22.800
the instance while causing minimal harm to&nbsp;
the body. SCP-3077-2 instances can be useful&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:22.800 --> 03:14:28.560
for running further tests on the anomalous&nbsp;
properties of SCP-3077, and there are simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:28.560 --> 03:14:33.900
procedures that allow an instance to be kept&nbsp;
alive indefinitely in containment. Any damage&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:33.899 --> 03:14:38.759
sustained during capture can severely hamper the&nbsp;
efficiency of these life-sustaining procedures.

03:14:38.760 --> 03:14:45.480
The worst-case scenario is that an SCP-3077-2&nbsp;
instance expires before being securely contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:45.479 --> 03:14:51.779
as this will cause the SCP-3077-1 instance to&nbsp;
emerge from its host and resume its relentless&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:51.779 --> 03:14:59.880
attacks on all nearby humans. It is far easier to&nbsp;
simply deal with SCP-3077-2 instances accordingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:14:59.880 --> 03:15:06.180
and this is because SCP-3077-2 only ever&nbsp;
attempts to continue the performance and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:06.180 --> 03:15:10.320
possesses neither the intention&nbsp;
nor the capacity for retaliation.

03:15:10.319 --> 03:15:14.880
If it is deemed necessary for the&nbsp;
effectiveness of a recapture effort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:14.880 --> 03:15:20.220
it can be permissible for the Mobile Task&nbsp;
Force to allow instances of SCP-3077-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:20.220 --> 03:15:26.940
outside of containing to find purchase&nbsp;
within SCP-3077-2 to increase the ease&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:26.939 --> 03:15:30.960
of containment and lessen the risk of&nbsp;
Foundation personnel being affected.

03:15:30.960 --> 03:15:35.939
The performances of SCP-3007-2&nbsp;
instances are rarely physically&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:35.939 --> 03:15:40.080
intensive enough to make capture too&nbsp;
difficult, but it can be said that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:40.080 --> 03:15:44.160
the whimsical antics of these affected&nbsp;
humans are anything but predictable!

03:15:44.160 --> 03:15:50.700
During some rare and special performances,&nbsp;
and if the SCP-3077-1 instance in control&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:50.700 --> 03:15:57.240
of the SCP-3077-2 instance is feeling especially&nbsp;
daring - it may try to show off an array&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:15:57.240 --> 03:16:02.340
of woefully inadequate acrobatic skills:&nbsp;
front flips that are more like belly flops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:02.340 --> 03:16:06.660
back flips that could be mistaken for&nbsp;
pratfalls, and the sort of tightrope and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:06.660 --> 03:16:11.040
trapeze acts that are better left to the&nbsp;
imagination. In lieu of prior incidents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:11.040 --> 03:16:17.160
The Foundation strongly advises that if&nbsp;
for any reason an instance of SCP-3077-2&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:17.160 --> 03:16:22.260
must exist in containment, it must always be&nbsp;
prevented from being at an altitude of more&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:22.260 --> 03:16:27.360
than six feet from the surface of the floor.&nbsp;
Especially if any humans it would perceive as&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:27.359 --> 03:16:31.319
an audience are located directly beneath&nbsp;
where its performance would take place.

03:16:31.319 --> 03:16:38.160
Regarding the creation of further instances&nbsp;
of SCP-3077-2, requests from any level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:38.160 --> 03:16:43.559
Foundation personnel at Site-81 or elsewhere&nbsp;
must be granted permission to proceed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:43.560 --> 03:16:49.320
SCP-3077’s head researcher. Because of&nbsp;
the horrific implications of what happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:49.319 --> 03:16:56.399
to the still-aware human mind while the body is&nbsp;
affected by SCP-3077-1, this process is only to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:16:56.399 --> 03:17:02.819
be approved for use on D-class personnel. That’s&nbsp;
right! And even then - in the event that all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:02.819 --> 03:17:07.500
rigamarole of the paperwork goes through,&nbsp;
it is not acceptable to create an instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:07.500 --> 03:17:13.859
SCP-3077-2 merely for the purpose of providing&nbsp;
live entertainment to fellow researchers.

03:17:13.859 --> 03:17:17.939
After all, not a single one of us should&nbsp;
be quick to forget the grotesque and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:17.939 --> 03:17:23.460
highly regrettable spectacle that was Dr.&nbsp;
Deitz’ Deplorable D-Class Dancers. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:23.460 --> 03:17:27.180
researcher involved with that ethical&nbsp;
nightmare was reprimanded severely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:27.180 --> 03:17:32.100
and the colorful novelty costumes and jangling&nbsp;
bells that all former D-Class personnel were&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:32.100 --> 03:17:38.280
made to wear after being reclassified to&nbsp;
SCP-3077-2 have been permanently confiscated.

03:17:38.279 --> 03:17:42.240
Let the cotton candy machine and&nbsp;
peanut dispenser located just outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:42.240 --> 03:17:48.120
the containment unit of SCP-3077 serve&nbsp;
as a stern reminder that there’s a time&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:48.120 --> 03:17:54.000
and place for monkeyshines and tomfoolery, and&nbsp;
sometimes - yes, every now and then - a highly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:54.000 --> 03:17:58.439
secure Foundation facility is neither&nbsp;
the right place nor the right time.

03:17:58.439 --> 03:18:04.620
In case you haven’t picked up on it, there are&nbsp;
very few practical applications of SCP-3077 due&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:04.620 --> 03:18:09.180
to the fact that its status as a food dish is&nbsp;
negated by the consequences of consumption.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:09.180 --> 03:18:15.960
The main reason for tests to be administered on&nbsp;
SCP-3077-2 instances is to discover if there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:15.960 --> 03:18:22.620
a safe method of extracting an SCP-3077-1&nbsp;
instance from the body of its host without&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:22.620 --> 03:18:28.260
causing the expiration of the original&nbsp;
human. Unfortunately, due to a persistent&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:28.260 --> 03:18:33.840
lack of success, these experiments have been&nbsp;
discontinued indefinitely. But that just won’t do!

03:18:33.840 --> 03:18:38.400
How else are we supposed to know if these things&nbsp;
actually taste as good as they look? I won’t rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:38.399 --> 03:18:43.559
until everyone is able to harmlessly ingest&nbsp;
a sugar golem of their very own! I might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:43.560 --> 03:18:49.081
old-fashioned, but to me, the safe object class&nbsp;
isn’t just a designation, it’s an invitation!

03:18:49.620 --> 03:18:53.220
I oughta be completely okay doing&nbsp;
whatever I like around a safe object,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:53.220 --> 03:18:58.680
because it’s safe! That word should actually&nbsp;
mean something - Ding dang darn it! And I&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:58.680 --> 03:19:02.520
don’t mean in the sense that the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation uses it, meaning an anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:02.520 --> 03:19:06.480
that doesn’t present an active threat to&nbsp;
containment efforts! And more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:06.479 --> 03:19:11.819
there aren’t that many anomalies that are also&nbsp;
delicious candy! And I want to eat this one!

03:19:11.819 --> 03:19:15.960
Sorry, sorry, I lost my cool a bit&nbsp;
there… I just have such a sweet tooth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:15.960 --> 03:19:20.279
and my brain is constantly drifting back to&nbsp;
my nostalgic childhood memories of playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:20.279 --> 03:19:24.120
CandyLand with my family. That was before&nbsp;
they all decided that they wanted nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:24.120 --> 03:19:27.899
to do with me because I became so obsessed&nbsp;
with dressing up like a carnival barker that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:27.899 --> 03:19:32.700
I drove away everyone who ever cared about&nbsp;
me. Other than that, my job here at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:32.700 --> 03:19:36.300
Foundation explaining confectionary SCPs&nbsp;
is the only thing I have left in my sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:36.300 --> 03:19:41.880
sad life. Some days I feel less like Gloppy,&nbsp;
and more like a real Lord Licorice. In hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:41.880 --> 03:19:45.960
times such as these, a fellow could really&nbsp;
use some entertainment to cheer himself up.

03:19:45.960 --> 03:19:51.540
Wait a flea-jumping moment! What is that? What’s&nbsp;
the big idea!? How did these escaped instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:51.540 --> 03:19:57.359
of SCP 3077-2 get in here? They’re all supposed&nbsp;
to be safe in containment a few floors down. Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:57.359 --> 03:20:00.839
somebody else from the research team let it in&nbsp;
here because they knew I was in costume standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:00.840 --> 03:20:07.620
in front of a pretend fairground set? That’s in&nbsp;
pretty poor taste, don’t you think? Pun intended!

03:20:07.620 --> 03:20:12.660
I should probably report to the head researcher…&nbsp;
That would be the ethical, reasonable thing to do…

03:20:12.660 --> 03:20:19.200
Then again… look at ‘em all go! Those sure are&nbsp;
some hilarious dances! I’m definitely seeing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:19.200 --> 03:20:25.200
snappy attempt at doing the Charleston - a classic&nbsp;
- and is that one doing the worm or… it is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:25.200 --> 03:20:30.359
flopping on the floor? I think one of these&nbsp;
instances knows about that Fortnite stuff all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:30.359 --> 03:20:35.460
kids are into these days, but I’m not sure if it’s&nbsp;
the human element or the golem that decides what&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:35.460 --> 03:20:41.580
dances it knows. Either way, this was actually&nbsp;
exactly what I needed to feel so much better!

03:20:41.580 --> 03:20:47.100
For once, it feels like I’m actually at a carnival&nbsp;
instead of just pretending to be at one! This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:47.100 --> 03:20:51.661
the greatest performance I’ve ever seen in&nbsp;
all years - which you can be sure that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:51.660 --> 03:20:52.650
have been a lot of! Until next time gents and&nbsp;
jolly strangers! I hope you enjoyed the show!&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:52.650 --> 03:20:52.740
Just remember, the next time you’re hankering&nbsp;
for a snack - watch your back! Ha! Ha! Ha!

03:20:52.740 --> 03:21:00.359
Now go check out “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional&nbsp;
Vending Machine” and “SCP-5962 - One Night&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:00.359 --> 03:21:04.740
at McDonalds” for more anomalies&nbsp;
that’ll really whet your appetite!

